1 NAME Shadrach /White/
2 GIVN Shadrach
2 SURN White
2 _MARNM White
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 STAE Missouri
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1721
2 PLAC USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1833
2 ADDR
3 STAE Missouri
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/86302338/shadrach-white
2 CONT
2 CONT Shadrach served in Revolutionary War. Shadrach's first wife was Gladis with possible maiden name Ramey. Shadrach married Sarah Gibson on April 12, 1799 in Washington County, VA. According to Judge John Onstott, in the year 1833, S
2 CONC hadrach's wife, Sarah, accompanied their daughter, Rebecca (White) Seela and son, Simon C. White, from Ralls County, Missouri, to what is now Sarcoxie, Jasper County, Missouri. Shadrach remained in Ralls County with his daughter, 
2 CONC Nancy Rama (White) Onstott. Shadrach became so distraught that his son-in-law, Abraham Onstott, brought him to where his wife was now living. 
2 CONT
2 CONT One source indicated that Shadrach was buried on Center Creek. John Onstott, stated in a 1901 newspaper interview that Shadrach died at age 112 and was buried in what became the Gibson Cemetery (Old Gibson Cemetery), now obliterat
2 CONC ed. He said the cemetery was located on what afterward became Dr. Carter's farm on Center Creek about a mile east of what was called the High Hill School. The school is shown on the 1895 Plat Book of Jasper County, MO. A flood in 
2 CONC 1875 may have destroyed the cemetery which was probably on land now owned by Precious Moments (2012).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family records and ancestry.com together list the children of Shadrach as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Shadrach and Gladis are 
2 CONT *Elizabeth (White) Onstott 1796 VA d 1826-1828 probably Clay County, IL and 
2 CONT *Nancy R. (White) Onstott 1795 Washington, Rappahannock, VA d 1838 Center Creek, Sarcoxie Township, Jasper County, MO. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Shadrach and Sarah are 
2 CONT *Peter White 07/09/1801 VA d 04/05/1865 Goliad County, TX; 
2 CONT *Gladis (White) Nowell 04/11/1803 KY d 06/08/1846 Hickory County, MO; 
2 CONT *Simon Cocral White 07/19/1806 Culpeper County, VA d 09/23/1873 Iberia Parish, LA; and 
2 CONT *Rebecca (White) Seela 1810 VA d Parker County, TX before 1873. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There may have been a son, Thomas White 1808 VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some researchers think that Shadrach born 1721 had a son, Shadrach born 1754 and Rebecca and Simon were children of Shadrach born 1754. John Onstott may have been referring to Shadrach 1721 and Sarah as grandparents when they were
2 CONC  actually his great grandfather and step great grandmother. If this is correct, then the children attached to this memorial would be Shadrach 1721's grandchildren. Burial of Shadrach 1754 is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT The creator of this memorial welcomes additional information.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Shadrach White Added by pgfrederick on 18 Sep 2007 Shadrach White was a widower from Virginia who fought in the Revolutionary War.  According to references in a Jasper County history book, this elderly gentleman left Pike County, 
2 CONC Missouri and arrived in Jasper County around 1832, along with his daughter, Rebecca, and her husband, Isaac Seela.  Shadrach died in Jasper County at the age of 112 years and was the first white man to be buried in Jasper County. 
2 CONC  Rebecca and Isaac later traveled on to Goliad, TX.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
