2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 15 Sep 2007 email unknown Cindi Schmerber posted:
2 CONT
2 CONT This may be a long shot, but does anyone have a Nancy R. White, d/o Shadrach White and wife Glades/Gledis/Gledes?
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy, b. abt 1795, married Abraham Onstott, and she definitely had a sister named Rebecca, b. 1809, who married Isaac Seela. A history of Jasper Co., MO, speaks of Rebecca and her family coming to Jasper Co. in abt. 1832 from Pik
2 CONC e Co., MO, with her elderly father, Shadrach, who was a longtime resident of VA and fought in the Revolution. He died at age 112 and was the first white man buried in Jasper Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT I am trying to prove that my ancestress Gladis White Nowell, b. 1803 and married in 1823 in Pike Co., MO to Abraham Nowell, was also their sister. The reason I believe that she may have been is that they were all born in VA, and e
2 CONC ach named a daughter Nancy Rama/Ramey/Ramah. Shadrach is definitely the father of Nancy and Rebecca, and if it is the same Shadrach White of Tazewell, VA, as evidence suggests, then his wife's name was Glades/Gledes/Gledis (depend
2 CONC ing on the record you look at). Since Gladys-by-any-spelling was an unusual name at the time, the naming of daughters the same, as well as sons named Shadrach by two of these women in the naming pattern which signified that their 
2 CONC father's name was Shadrach White, I do believe that it's true they are sisters. Unfortunately, all I have is circumstancial evidence at this point (what I have stated above and more). And IF it's true, then the name Rama/Ramah/Ram
2 CONC ey repeating for the women suggest that Glades/Gledis/Gledes would have Ramey as her maiden name, or at least a tie to the family. The area of VA where they lived in the late 1700's and early 1800's was what is today Tazewell Co. 
2 CONC There are some Ramey's there along with Shadrach and his brothers Abednigo and Meshack.
2 CONT
2 CONT Does this sound familiar to anyone?
