2 CONT quoting the above ref.:
2 CONT Anneken Margaretha OpDenGraeff was born in 1683 in Crefeld, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Germany, the daughter of Abraham & Catharina Trintje 'Jansen' OpDenGraeff. (Crefeld was under the jurisdiction of the Dutch Republic at this time.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anneken & her parents and siblings boarded the ship "Concord", carrying 13 families (inc. 3 OpDen Graff bros. & fams.) from Krefeld, North-Rhine Westphalia, set sail on 6 Jul 1683 from Rotterdam to London, departing London on 24 J
2 CONC ul 1683 & landed in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, Colonial America on 6 Oct 1683.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anneken married Herman 'Harmond' InDenHoffen (DeHaven) on 6 Feb 1711 in the Presbyterian Church, Whitmarsh, Montgomery, Pennsylvania, Colonial America. According to the Dutch Reformed Church of Bensalem, Bucks County, Pennsylvania
2 CONC , the Rev. Van Vlerq performed the ceremony. Harmond & Anneken had 10 children:
