1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Initially: Inherited land from his mother's side of the family in Providence Township near the Perkiomen. See Barbara Wentz' map in documents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from Lloyd D. Ellis:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dubart&id=I713
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I713 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Abraham DEHAVEN 
2 CONT
2 CONT RFN: 713 
2 CONT
2 CONT Change Date: 13 NOV 2005 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1715 in Philadelphia County,, PA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Change Date: 7 JUL 1998 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: 13 SEP 1770 Loudoun County,, VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sherry Johnson sherrjoh7@yahoo.com 16 Aug
2 CONT
2 CONT 2003 Loudoun County, Virginia Will Books, Will Book A
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Abraham Dehaven, Loudoun Co., VA, dated 13 Sept. 1770 Proved: on oaths of George McKenney, Elias Ellis, and William DeHaven.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Robetta - my new house and 1 acre of land it stands on, situated at the great road leading from Noland's ferry to Leesburg with 20 acres joining house on the south side of road during her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons: Jesse - 20 acres at wife's decease
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob - residue of land on south side
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham & Isaac - land on north side of road
2 CONT
2 CONT Daus: Robetta & Sarah - each to have a horse or mare of 12L value, feather bed 6 pewter plates, two dishes, bason, spinning whel, saddle of 4:10 Pennsylvania currency value; sows, cow, etc...to be paid out of the estate on north s
2 CONC ide of road by Abraham and Isaac. Robetta's to be paid within two years. The daughters to have maintenance with Abraham and Isaac until they marry or remove; to work for use of family as long as they remain with their brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dau. Elizabeth - horse, saddle of equal value with her sisters, pewter,...paid when she is 18 years old, to be  paid by Jacob.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jesse [son] and Elizabeth to each get a years schooling out of estate
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter Hannah - one shilling, she being fully provided for.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter Ann - one shilling, she being already provided for.
2 CONT
2 CONT Executors: wife Robetta, sons Abraham and Isaac
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: George McKinney, Elias Ellis, William DeHaven
2 CONT
2 CONT Securities: Isaac DeHaven, Henry Oxley, jr., Shadrach Samuels, and Elias Ellis
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventory of Abraham DeHaven returned Sept. 10, 1771 by Josias Clapham, Phil Noland, Thomas George, John Steere. (p. 920) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Book A: Loudoun County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Abstract from: D.A.R. Magazine, v. 82, p. 848; photocopy of original document in Dehaven file.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1771 in Loudoun Co.,, VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note the intermarriages: (Ref. Van Bibber) Dehaven (In den Hoffen), Op den Graeff and Van Bebber (sp). all founders of Germantown, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrived 1683 on ship Concord. All most likely from the area of Krefeld Mulheim (see Jane Dubart). Sometimes Quakers but mostly Anabaptist Mennionites who fled from the area around Tournai (now Belgium).
2 CONT
2 CONT Refer to "The Dehaven Club" for ancestors and siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://members.aol.com/dehavenks
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see on the internet <DEHAVEN-L@rootsweb.com>
2 CONT
2 CONT Several of Abrahams sons migrated to Scott County, KY in the early 1800`s. Possibly Scotts in Allen County, nearby the Robert Ellis family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Harmon DEHAVEN 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Annica Op den GRAEF
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Rebecca PAWLING
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 1736 in Now Montgomery Co.,, PA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Was Philadelphia County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sarah DEHAVEN b: 1753 in Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Rebecca DEHAVEN b: ABT 1751 in ,, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Isaac DEHAVEN b: 16 FEB 1749/1750 in Philadelphia County,, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
