1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  The New York Genealogical & Biographicail Record, Vol 48, 1917 Page 385,386,387. One line of Seely Lineage, contributed by William Plub Bacon. Christopher (5) Seely of Acquackanonck, N J m, Mary _____ He preached 
2 CONC the first sermon in the Presbyterian Church at Parsippanny, NJ. In 1761 he explored the country afterward composing Wayne Co, PA. and located tracts on Middle Creek, Dyberry and West Branch, and also in Pike Co. Sons; Sylvanus (6)
2 CONC  Joseph, Joshua, Samuel C, David, Jonathen, ( the last two being twins), and Christopher. Also three daughters. Note found from papers from The Genealogical Society of New Jersey. 4/10/1995 ' Born 1716, died March 24. 1792, Newark
2 CONC  Journal Acquackanock, NJ Occupation*: Carpenter Birth*: 1716, Orange Co, NY Marriage*: 1742, Principal=Mary Ball Death*: 1801, Elizabeth, NJ
2 CONT
