1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 【4E—Joplin Globe, Sunday, May 4, 1986】
2 CONT
2 CONT HAROLD SWINEHART
2 CONT
2 CONT Harold F. Swinehart, 73, Iron Gates community at Joplin route 5, died at 2:45 a.m. Saturday at his home after an illness of five months. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Swinehart was born Feb. 27, 1913, in Jasper County and was a lifelong area resident. He was employed as a mechanic at International Harvester Company and Joplin White Trucking, retiring from there in 1976. He was a member of t
2 CONC he La Russell Baptist Church. He married Grace Jones on Jan. 30, 1937, at Webb City. She survives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other survivors include two daughters, Sue Beckham, 2427 Murphy Blvd., and Betty Cole, 4521 Country Lane; a sister, Verna Grundy, Carthage; five grandchildren; and four great-grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Graveside services will be held at 10:30 a.m. Monday at Ozark Memorial Park Cemetery. Cecil Woods, minister, will officiate. Arrangements are under the direction of Mason-Woodard Mortuary.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/m
2 CONC emorial/11911898/harold_franklin_swinehart Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 26 2024, 10:56:10 UTC''
