1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Verna May Swinehart Grundy, 92, died peacefully at Excelsior Springs Nursing Home, Sunday, Aug. 23, 2009.
2 CONT • • Verna was born in LaRussell, Mo., Feb. 13, 1915, to Frank Swinehart and Mary Elizabeth Seela Swinehart. Through school she helped her mom, who owned the Carthage Café on the north side of the square. She graduated from Carthag
2 CONC e High School in 1932. Following high school, she and her mom worked at the Drake Hotel.
2 CONT Verna and Leroy Grundy were married on Feb. 14, 1934. They lived most of the rest of their lives in the Carthage area, interrupted only by the second World War when Verna went to California, to be with her mom. Returning to Cartha
2 CONC ge after the war, Verna and Leroy built their love and their lives around the First Baptist Church. Verna taught Sunday School, Vacation Bible School and was active in the Women's Missionary Union and was a member of several Sunda
2 CONC y school classes through the years. At age 53, Verna returned to the workplace, first for the Carthage Credit Bureau and then, until age 72, at Jasper County Title.
2 CONT Verna was preceded in death by her husband, Leroy Herbert Grundy; and two infant daughters.
2 CONT She is survived by their son, Don and his wife, Ann; grandson, Matt, his wife, Jen and great-granddaughters, Kate and Jane, all of Liberty, Mo.; and granddaughter, Leigh Simrall Burgener, her husband, Ryan and great-granddaughter,
2 CONC  Megan, of Kansas City, Mo.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/113598766/verna_may_grundy Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 26 2024, 10:56:10 UTC''
