2 CONT [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/DeHaven-126 Anneke (DeHaven) op den Graef (1690 - 1745)]
2 CONT Born 1 Jan 1690 in Mülheim on the Ruhr, Westphalia, Germany
2 CONT  Died 10 Sep 1745 at age 55 in Perkiomen, Montgomery, Pennsylvania
2 CONT  Anneke op den Graef formerly DeHaven aka Dehaven, DeHaven 
2 CONT Daughter of Evert (In Den Hauven) Inden Hoffen and Lisebiet (Schipbower) Dehaven
2 CONT Sister of Anna Gerdruth Dehaven, Gerhard (Dehaven) De Haven, Herman In den Hoffen (Dehaven) De Haven, Wilhelm DeHaven, Peter De Haven and Wilhelm In Den Hauven
2 CONT Wife of Jacob op den Graef — married 29 Apr 1712 in Bensalem Dutch Reformed Church, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania  at age 22
2 CONT Mother of Margaret (op den Graef) Dehaven and Annaken Op Den Graeff
2 CONT Biography 
2 CONT Anneke (DeHaven) op den Graef (b. 1 Jan 1690, d. 10 Sep 1745)
2 CONT Anneke (DeHaven) op den Graef
2 CONT  (daughter of Evert (in den Hoven) DeHaven and Lisebiet Schippenbauer) was born January 1, 1690 at Menden in Mülheim on the Ruhr, Westphalia, Germany; died September 10, 1745 in Perkiomen, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania. She marr
2 CONC ied Jacob op den Graef (son of Abraham op den Graef and Catharina Jensen) April 29, 1712 in Bensalem Dutch Reformed Church, Bucks, Pennsylvania; born 1687 in Germantown, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania; died 1750, Skippack Twp.,
2 CONC  Montgomery County, Pennsylvania.
