1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Abraham Isaacs op den Graeff==
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the thirteen original families who settled Germantown. Lived across Germantown Pike from Thomas Kunders. There is a marker on the original site of the Kunders house. (near 5125 Germantown Avenue.. see map in ''MEDIA''.)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abraham Isaacs Op Den Graef''', born Abt. 1658 in Krefeld, Germany; died March 25, 1731 in Perkiomen, Montgomery, Pennsylvania. He was the son of . Isaac Op Den Graef and 5549. Greietjen Pieters. He married. Trintgen Jansen Jul
2 CONC y 23, 1679 in Reformed Church of Krefeld,
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth also found as 1651, and death as Mar. 25, 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT Linen weaver. Immigrated with mother and siblings on the 'Concord' Jul. 24, 1683, William Jeffries, Master, arriving in Philadelphia on Oct. 6, 1683. 
2 CONT Concord
2 CONT
2 CONT Rotterdam, Germany (6 July) via London, England (24 July) to Philadelphia, Pennsylvania
2 CONT 6 October 1683
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain William Jeffries
2 CONT A 500 ton ship measuring 130 x 32 feet.
2 CONT Global Anabaptist Mennonite Encyclopedia Online
2 CONT
2 CONT    PASSENGERS                             VARIANT SPELLINGS
2 CONT
2 CONT    1   Abraham Opden Graeff               Abraham op den Graeff  > see Barbara Wentz' map for land held by the Perkiomen
2 CONT    2   Herman Opden Graeff                Herman op den Graeff
2 CONT    3   Dirck Opden Graeff                 Dirck/Derick op den Graeff
2 CONT    4   Lenart Arets                       Leonard Arets > see Barbara Wentz' map for land held by the Perkiomen
2 CONT    5   Jan. Seimens                       Johan Simons
2 CONT    6   William Streyper                   Johan Strepers
2 CONT    7   Jan. Lensen                        Johann Lenssen
2 CONT    8   Thomas Kunders                     Thonas or Thones Kunders
2 CONT    9   Reynier Tyson                      Reiner Theisen-Doors
2 CONT   10   Jan Lucken                         Johann Lucken
2 CONT   11   Johannes Bleikers                  Johannes Bleickers
2 CONT   12   Peter Kewrlis                      Peter Kürlis
2 CONT   13   Abraham Tunes                      Abraham Tunes
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional passenger
2 CONT   14   Gerhard Brumbach
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcriber's Notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * The use of an * indicates an omission or error made by the original recorder, or is used
2 CONT   by this transcriber to call your attention to additional information in these Notes.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ? The use of a ? indicates a word or letters that could not be read due to the quality of
2 CONT   the original document or handwriting of the recorder.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Other sources of information about these emigrants may be found at:
2 CONT
2 CONT Global Anabaptist and Mennonite Encyclopedia Online
2 CONT
2 CONT The Concord, a Tale of Two Stamps  
2 CONT
2 CONT Herman op den Greaff, Wikipedia article
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad Kunders Family History
2 CONT
2 CONT Pennsylvania German Roots Across the Ocean, Marion F. Egge, Genealogical Society of Pennsylvania, 
2 CONT 1305 Locust Street, Philadelphia, PA 19107-5405; 2000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information was copied from a family Bible. It lists the heads of thirteen German families that sailed 
2 CONT from London on the ship Concord, arriving in Philadelphia on 6 October 1683. The agent for the passage 
2 CONT was Francis Daniel Pastorius, to whom William Penn had granted land that became the Germantown Township 
2 CONT of Bucks County, Pennsylvania (now known as the Germantown section of Philadelphia). 
2 CONT Generously provided by Tom Eisenhardt 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Naturalized at Philadelphia in 1692. He was the subject of the poem "The Pennsylvania Pilgrim," by John Greenleaf Whittier, with stanzas 67 and 68 from the 1872 edition reading:
2 CONT
2 CONT Or, talking of old home scenes, Op Den Graaf
2 CONT
2 CONT Teased the low back-log with his shodden staff,
2 CONT
2 CONT Till the red embers broke into a laugh
2 CONT
2 CONT And dance of flame, as if they fain would cheer
2 CONT
2 CONT The rugged face, half tender, half austere,
2 CONT
2 CONT Touched with the pathos of a homesick tear!
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Chester County Ships Listing for The Concord
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of Arrival: 10/1683 Master: William Jefferies
2 CONT
