4 CONC e of Zweibrücken and by occupation a weaver.  Shortly after his arrival in this country he settled in Whitpain township, Montgomery (then Philadelphia) county, Pa., and according to tradition carried on the business of weaving in 
4 CONC a log house which he built a short distance north of the present village of Center Square.  He was married July 11, 1734 to Elizabeth Schumbach (Shambaugh).  Six years later he purchased what is known as the “Homestead Farm,” remo
4 CONC ved thereto, developing and improving the same, whilst engaging in many affairs of local importance.  He was naturalized April 11, 1761.
