2 CONT  9. Jonas4 Seely (Obadiah3, William2, William1) was born July 22, 1652 in Stamford, Fairfield County, Connecticut, and died March 27, 1703 in Stamford, Fairfield County, Connecticut. He married (1) Mary Slawson 1683 in Stamford, F
2 CONC airfield County, Connecticut. She was born Abt. 1660 in Stamford, Fairfield Co., Connecticut, and died Abt. 1689 in Bedford, Westchester Co, New York. He married (2) Mary Wicks Waterbury 1689 in Stamford, Fairfield County, Connect
2 CONC icut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Jonas Seely:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas was one of the original 22 proprietors of Bedford, NY. 1680/1, where he received a home lot. He sold his Bedford property between 1680-85 to Cornelius Seeley, Sr. and Jonathan Miller, and returned to Stamford, CT. Jonas will
2 CONC  dated Mar.20,1702/3, was not allowed. Inventory of his estate was taken Mar. 5,1704/5; his widow Mary and 8 children were mentioned. Apr. 22, 1719, Jonathan Holmes of Horse Neck was appointed administrator Feb. 13,1721/2, it was 
2 CONC represented that Jonas, Jr, Martha and Susanna had
2 CONT
2 CONT died after distribution was granted 1705; surviving children: Ebenezer, Nathaniel, Eliphalet, Samuel the eldest son, Sarah. Some records also give him a daughter. Elizabeth, supposed twin to Eliphalet. She m, Nathaniel Sanford in 
2 CONC 1728. She is not mentioned in any documents concerning the children of Jonas. She was actually the daughter, of John (3) She is.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Taken from SGS files) VOL 1,page, 11
2 CONT
2 CONT Data from, Roselyn Whitman who states that her data came from
