1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Isaac Herman Opdengraeff=
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Grietjen Pieters''' on July 31, 1633 in Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands. She was born ca. 1620 in Krefeld. She died Nov 19, 1683 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania around the age of 63, enroute to the Germantown set
2 CONC tlement.  Isaac Hermans op den Graeff, b. in 1616, married Grietjen Peters (d. 1679), was converted with his family to Quakerism. His widow, who died in Philadelphia 19 October 1683, his three sons Derick (Dirk) Isaacs, Herman Isa
2 CONC acs, and Abraham Isaacs, and a daughter Margrit (m. later to Peter Schumacher, immigrant from Kriegsheim who arrived in 1685) emigrated to Germantown as part of the 13 famous first families on the Concord, arriving at Philadelphia
2 CONC , 6 October 1683, settling in Germantown soon thereafter. 
2 CONT
