2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Krefeld,_Nordrhein-Westfalen]]
2 CONT == Biography<ref name="Hull">William I. Hull, William Penn and the Dutch Quaker Migration to Pennsylvania:   (Baltimore:  Genealogical Publishing Company, 1970), p.210.</ref> ==
2 CONT Isack Hermans Op den Graeff was born in Krefeld in 1616 to [[Op den Graef-10| Herman Op den Graeff]] and [[Pletjes-1|Greitijen Pletjes]]. Hemarried [[Pieters-42|Greitijen Peters]] and was converted along with his family to Quakeri
2 CONC sm. He died in 1679 leaving his widow, three sons, Derick, [[Op den Graeff-12|Herman]], and [[Op den Graeff-7|Abraham]]and one daughter, [[Op den Graeff-16|Margrit.]]
2 CONT The family, including the widow set sail for Philadelphia on the "Concord" and arrived in October 1683. The widow died soon after arrival, but the children went on to help establish Germantown, Pennsylvania. Note: This wiki profil
2 CONC e had the date of birth listed as 28 Feb 1616 and the date of death listed as 17 Jan 1679 when it was adopted by [[Friebel-9|Donna Storz]]. There were no sources for the exact dates provided.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Information on this family was extracted from the "History of the Op den Graef/Updegraff Family" by June Shaull Lutz, available at the Mennonite Library and Archives of Eastern Pennsylvania, and other material on Pennsylvania hist
2 CONC ory. Four of the grown children of Isaac and Greietjen, Herman, Dirck, ≤b>Abraham≤/b>, and Margaret, were in the original Krefelder emigration to America who settled in Germantown, about six miles outside of Philadelphia.  Greietj
2 CONC en went with them also, as Isaac had died earlier, but she did not long survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT By b.k.uptagrafft 4/27/94: conflict in birth and death dates probably occasioned to faiding print or poor handwriting. Birth date: 12/28/1615 or 2/28/1616. Death date:1/16/1679 or 1/17/1669. Isaac hermans op den graeff arrived in 
2 CONC america 10/19/1683 (note: same date as given for the death of his wife, greietjen.
