2 CONC 48; died at Louisville, Ky., April 12, 1872. Ran away from home to enlist in Civil War. Enlisted ln a company of the Second Connecticut Heavy Artillery. Was made clerk of his company. Enlisted under false name of Charles Franklin 
2 CONC Morse. 149. Rov. Aldace (7) Walker Leonard 6 and Chloe (Child) was born in Strafford, Rutland, Vt., July 24, 1878; married in Lebanon. N. Il April 30, 1841. Mary Ann, daughter of Abel and Lydia (Challis) Baker; she was horn in Leb
