2 CONT *'''''(7) Ann d. after 1773, m. in 1729 ''William Adams (July, 1705 - May 26, 1773),'' son of Richard Adams and Gertien Op den Graff,''''' 
2 CONT **grandson of Abraham and Trintje (Janson) Op den Graff. 
2 CONT *** ''William'' paid taxes in 1734 in Providence Twp. on land he had bought from Samuel Lane in 1731 and sold to Jacob Shrack 1737/38. 
2 CONT >When his father's land was sold as per his 1747/48 will he was listed as of Brecknock, Lancaster Co., PA. He died in Adamstown, Lancaster Co., where his tombstone carries the inscription, "having lived in wedlock for 44 years".
2 CONT
