1 NAME Dirck /Pennybacker/
2 GIVN Dirck
2 SURN Pennybacker
2 _MARNM Pennybacker
2 NICK Dirck
2 NICK Pennybacker
2 NICK Pannebecker
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 JAN 1737
2 ADDR
3 CITY Providence Township
3 STAE Province of Pennsylvania
3 CTRY (Present USA)
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 FEB 1802
2 ADDR
3 CITY Pine Forge
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Iron Master, DAR Patriot #A088626
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR Ancestor #: A088626
2 CONT
2 CONT 1783 Age: 18 Military Berks Co., Pennsylvania Captain in militia.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Compiled from "A History of Shenandoah County, Virginia," "The German Element of the Shenandoah Valley of Virginia,"and  current research done by Sherry Johnson and others.  This compilation is intended for personal, non-commerci
2 CONC al use only.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dirck (also spelled Derick or Derrick) Pennybacker was born January 1, 1737 in Pennsylvania to a prosperous and prominent family. He was a son of Col. John Pennebacker and a grandson of Henry (Hendrick) Pannebecker. The spelling o
2 CONC f the surname was altered more than once over the generations.  Dirck, although a Quaker, served as a captain in the Berks County (Pennsylvania) militia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Dirck married Hannah DeHaven on March 3, 1756 in Pennsylvania, when he was 19 years old. They had at least 9 children (and at least 64 grandchildren):
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin D. Pennybacker, 1760-1820, married Sarah Margaret Samuels, 13 children
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Pennybacker, about 1762-1730, married George Mayberry, 8 children
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Pennybacker, 1764-1819, married Elizabeth Ruffner, 9 children
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Pennybacker, 1766-1824, married Isaac Samuels, 11 childrenJohn Pennybacker, 1768-1834, married Phebe Fugett, 12 childrenHannah Pennybacker, 1770-1856, married Mounce (Moses) Bird, Jr., 10 children
2 CONT
2 CONT Dirck/Derrick Pennybacker, Jr, 1780-1817, married Elizabeth Neal, 1 child
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine "Caty" Pennybacker, 1781-1860, marriage and children unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary "Polly" Pennybacker, abt. 1783-?, marriage and children unknownOn February 3, 1770 Dirck Pennybacker purchased a gristmill and farm on 200 acres in Amity Township, Berks County, Pennsylvania from the estate of William Bird of
2 CONC  Birdsboro.  Dirck was very prosperous during the Revolutionary War, when his gristmill supplied flour to the Continental Army.  However, his business declined when the war ended, and in May 1783 he lost his gristmill and land as 
2 CONC a result of a lawsuit over a debt.  His land was seized and sold at a sheriff's sale to pay the debt.  
2 CONT
2 CONT At that time, 1783, Dirck and his family left Pennsylvania and moved briefly to Washington County, Maryland near Sharpsburg, where he leased an iron-working establishment.  However, within a few months a flood destroyed the operat
2 CONC ion and Dirck left Maryland for Virginia.  According to a deposition made in 1814 by his son Benjamin, Dirck and family arrived in the Shenandoah Valley in [late]1783.    
2 CONT
2 CONT In December of 1783, records show Dirck accepted the results of a survey done to establish the boundaries of a land grant in Shenandoah County.  He and his family moved onto this land and Dirck built Redwell Furnace on Hawksbill C
2 CONC reek near Luray.  Soon he and his family established another forge and  iron works business on Smith's Creek near New Market, which they called Pine Forge.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was in Pine Forge in 1784, as evidenced by a letter he wrote from there to his brother Jacob regarding their father John's death on June 14, 1784 and the settlement of the estate.  The letter, as transcribed in about 1877 by Go
2 CONC v. Samuel W. Pennypacker, who was in possession of the letter at that time, read:
2 CONT
2 CONT "To Jacob Pennybacker, Pine Forge October 16, 1784
2 CONT
2 CONT My advice to you is to Make Sale of the place at any Time when it Suits you but I shall be willing to Make a Sale at any time when Required wich you may Rely on. I will be down in the Spring and expect whe can settle without any f
2 CONC arder cost. Any farder I have Nottien to Rite as whe are all well at present. Hoping thes Lines wil find you all in the Same. I Remember my Kind Love to you all spesly to Mother. If the winter should prove faberel [favorable? ] it
2 CONC  is Likele I shall be down abought the first of January. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Derick Pennybacker
2 CONT
2 CONT I should be willing if there could be some Money made up for Samul for I Expect he must want it as he has had Nottien of the Estate yet." 
2 CONT
2 CONT The iron-working businesses were very successful, and Dirck's descendents started additional iron businesses.  The Pennybackers are considered to be the pioneers of the iron working industry.  A few stoves can still be found today
2 CONC  with the name "D. Pennybacker" on them.  A local census in 1785 reported that Dirck Pennybacker had 64 "white souls" in his household, which seems like a very large number of people, but probably included workers in his iron busi
2 CONC ness, in addition to sons, daughters, and sons-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dirck worked as an iron master until his death.  Older histories report his death as 1799, but his obituary has since been found.  It was published in the March 3, 1802 issue of the Winchester Gazette newspaper and establishes tha
2 CONC t his death occurred on February 15, 1802 at Pine Forge.  The obituary reads:  "On the evening of Monday the 15th Derrick Pennybacker, Esq., of Shenandoah was casually [causually?] killed by a fall from his horse.  The day followi
2 CONC ng his remains were decently interred on his own premises attended by a very numerous concourse of relatives and friends."
2 CONT
2 CONT His will, written 21 Oct 1798 and proved 1 Apr 1802, was located among the unrecorded wills in Shenandoah County Clerks Office.  Dirck/Derrick Pennybacker made bequests to his wife Hannah, to his sons Benjamin, Derrick, John, and 
2 CONC Abraham, to his daughters Hannah Bird, Caty Pennybacker, and Polly Pennybacker, and to son-in-laws George Mayberry (married to daughter Rebecca) and Isaac Samuels (married to daughter Elizabeth). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dirck and Hannah's grandson Isaac Samuels Pennybacker (1805-1847), son of their eldest son Benjamin and his wife Sarah Margaret Samuels, became a well-known lawyer, federal judge, and politician who represented Virginia in the U.S
2 CONC . House from 1837-39 and served as U.S. Senator from Virginia from 1845-47. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From: Sherry <sherrjo@tenet.edu>  Subject: Pennybacker Family Vital Statistics  Date: Tue, 24 Nov 1998 09:11:28 -0600 
2 CONT
2 CONT I don't have the birth dates for all of Dirk & Hannah Pennybacker's
2 CONT  children, but I do have the following dates that were copied from
2 CONT  records at the Winchester Frederick Co. Historic Society in Winchester,
2 CONT  VA. The records were copied by John W. Wayland from the family Bible of
2 CONT  Benjamin Pennybacker, son of Dirk. On p. 17 he notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  "The following entries are copies from an old Pennybacker
2 CONT  Bible--leather-bound, 9 1/2 by 11 inches & 4 inches thick. It was
2 CONT  printed for Mathew Cary, by Joseph Charless, Philadelphia, October 20,
2 CONT  1801. It was first the property of Benj. Pennybacker, Sr. (1760-1820),
2 CONT  then of his son Geo. M. Pennybacker (1787-1880). The old home of these
2 CONT  Pennybackers was Pine Forge, Shenandoah County, on Smith Creek, three
2 CONT  miles below New Market. This old Bible is now (1928) in the hands of
2 CONT  Miss Kate Pennybacker of Linville Creek, Rockingham Co., VA, who loaned
2 CONT  it to me that I might copy the records. Miss Kate Pennybacker is a
2 CONT  daughter of John Dyer Pennybacker and his wife Mary Elizabeth Lincoln.
2 CONT  John Dyer Pennybacker was a son of U. S. Senator Isaac Samuels
2 CONT  Pennybacker (son of Benj. Sr.)"
2 CONT  Family Records of Benj. Pennybacker
2 CONT  Births
2 CONT  Benj. Pennybacker Senr was born 29 Sept. 1760
2 CONT  Sarah Pennybacker wife of B.P. was born 10 Feby 1768
2 CONT  Geo. M. Pennybacker 31st Dcr. 1787
2 CONT  Ann Pennybacker 8 July 1789
2 CONT  Nathan Pennybacker 19 Octo. 1791; m. Mary Samuels 5 Apr.1826 [dau. of
2 CONT  Joseph--SJ] Joel Pennybacker 9 Augt. 1793
2 CONT  Charlotte Pennybacker 27 Sept. 1795
2 CONT  John Pennybacker 15 Apl. 1798
2 CONT  Mary Pennybacker 21 Augt. 1800
2 CONT  Mark Pennybacker 1st Apl. 1801
2 CONT  Rebecca Pennybacker 26 Mar 1803
2 CONT  Isaac S. Pennybacker 3rd Sept. 1805
2 CONT  Sarah Pennybacker 2nd Mar 1808
2 CONT  Benja. Pennybacker 9 Octo. 1809
2 CONT  Saml. A. Pennybacker 11the Octo. 1812
2 CONT
2 CONT  The above are the children of Benj. & Sarah Pennybacker being in all
2 CONT  13---
2 CONT
2 CONT  Deaths
2 CONT  Jno. Pennybacker died 15 Apl. 1798
2 CONT  Mary Pennybacker died 25 Augt. 1800
2 CONT  Benja. Pennybacker Jr. 8 July 1811
2 CONT  [illegible]Benjamin Pennybacker [d. 1820]
2 CONT  Sarah Pennybacker wife of B.P. Senr. died 9th July 1825
2 CONT  Sarah Thompson wife of Wm. G. Thompson died 31st July 1838
2 CONT  Ann Douglass wife of Adam Douglass died October 1843 [no day]
2 CONT  Isaac S. Pennybacker died 12th Jany. 1847 in Washington City. U.S.
2 CONT  Senator
2 CONT  Rebecca Pennybacker died 29th July 1849
2 CONT  Saml. A. Pennybacker died 15th June 1850
2 CONT  Charlotte Newman died 3rd July 1851
2 CONT  Joel Pennybacker died 5th April 1862
2 CONT  Walter Newman died 15 Nov. 1867
2 CONT  Margaret Pennybacker wife of Joel Pennybacker died on July 20th 1861
2 CONT  Geo. M. Pennybacker died 27th Sept. 1880
2 CONT
2 CONT  The above are the death of Benja. & Sarah Pennybacker and their children 
2 CONT
2 CONT  [Note: If any of you happen to visit the Historic Society in Winchester,
2 CONT  I would like to have the exact death date for Benjamin, Sr. This entry
2 CONT  was at the bottom of the page and is not legible. Other notations by
2 CONT  Wayland indicate the 1820 death date and I have copies of newspaper
2 CONT  advertisements for parts of his estate at that time.--SJ]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marriages
2 CONT  Benja. Pennybacker Senr. was married to Sarah Samuels 13 th March 1787
2 CONT  Charlotte Pennybacker was married to Walter Newman 20th Augt. 1818
2 CONT  Joel Pennybacker was married to Margaret Stribling 27 May 1823
2 CONT  Mark Pennybacker was married to Catharine Kratzer 26 June 1823
2 CONT  Nathan Pennybacker was married to Polly Samuels 4 Apl. 1826--The record
2 CONT  in Harrisonburg says April 5, 1826
2 CONT  Sarah Pennybacker was married to Wm. G. Thompson 21st Sept. 1825
2 CONT  Isaac S. Pennybacker was married to Sarah A. Dyer May 1832. S.A.P. died
2 CONT  June 17, 1891
2 CONT  Geo. M. Pennybacker was married to Anna Crim (widow of M.C.) 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Births
2 CONT  Michael Crim was born 15 July 1793
2 CONT  Anna Crim his wife 28 Decr. 1794
2 CONT  David Crim born 29 Augt. 1822
2 CONT  Sophia Crim born 14 Jany. 1825
2 CONT  The above are the ages of Michael Crim & Anna His wife, together with
2 CONT  their children
2 CONT  Deaths
2 CONT  Michale Crim died 16 Jany 1827
2 CONT  David Crim died 10 April 1860
2 CONT  Martha J. Crim died 20th April 1874
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sophia Crim was married to Jno. D. Zirkle 4 July 1843(?)
2 CONT  David Crim was married to Martha Windle 28 Decr. 1843
2 CONT  The above are the marriages of Michael Crim's children
2 CONT
2 CONT  Births
2 CONT  Geo. M. Pennybacker 31 Dec. 1787
2 CONT  Anna Pennybacker 28 Decr. 1794
2 CONT  Benja. Pennybacker son of Geo. M. & Anna Pennybacker was born 24 October
2 CONT  1835
2 CONT  The above are the ages of Geo. M. P. & Ann his wife with an only son
2 CONT  Benjamin
2 CONT
2 CONT  Deaths
2 CONT  Benja. Pennybacker son of Geo. M. & Anna Pennybacker died in Staunton on
2 CONT  Thursday evening the 5th September 1861. was buried in St. Mathews
2 CONT  Graveyard, New Market, Shenandoah Co., Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT  John D. Zirkle died 26 August 1877. 4 p.m.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Geo. M. Pennybacker died 27th Sept. 1880. Aged 92 years 10 months & 26
2 CONT  days [have obituary]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Birth of David Cauldwell & Hannah his wife--The Father & Mother of Anna
2 CONT  Pennybacker
2 CONT  David Cauldwell born 18 Decr. 1763
2 CONT  Hannah Cauldwell born 28 Sept. 1763
2 CONT
2 CONT  Anna Pennybacker wife of G. M. P. died 21 January 1884 aged 89 years &
2 CONT  23 days
2 CONT  Hannah Cauldwell died 7th Feby. 1849 age 85 yrs. 4 m. 10 d.
2 CONT  David Cauldwell died [missing]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Thus far from the old Pennybacker Bible mainly in the excellent
2 CONT  handwriting of Geo. M. Pennybacker. In the Bible is a loose sheet,
2 CONT  apparently written in 1878 by Saml. W. Pennypacker of Pennsylvania,
2 CONT  containing a sort of Pennybacker family tree. From it I note the
2 CONT  following:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Benjamin Pennybacker (1760-1820) was the son of Dirck (1737-1799) and
2 CONT  his wife Hannah Dehaven; Dirk was the son of John Pennebacker
2 CONT  (1713-1784) and his wife Anneke Keyser (1717-1807); John Pennebacker
2 CONT  (1713-1784) was the son of Heinrich Pannebacker (1674-1754) and his wife
2 CONT  Eve Umstat.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Miss Margaret M. Pennybacker ("Miss Doon") was a daughter of Joel
2 CONT  Pennybacker (1793-1862) She lived in Mt. Jackson some time; her last
2 CONT  years on Linville Creek, Va., with her cousin Kate Pennybacker. She is
2 CONT  buried in the Lincoln graveyard on Linville Creek.
2 CONT  Frank S. Pennybacker, a son of Joel Pennybacker (above) lived his last
2 CONT  30 years or so in Mt. Jackson and died there February 1, 1925, aged 84.
2 CONT  Some Pennybackers are still living in Broadway, Rockingham Co., Va.
2 CONT  1928.
2 CONT  Miss Kate Pennybacker, of Linville Creek, has a sister Mary Lee
2 CONT  Pennybacker, who has lived in New York City a number of years.
2 CONT  Miss Kate and her sister are both now upwards of 60.
2 CONT  Mary Lee Pennybacker died about 1931; unmarried
2 CONT
2 CONT  >From book 2 of Wayland's Bible Records
2 CONT
2 CONT  1826, April 5--Nathan Pennybacker and Mary Samuels; by Rev. Joseph
2 CONT  Samuels
2 CONT
2 CONT  John Dyer Pennybacker was born in Harrisonburg, Rockingham Co., Va.
2 CONT  March 20, 1833, son of Isaac Samuels Pennybacker (1805-1847) and his
2 CONT  wife Sarah Dyer (1816-); died March 17, 1905. John Dyeer Pennybacker
2 CONT  married Mary Elizabeth Lincoln (d/o Abraham and Mary Homan Lincoln)
2 CONT  August 28, 1865. Mary Elizabeth Lincoln was b. Nov. 11, 1827.
2 CONT  Children of John d. and Mary E. Pennybacker:
2 CONT  Mary Lee, born August 24, 1866
2 CONT  Kate Abigail, born may 30, 1868
2 CONT  John George, born Nov. 18, 1870
2 CONT
2 CONT  Abraham Lincoln, father of Mary E. Lincoln Pennybacker, was born March
2 CONT  20, 1799; died June 13, 1852. Mary Homan Lincoln was born October 24,
2 CONT  1802; died March 8, 1874.
2 CONT  Abraham Lincoln was son of Jacob, one of the 5 sons of "Virginia John."
2 CONT
2 CONT  The foregoing notes given by Kate Abigail Pennybacker Aug. 18, 1929,
2 CONT  from records in Bibles and elsewhere, Linville Cree, Rockingham Co., Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She states that Sen. Isaac S. Pennybacker (her grandfather) had 6
2 CONT  children, only three growing up.
2 CONT  John Dyer--lived on Linville Creek, Va.
2 CONT  James Edwin--lived in Washington City
2 CONT  Isaac S. Jr.--died in Franklin, W.Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Kate Abigail Pennybacker died in Rockingham Memorial Hospital,
2 CONT  Harrisonburg, Saturday, December 17, 1938.
2 CONT
2 CONT  * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
2 CONT  * * * * * * *
2 CONT
2 CONT  The above records are just as written in Wayland's notes except where
2 CONT  I've made comments in brackets [ ]. The records continue with more
2 CONT  vital stats. on the Lincolns, Maupins, Zirkles, and some later
2 CONT  Pennybackers. I'm out of time for now, but if there is interest I could
2 CONT  post additional information later.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In addition to the information on Benjamin Pennybacker given above, I
2 CONT  have dates for the following children of Dirk Pennybacker:
2 CONT  John Pennybacker b. August 1768 d. 28 Feb. 1834 Wood Co., WV
2 CONT  Rebecca Pennybacker b. ca 1762
2 CONT  Elizabeth Pennybacker b. June 1766 d. Oct. 1824 Greenhope Farm,
2 CONT  Shenandoah Co., Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In his will [copy] Dirk Pennybacker named his wife Hannah and seven
2 CONT  children: Benjamin Pennybacker, [sons-in-law] George Mayberry and Isaac
2 CONT  Samuels, Derrick Pennybacker, John Pennybacker, Abraham Pennybacker,
2 CONT  Hannah Bird and Caty Pennybacker, Polly Pennybacker.
2 CONT  Isaac Samuels married Elizabeth Pennybacker and George Mayberry married
2 CONT  Rebecca Pennybacker, other daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Hope this will help a few of you fill in gaps.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sherry sherrjo@tenet.edu
