2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: EST 1749 in Caernarvon twp 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Could have been born earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT Was Lancaster now S.E. corner of Berks County near
2 CONT
2 CONT Morgantown, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Estate documents she is listed as Eliz. Ann and later as Ann, and called Nancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Am beginning to favor:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Hughes ?) Ellis, widow (1766) of Robert Ellis, Sr., mother of Robert Ellis, Jr.and Elizabeth Ann Ellis (who becomes Isaac Dehavens wife) who marries Wm. Jones (widower) ca 1768. She becomes known to the children and others a
2 CONC s Mary Jones, and Nancy may have been adopted by Wm. Jones.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Robert ELLIS Sr. b: ABT 1713 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Mary HUGHES ? b: 24 MAR 1719/1720 in Gwynedd twp
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Isaac DEHAVEN b: 16 FEB 1749/1750 in Philadelphia County,, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: EST 1774 in Loudoun Co.,, VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT This marriage is based upon circumstantial evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT One William Jones and wife Mary from PA to Loudoun County, VA. in 1759.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1772 William Jones died. His Will names 2nd wife Mary*, sons James and Joshua together with daughter Mary Griffith.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1775 Loudoun tithtable shows Mrs. Mary Jones together with Robert Ellis, Jr. then age 17.
2 CONT
2 CONT * She is believed to have been the widowed (1766) wife of Robert Ellis, Sr. (and the mother of Robert Ellis, Jr. and Elizabeth Ann "Nancy" Ellis). She remarried Wm. Jones in Loudoun sometime after 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT For more evidence on the Jones, Dehaven, Ellis relationship see Wm. and Mary Jones and their sons, property sales etc.
