1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From information taken from Lloyd D. Ellis: http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dubart&id=I446
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I446  Name: Snelling ELLIS  RFN: 446  Change Date: 3 AUG 2005  Sex: M  ALIA: His name was also written Surnellan & /"Sirnellin"  Birth: ABT 1785 in ,, VA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  Probably Loudoun or Culpepper County and probably named for John Snelling. John Snelling was killed in the Revolutionary War. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref. sherrjo@tenet.edu (Sherry Johnson) "Shenandoah County Continental Soldiers" Rootsweb.com
2 CONT
2 CONT John Snelling, 8th Va. Reg., husband of Elizabeth enlisted in Feb. 1776. Died Nov. 1776. Elizabeth remarried in 1781 after her husband was deceased...granted pension in Shenandoah County. See Rev. War Muster roll film # 120 served
2 CONC  as a Matross.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, one Enoch Snelling died at Valley Forge in June 1778, where Elias, Samuel and Jesse Ellis died. Orphans Court Minute Book 1774-1780 for Shenandoah County, VA p.2. "May 25, 1780 Acquilla Snellings, orphan of John is bound to 
2 CONC John Richardson to teach him the trade of blacksmith. He is now 14 years of age" i.e. born 1776.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Vol 30, p. 332 of DAR Index
2 CONT
2 CONT Gr.-granddaughter of John Snelling and Katherine Snelling, his wife. Gr.-gr.-granddaughter of Joseph Snelling, Jr. and Hannah Fulker, his wife, m. 1740.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gr.-gr.-gr.-granddaughter of Joseph Snelling (1695-1748) and Mary Payson, his wife, m. 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Snelling, Jr., served as clerk to the Commissary of Issues, at Boston, where in 1720 he was born.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1 Quality: 0 ABT 1828 in Sumner Co.,, TN 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Snelling sells his 250 acres on Drakes Creek, where he lived, on 28 October, 1828. See Estate records. By 21 January, 1829 Court appoints Estate administrator. We assume that Snelling dies (Nov.-Dec.) 1828.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret b. June 30, 1830 (conceived ca October 1829) was not his daughter. i.e. she was conceived after Snelling died. He is not shown in the 1830 census. It is therefore possible that widow "Peggy" marries the Mr. (Abram?) Ellis
2 CONC  in 1829. Jane Ellis, their daughter, is born August 25, 1835. Mr. (Abram ?) Ellis dies after May 1836 (when Edward S. is conceived) and before June 30, 1838 when "Peggy" is shown in Gallatin with school children under the name Ma
2 CONC rgaret Ellis.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1840 we find Margaret Ellis in Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: See Birth info.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1816-1819 held 200 acres near his brothers on Barrens River, Sumner Co., TN. North Drakes Creek, but is near the Barrens River. There are 2 Drakes Creeks. Isaac's and Snelling's property lay in what is now the town of Portlan
2 CONC d (was Richland Station).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1828 Snelling sold 250 acres, on which he lived, to Richard Baskerville. See estate papers. The land is shown on the 1878 map as lying near the border of Dist. 16 and 13. His land was bordered on the north by D. D. Cardwell(sp?
2 CONC ), on the East by heirs of Thomas Baskerville, on the South by John L. Bunton and George Blain, and on the West by O.H.P. Duval. All these names are shown in this area on the map.
2 CONT
2 CONT This land is located NNE of Richland Sta. P.O. (Now Portland), which is near the road and rail line NE of Fountainhead. 
2 CONT
2 CONT N.B. Thomas Snelling on Bread & Cheese Island. Thomas Snerling at Newcastle. From "1686 Pennsylvania census - along the Delaware River."
2 CONT
2 CONT Others named Snelling lived in NC near the Virginia border in the late 1700s. Said to have intermarried with the Hudsons. Snelling served in the War of 1812 with Samuel, in the 1st Regt. (Wynnes) W. Tennessee Militia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Robert ELLIS Jr. b: 1758 in Caernarvon twp 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Sarah DEHAVEN b: 1753 in Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Margaret "Peggy" HUDSON b: 20 SEP 1794 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *Married: 14 NOV 1810 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT *1. Samuel ELLIS b: 1813 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *2. John ELLIS b: 1813 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *3. Joshua ELLIS b: 4 JUL 1824 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *4. Thomas ELLIS b: 1813 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *5. Robert Chamberlain ELLIS b: 4 FEB 1812 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Note: Page 81 of the "Unpublished Manuscript" hints that he died prior to 1830.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct. 28, 1828 He signed a deed in Sumner County. Estate documents show deceased prior to January 1829. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Ansearchin News, published by the Tennessee Genealogical Society, Spring 1969: http://www.tngs.org/ansearchin/pdf/1969-1.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIAGE RECORDS OF SUMNER COUNTY, TENNESSEE, 1787-1838
2 CONT
2 CONT Copied· from the microfilm by Bettie Davis. (Mrs. Gene F.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Snelling Ellis and Peggy Hudson marry Nov. 14, 1810. Bondsman Benj. Hudson.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From the We Relate page on Snelling Ellis:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Snelling_Ellis_(2)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse and Children
2 CONT *H.  Snelling Ellis ABT 1785 - ABT 1829
2 CONT *W.  Margaret Humphreys Hudson 1794 - 1851
2 CONT *m. 14 NOV 1810
2 CONT *1. John Ellis
2 CONT *2. Samuel Ellis
2 CONT *3. Thomas Ellis
2 CONT *4. Richard Chamberlain Ellis 1812 - 1884
2 CONT *5. Joshua Ellis 1824 -
2 CONT
2 CONT Facts and Events
2 CONT *Name	Snelling Ellis
2 CONT *Gender	Male
2 CONT *Birth?	ABT 1785	VA
2 CONT *Marriage	14 NOV 1810	Sumner Co, TN to Margaret Humphreys Hudson
2 CONT *Death?	ABT 1829	
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably Loudoun or Culpepper County and probably named for John Snelling. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Snelling was killed in the Revolutionary War. Ref. sherrjo@tenet.edu (Sherry Johnson) "Shenandoah County Continental Soldiers" Rootsweb.com John Snelling, 8th Va. Reg., husband of Elizabeth enlisted in Feb. 1776. Died Nov. 17
2 CONC 76. Elizabeth remarried in 1781 after her husband was deceased...granted pension in Shenandoah County. See Rev. War Muster roll film # 120 served as a Matross. Orphans Court Minute Book 1774-1780 for Shenandoah County, VA p.2. "Ma
2 CONC y 25, 1780 Acquilla Snellings, orphan of John is bound to John Richardson to teach him the trade of blacksmith. He is now 14 years of age" i.e. born 1776. From Vol 30, p. 332 of DAR Index Gr.-granddaughter of John Snelling and Kat
2 CONC herine Snelling, his wife. Gr.-gr.-granddaughter of Joseph Snelling, Jr. and Hannah Fulker, his wife, m. 1740. Gr.-gr.-gr.-granddaughter of Joseph Snelling (1695-1748) and Mary Payson, his wife, m. 1717. Joseph Snelling, Jr., serv
2 CONC ed as clerk to the Commissary of Issues, at Boston, where in 1720 he was born. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: We assume that Snelling dies ca 1829. More than likely, Margaret b. June 30, 1830 (conceived ca October 1829) was his daughter. i.e. she was born after her father died, as he is not shown in the 1830 census. If he was the fa
2 CONC ther, then he died sometime after October 1829 and prior Nov. 21, 1830, the date the census taker turned in all his data. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is therefore possible that widow "Peggy" marries the Mr. (Abram?) Ellis say ca 1834. Jane Ellis, their daughter, is born August 25, 1835. Mr. (Abram ?) Ellis dies after May 1836 (when Edward S. is conceived) and before June 30,
2 CONC  1838 when "Peggy" is shown with school children under the name Margaret Ellis. In 1940 we find Margaret Ellis in MO. Note: See Birth info. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1816-1819 held 200 acres near his brothers on Barrens River, Sumner Co, TN (This is North Drakes Creek near Fountain Head). N.B. Thomas Snelling on Bread & Cheese Island. Thomas Snerling at Newcastle. From "1686 Pennsylvania 
2 CONC census - along the Delaware River." Others named Snelling lived in NC near the VA border in the late 1700`s. Said to have intermarried with the Hudsons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Snelling served in the War of 1812 with Samuel, in the 1st Regt. (Wynnes) W. TN Militia.
