2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I313 
2 CONT *Name: Isaac ELLIS 
2 CONT *RFN: 313 
2 CONT *Change Date: 27 JUN 2006 
2 CONT *Sex: M 1 Quality: 0 
2 CONT *Birth: 1788 in ,, VA 
2 CONT *Note: Franklin or Culpepper County (?), Virginia. 
2 CONT *Change Date: 22 JUL 1996 
2 CONT *Death: 1864 in Sumner Co.,, TN 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Isaac's oldest son Hudson C. Ellis was appointed by the Court as Administrator of the estate. Hudson was sued by all of the other heirs as it appears that he did not wish to sell the land and have the proceeds divided among 
2 CONC them. The Court decided in their favor and the land was sold and the heirs paid. If the estate was settled (debts were paid off by Hudson) would he have inherited the land as the eldest son ? i.e. thus the law suit. He died intest
2 CONC ate. In the settlement of the estate no mention is made of a wife and Olivia is presumed to have "departed" prior to 1864.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were two Sarahs, one Isaacs dau. married to John Reed. The other Sarah married to Ezekiel Harper is a "mystery".
2 CONT
2 CONT She received a share of the estate. N.B. This is in error !
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter Sarah married Ezekiel Harper. The other Sarah was the daughter of Ellen Ellis and William Butler (Ellen deceased prior to August 1843). Sarah Butler married Johnathan "John" Reed.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: It should be noted that Isaac and Snelling married Hudson girls and their sister Elizabeth married John Hudson. Refer to land given by Chamberlain to his sons in law.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1816-1819 held 100 and later 200 acres on Barrens River, Sumner Co., TN. Ref. Tax records. N.B. This location was on what is called North Drakes Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are 2 Drakes Creeks. Isaac's property lay in what is now the town of Portland (was Richland Station).
2 CONT
2 CONT There was an Isaac Ellis who served in the 14th. Regt. (Mitchissons) Kentucky Militia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Robert ELLIS Jr. b: 1758 in Caernarvon twp 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Sarah DEHAVEN b: 1753 in Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Mary "Polly" HUDSON b: 7 JUN 1792 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *Married: 2 19 MAR 1810 in Sumner Co.,, TN 
2 CONT *Note: John Hudson was the Bondsman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *1. Alexander Duval ELLIS b: 4 APR 1824 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *2. John D. ELLIS b: 1820 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *3. William Edward ELLIS b: 13 MAR 1826 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *4. Eliza ELLIS b: 1836 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *5. Hudson C. ELLIS b: 1818 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *6. Margaret G. ELLIS b: ABT 1813 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *7 Catherine Ann Ellis b: 27 FEB 1827 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *8. Ellen ELLIS b: in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT *9. Isaac Jr. ELLIS b: 1825 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: 1850 Sumner County, TN
2 CONT *Abbrev: US CENSUS 1840-1870
2 CONT *Type: Census - Filmed
2 CONT *Date: 8 DEC 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Family shown in 1820 thru 1870 Census to be in Sumner County, TN. p. 166--1840; p.66--1850; p. 231--1860; p. 98--1870.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1850 Sumner County Census (Sept. 27, 1850) shows: Isaac Ellis 62, land value $4000, b. VA; Mary Ellis 58 wife; John 30; William 19; Elizabeth 14; Sarah 13; Currin 13. Not shown: Ellen, Catherine, Hudson, Isaac, Jr., Alexander 
2 CONC D., and Frank Ellis.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1860 Census, p. 198 (338) shows: Isaac 70; Olivia 54 (really 57); Elizabeth 21; John D. 35; John Riddle 13; Sarah Butler 20.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olivia Pierce b. 26 June 1803 was from Pittsylvania Co., VA. First married to Thomas Lester. Died 26 Oct. 1887 and buried in Skeen Cemetary, Simpson Co., KY. The County Probate records show Pierce and Riddle in the same timeframe.
2 CONC  The Sumner County Marriage records 1787-1834 show Eleanor, Isaac, Snelling, Jesse and Elizabeth. 
