1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Served in the War of 1812 under General Jackson
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from Lloyd D. Ellis:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dubart&id=I448
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I448 Name: Samuel E. ELLIS RFN: 448 
2 CONT
2 CONT Change Date: 15 MAY 2004 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 17 OCT 1791 in Culpepper or Franklin Co.,, VA and Death: 20 SEP 1879 in Allen Co.,, KY 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Allen County, Kentucky Cemetery Records, Volume 1 by Rabold and Price p. 131-132: Stoney Point Cemetery
2 CONT
2 CONT Stoney Point Cemetery is at Stony Point Church on Highway 100, near Alonzo in Allen County, Kentucky. It is about 4 1/2 miles from the Simpson County line, and about 4 miles from the Sumner County, Tennessee line. One part of the 
2 CONC cemetery is beside the church, the other is across the road from the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellis, Samuel, October 17, 1791 - September 20, 1879
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellis, Elizabeth F., wife of Samuel Ellis, August 20, 1791 - July 22, 1862
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Could the E. in his name stand for Elliott? He named one of his sons Fountain Elliott Ellis.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served with Snelling in the 1st Regt. (Wynnes) W. Tennessee Militia in the War of 1812.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Allen County Ky marriages:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fountain E. Ellis m. Martha Elizabeth Anthony 12-4-1855.
2 CONT
2 CONT *James " Mary Parker 3-3-1840
2 CONT
2 CONT *Joseph " Martha Tracy 7-9-1829
2 CONT
2 CONT M. E. M. (Muse) Virginia C. Clark 3-23-1842
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel " Elizabeth Gaines 3-19-1815
2 CONT
2 CONT *Wm. J. " Catherine A. Austin 10-15-1851
2 CONT
2 CONT *Wm. J. " Ann R. Acres 12-14-1868
2 CONT
2 CONT *Leonidas A. " Lauretly G. Alexander 5-15-1869
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha A. " Grandson Terrill 11-3-1834
2 CONT
2 CONT *Nancy " Humphrey Rice 12-5-1835
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy J. " Jonathan W. Roark 9-4-1865 (Samuels GD)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Jane " Asa D. Brashear 9-6-1852
2 CONT
2 CONT (other females)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Could these be children of Abram Ellis ?
2 CONT
2 CONT All the rest are children of Samuel E. Ellis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Robert ELLIS Jr. b: 1758 in Caernarvon twp 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Sarah DEHAVEN b: 1753 in Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Elizabeth (Betsy) GAINES b: 20 AUG 1791
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 20 APR 1815 in Allen Co.,, KY 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Allen County marriages shows date as May 19, 1815. The April date may be the date of the bond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Fountain Elliott ELLIS b: 13 OCT 1833 in ,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Martha A. ELLIS b: 14 APR 1816 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Mead F. ELLIS b: 24 DEC 1817 in Allen Co.,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Muse M. ELLIS b: 27 DEC 1819 in Allen Co.,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Samuel G. ELLIS b: 21 DEC 1821 in Allen Co.,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Sarah Jane ELLIS b: 31 MAY 1824 in Allen Co.,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. John J. ELLIS b: 17 JUN 1826 in Allen Co.,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Mary Adeline ELLIS b: 23 JUN 1828 in Allen Co.,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Abram Thomas ELLIS b: 25 JAN 1831 in Allen Co.,, KY
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Samuel and Elizabeth were born in Culpepper Co., Va and must have known each other from childhood. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gaines families early founders of Culpepper County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
