1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information from Lloyd D. Ellis:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dubart&id=I450
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I450 
2 CONT *Name: Abram ELLIS ? 
2 CONT *RFN: 450 
2 CONT *Change Date: 5 JUL 2004 
2 CONT *Sex: M 
2 CONT *Birth: 1795 in Franklin Co VA 
2 CONT *Death: 1836 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT We assume that Snelling dies ca 1829. More than likely, Margaret b. June 30, 1830 (conceived ca October 1829) was his daughter. i.e. she was born after her father died, as he is not shown in the 1830 census. It is therefore possib
2 CONC le that widow "Peggy" marries the Mr. (Abram?) Ellis say ca 1829. Jane Ellis, their daughter, is born August 25, 1835. In 1840 we find Margaret Ellis in Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abram lived in Humpreys Co. TN then Simpson Co., KY. Said to have had 5 children. An Abram Ellis shown in the 1820 census for Caldwell county KY, p. 32. with 2 boys under age 10, 2 age under 18, 2 girls under 10, 2 females over 18
2 CONC  (hard to read). If he married in 1818, this is not our Abram. The 1830,40 and 50 census does not show Abram in KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1840 Missouri Census Lewis County, p. 187 shows an Abram Ellis with 3 male children under age 5; 1 age 5-10; 1 adult male age 40 & under 50. Three female children ages 10 to under 15 and one adult female age 30 to under 40. Th
2 CONC is female was born 1800-1810 whereas "Peggy" was born in 1794. Some ages fit and there are 7 children. The 1850 census does not show this Abram Ellis.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no Abram in 1840 TN census. The TN 1830 census for Humphrey County p. 309 shows one Abram Ellis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Males
2 CONT *1 b. 1815-1820
2 CONT *1 b. 1790-1800 Abram
2 CONT
2 CONT Females
2 CONT *1 b. est. 1829
2 CONT *1 b. est. 1827
2 CONT *1 b. est. 1826
2 CONT *1 b. 1810-1815
2 CONT *1 b. 1800-1810 Wife R.....
2 CONT *1 b. 1770-1780 ? Wrong ages given ?
2 CONT
2 CONT In the next household was Elizabeth Hudson (his sister) wife of John Hudson. Upon his death she married Benjamin Hudson. One of the neighbors was a William W. Dixon. See later marriage of Jennie Ellis to a Wm. Dixon.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: Robert ELLIS Jr. b: 1758 in Caernarvon twp 
2 CONT *Mother: Sarah DEHAVEN b: 1753 in Pennsylvania
2 CONT *Marriage 1 Margaret "Peggy" HUDSON b: 20 SEP 1794 in Sumner Co.,, TN
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *1. Edward Silvanus ELLIS b: 4 FEB 1837 in Sumner Co., TN ?
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 2 R...
2 CONT **Married: 1818 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellis family Bible is very faded. Appears to be 1818 but probably 1815. Dixie McCrary notes show date as 1825. Possible names: Ruth, Rachel, Rebecca.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret "Peggy" Hudson remarried a Mr..........Ellis after the death (ca 1829) of her first husband Snelling Ellis, brother of Abram. To stay in the family, could she have married Abram? See Humphrey Co., TN (where her parents li
2 CONC ved) and Simpson Co., KY.
