1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Obadiah Seely=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT M, b. 5 June 1614, d. 25 August 1657
2 CONT
2 CONT •Father: William Seely b. c 1580
2 CONT •Mother: Alice Bisshell b. c 1580
2 CONT •Note*: Item 2 of the 2nd Generation of Robert Seely
2 CONT •Burial*: Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT •'''Note''': Many things our unknown about Obadiah. Not sure when and where he was born. His real mother and father has not been recored to this date. (This date not proven) Came with Robert Seely from England 1630. Obadiah Seeley
2 CONC  was an early resident of Stamford, C bounded by lands of Obadiah Seeley on the north. Obadiah and Mary were married in Stamford, CT. and their first child was born there 1648. In Obadiah acknowledged payment of a debt due hin fro
2 CONC m John Lareson. Obadiah died intestate Aug. 25,1657. Inventory of his estate was dated Dec. 24 1665 and mentions his widow Mary and their sons Obadiah, Cornelius and Jonas. Distribution of estate was dated Sept. 3, 1666. Habakuk S
2 CONC eeley died at the age of 3 in
2 CONT •Note: More information on Obadiah will be comeing from the next meeting of the SGS. Aug. 1992. No m
2 CONT •Note: SGS VOL 1 page, 6
2 CONT •Birth*: 5 June 1614, Birmingham, Warwickshire, Eng
2 CONT •Birth: 1630/31, England
2 CONT •Marriage*: 1647, Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT., Principal=Mary Angel
2 CONT •Death: 25 August 1657, Stamford, Fairfield, Ct, Usa
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: : '''Mary Angel''' b. c 1623, d. a 7 Nov 1666. Married in 1647, Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''Obadiah Seely II'''+ b. c 1645, d. 25 Jul 1679
2 CONT *  '''Cornelius Seely'''+ b. c 1649, d. a 1714
2 CONT *  '''Jonas Seeley'''+ b. 22 Jul 1652, d. 27 Mar 1703
2 CONT *  '''Habakuk Seely''' b. c 1655, d. 13 Jun 1658
2 CONT
2 CONT =SECOND GENERATION OF OBADIAH SEELEY LINE=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Seeley Genealogical Society, 2000, by, Katherine M Olsen 639 8th Avenue , Salt Lake City, UT 84103-3124
2 CONT
2 CONT Please read the information contained in this book carefully, especially the entries that deal with your ancestors. if you have additions, corrections, comments, or concerns, please send documentation to me at the above address. I
2 CONC  will continue to update the three books which my mother and I have compiled. Members will be informed of changes to any of the three books in the Seeley Genealogical Sociely Newsletter.
2 CONT
2 CONT This particular book took more than three years to compile and is twice as big as the Sixth Generation Families! We believe that an Eighth Generation Families is out of the question! We, therefore, challenge descendants to locate 
2 CONC information, compile and publish similar books beginning with either a seventh or eighth generation person listed in this book and submit that publication to the Seelye Research Center Director, Terry Tietjens, P0 Box 337, Abilene
2 CONC , KS, 67410- 0337.
2 CONT
2 CONT We appreciate all those who have contributed to the body of knowledge that we have about the Seeley (with the various spellings) family. We acknowledge countless hours of research and preparation of records by many people includin
2 CONC g Esther L. Houtz Walters, Elizabeth White, Helene Ault, and many others.
2 CONT
2 CONT We would like to thank John R. Seely, Eugene Seelye, Terry Tietjens and Lester Stevens and many others for their assistance with this project.
2 CONT
2 CONT Not all records agree. We have had to use "discretion and logic" in trying to assemble family groups. We have had to make some "judgment calls." Some records may not agree with your collected records. Some problems have been resol
2 CONC ved and some have not. It is our wish that what we have done is acceptable. We wanted it to be perfect. We know that is not possible.
2 CONT
2 CONT There has been a question of the ancestry of Obadiah (SGS#4) for some time. It is clear from the evidence that Obadiah is not the son of Robert and Mary Mason Seeley, nor does there appear to be any close relationship. Because SGS
2 CONC  numbers have already been assigned in the previous publication of Generations One Through Five, and The Sixth Generation Families, it has been decided that the numbering of Obadiah's descendants will not change. At the time of th
2 CONC e original publication, Obadiah was considered a son of Robert, and so he was listed as being a part of the second generation. We have kept that designation. It appears that Obadiah's father may have been William Seeley. We are wa
2 CONC iting for more research to be concluded in this area.
2 CONT
2 CONT Using this book should be simple. Each individual has been given a number. Robert Seeley is SGS #1. His son, Nathaniel Seeley, is SGS #2. Obadiah Seeley is SGS #4. This numbering continues through each successive generation. These
2 CONC  numbers are referred to as SGS numbers. The numbers, once assigned, do not change. When further data is known of an individual, the number will be followed by an asterisk and the name will be capitalized. Data for that individual
2 CONC  will follow in the next generation in numerical order.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since this is a Seeley (with the various spellings) genealogy we have not included information beyond the initial generation for individuals with other simiames. Example--When Ann Seeley married John Smith, her children with surna
2 CONC me "Smith" are included with as much information as we have, but are not carried forward.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following abbreviations have been used: b=born; bapt=baptised; d=died; m=marned; bur=buried. Dates are listed day/month/year. We have given information about parentage of spouse when available. We have included residence if kn
2 CONC own. if military service has been rendered, we have noted it as a part of the record.
2 CONT
2 CONT We are grateful to have had access to computers for this massive undertaking. This is a ©Microsoft Word 6.01 document. The indices have been prepared using ©Microsoft Word 6.01. It is hoped that in the future, this information wil
2 CONC l be entered into ©Personal Ancestral File. At that point, family group sheets and pedigree charts could be generated in both DOS and MAC formats.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jim Seeley, 3003 Gatepost Lane, Herndon, VA 20171-2247, 703-860-4897, jrseeley@aol.com, is serving as the Genealogist of the Seeley Genealogical Society. Contact him if you need or have information on other Seeley (or any of the v
2 CONC arious spellings) individuals that are not included in any of the three books.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seeley Genealogical Society, 1997 (SGS#4) OBADIAH SEELEY (2) (?William) (chr 5 Jun 1614, SL Martin Parish, Birmingham, Warwickshire, England; d 25 Aug 1657, intestate, Stamford, CT; estate distributed, 3 Sep 1666) Perhaps the son 
2 CONC of William Seeley. married Stamford, CT, Mary Angel Miller (b about 1623, probably England). Daughter of James and Anna Elliot Angel. Widow of John Miller (d 1642, Stamford, CT). John Miller was one of the first settlers of Wether
2 CONC sfield, CT and Stamford, CT. John Miller's will mentions his wife Mary and sons; John, Jonathan, and Joseph. John and Jonathan Miller settled in Bedford, NY. Joseph Miller (d 1730, Cohansy, NJ) settled in Cohansy, NJ in 1691. Obad
2 CONC iah Seeley was an early resident of Stamford, CT. On 20 Feb 1648, it was recorded that the land owned by John Holly was bounded on the north by lands owned by Obadiah Seeley. Obadiah and Mary Angel Miller Seeley resided in Stamfor
2 CONC d, CT. Their first child was born there in 1648. In 1649, Obadiah Seeley was listed as a citizen of Stamford, CT. In 1651, Obadiah Seeley acknowledged payment of a debt due him from John Lareson. Obadiah died intestate 25 Aug 1657
2 CONC . Inventory of his estate was dated 24 Dec 1665. The inventory mentions his widow, Mary and their sons Obadiah, Cornelius and Jonas. Mary Angel Miller Seeley made an oath on 7 Nov 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT = Children (2)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * 17* '''OBADIAH SEELEY''' (b about 1648/49, Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT; d 25 Jul 1679/80, Stamford, Fairfield Co., CT) m 1669, Esther Stevens (b about 164&9). Daughter of Thomas and Ann Stevens of Stamford.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 18* '''CORNELIUS SEELEY''' (b about 1649/50, Stamford, CT; d after 1714/15, Bedford, Westchester Co., NY) m before 1674, Priscilla Osborn (b 3 Mar 1650; d after 1710, probably Bedford, Westchester Co., NY). Daughter of Richard a
2 CONC nd Mary Osborn.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 19* '''JONAS SEELEY''' (b about 1653, Stamford, CT; d 1703, Stamford, CT) m 1st, Sarah/Mary Slawson/Slason m 2nd, about 1689, Mary Wicks/Weeks Waterbury (b about 1660; d 31 Dec 1738, Stamford, CT). Daughter of Thomas and Elizabe
2 CONC th Wicks of Stamford, CT. Widow of John Waterbury. Son of John Waterbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 20 '''Habakuk Seeley''' (b about 1655, Stamford, CT; d Jun 1658, Stamford, CT)
2 CONT
2 CONT = References:=
2 CONT
2 CONT Anderson, Jerome research Chase Saga of Seelys History of Stamford, CT, p 164. Houtz, Esther research Phipps, Alan research Seely, John R. One Line of Seely Descendants 
2 CONT
