1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abigail (Smith) Gustin
2 CONT ==Birth==
2 CONT Abigail (Smith) Gustin was born on March 27, 1766 in Sussex, New Jersey, British America. She was the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Abraham-Smith-I/6000000041721729979 and https://www.geni.com/people/Hannah-Smith/6000000
2 CONC 041723246076. See the note below about her parents. 
2 CONT ==Marriage==
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/John-Gustin/6000000011564853883 and https://www.geni.com/people/Abigail-Gustin/6000000011564762175 were married before 1783 in New Jersey.
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Abigail-Mabee/5671297656300123134 
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Sophia-Wood-Gustin/6000000047517041975
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Gustin-Jr/6000000011564876138
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Jemima-Wood/6000000011565071702
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Katy-Gustin-Wood/6000000011563495085
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Rachel-York/6000000059567068869
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Eliphalet-Gustin/6000000011564071748
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Isaiah-Gustin/6000000011562753004 (not in father's will)
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Gustin/6000000011564836610 (not in father's will or Pioneer Sketches)
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Patience-Gustin/6000000011564688421 (research is needed - no sources)
2 CONT * https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/11647/images/dvm_GenMono001186-00113-0?ssrc=&backlabel=Return&pId=201
2 CONT ==Death and Burial==
2 CONT Abigail (Smith) Gustin passed away by 1814 when https://www.geni.com/people/John-Gustin/6000000011564853883 remarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Research==
2 CONT Pioneer Sketches of Long Point Settlement: Or, Norfolk's Foundation Builders ...By Egbert Americus Owen
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gustin married Abigail, daughter of Abraham Smith, He had three sons-- Charles, Isaiah, and Eliphalet, and six daughters-- Abigail, Freelove, Jemima, Catherine. Salome, and Sophia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT pg 125.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Abigail was the daughter of Abraham Smith, who came from Orange Co., NY, to Fort Erie, Upper Canada (Ontario) in 1787. It is possible that her mother was Abraham's wife Rachel, but also possible that she and her two oldest sibling
2 CONC s were children of an earlier wife. Abraham and Rachel were on the membership roll of the Wantage Baptist Church in Sussex Co., NJ, in 1783, about the time of Abigail's marriage to John Gustin of Sussex Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT "While in New Jersey, Abraham’s oldest daughter Abigail married John Gustin prior to the birth of their first child in New Jersey about 1783. John Gustin`s uncle Jeremiah Gustin married Bethany Fuller, daughter of the first Baptis
2 CONC t minister of Wantage Baptist Church at Newton, Sussex County, New Jersey." https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/11647/images/dvm_GenMono001186-00112-1?ssrc=&backlabel=Return&pId=199
2 CONT
2 CONT She and her husband, and their first two daughters, settled in Upper Canada (Ontario) with her parents and siblings in 1787. She had 11 known children, all of whom are linked below.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail was mentioned in her husband's will in 1800. She signed a deed with him in 1807, and also had a child born that year. She died sometime between then and her husband's second marriage in 1814.
2 CONT ==Notes== 
2 CONT # Genealogist Alan Clark has published an article conjecturing that Abigail's mother was a woman named Hannah Finn. This is entirely unsubstantiated, along with the existence of Hannah Finn (as the first wife of Abraham Smith or o
2 CONC therwise). Clark also speculated that Abraham Smith's wife Rachel's maiden name was Decker based on their naming a daughter Mary Decker Smith. Again, this is speculation and should not be considered anything other than that until 
2 CONC further documentation of her identity is discovered.
2 CONT # Also, the creator of this memorial, Tom Hoot, placed the memorials for John and Abigail Smith Gustin in the Ingersoll Rural Cemetery with eldest daughters Abigail Mabee and Sophia Wood. I am not aware of any documentation of eit
2 CONC her John's or Abigail's grave. It seems more likely, based on the information I have, that they were buried in the Vittoria Baptist Cemetery given that they were founding members of the church. Her parents and their eldest son Cha
2 CONC rles are interred there. If this is the case, then no gravestone survive for them. Any information to help resolve this question will be much appreciated. --Joseph R. Klett Note: Heartfelt thanks to Tom Hoot for creating this memo
2 CONC rial.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=45402079 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 26 2017, 18:19:21 UTC''
2 CONT
