1 NAME Lavinia "Vinie" S. /Rumbaugh/
2 GIVN Lavinia "Vinie" S.
2 SURN Rumbaugh
2 _MARNM Newhouse
2 NICK Vini
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 APR 1851
2 ADDR
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 OCT 1934
2 ADDR
3 CITY Pittsburgh
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} # Event: Fact 4. Unknown 5 Oct 1901 Sold lot and house in Delmont, PA 1
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: Fact 3. Unknown 25 Sep 1893 Purchased her sister's interest in house and lot in Delmont, PA 2
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: Fact 3. Unknown 4 Apr 1891 Deed to the Estate of John M. Rumbaugh conveyed to William Hugas 3
2 CONT
2 CONT # Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Alias: "Vinie /Newhouse"/
2 CONT
2 CONT     Lavinia aka "Vinie". She is not in Josial's will and did not live with
2 CONT
2 CONT     him when he died. Therefore she probably died between 1901 and 1907 or
2 CONT
2 CONT     was separated. The 1901 deed states she lived in Pittsburgh and he in
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hempfield Twp. Must check 1910 Census for Pittsburgh. She appears to have
2 CONT
2 CONT     been divorced from her first hushand, George E. Stoker.
2 CONT
2 CONT     A two story brick house and lot in Delmont (then called New Salem) was
2 CONT
2 CONT     sold by Jacob Newhouse, brother of Josiah to Lavina's father, John
2 CONT
2 CONT     Rumbaugh in 1879 for $500. After John died, his wife Mary sold the
2 CONT
2 CONT     property to her two daughters Lavinia and Zora in 1891 for $750. Zora
2 CONT
2 CONT     sold her share to Lavina in 1893 for $600. Lavina sold the property (or
2 CONT
2 CONT     her share, as she was married to Josiah Newhouse) to John McCreary in
2 CONT
2 CONT     1901 for $250. But Josiah did not die until 1907 and does not mention
2 CONT
2 CONT     Lavinia in his will. Therefore, it is my theory that they were divorced
2 CONT
2 CONT     and the sale to McCreary was part of a settlement.McCreary might have
2 CONT
2 CONT     been an attorney.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Title: Deed of Lavina and Josiah Newhouse to John McCreary
2 CONT
2 CONT       Repository:
2 CONT
2 CONT       Page: Deed Book Vol. 329 Pages 186-187
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Title: Deed: Izora Newdorfer to Lavina Stoker
2 CONT
2 CONT       Repository:
2 CONT
2 CONT       Page: Deed Book Vol. 228 Pages 559-560
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Title: Power of Attorney: Mary Rumbaugh et al to A.J. Newdorfer
2 CONT
2 CONT       Repository:
2 CONT
2 CONT       Page: Deed Book Vol. 192, p.610 
