1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LA PLATA HOME PRESS, La Plata, Missouri Wednesday, July 11, 1953. MARY BLOOM ---Mrs. Mary Bloom died at their farm home southeast of La Plata at 7:00 Tuesday night, being at the time of death, seventy-nine years of
2 CONC  age. ---Mary Viola Space, daughter of George and Mary Space, was born near Bowling, Rock Island County, Illinois on August 25, 1856 and died July 9, 1935 near La Plata, Missouri. On March 24, 1877 she was married to George Bloom 
2 CONC of Bowling, Illinois. In 1906 she and her family moved near La Plata where she spent the rest of her life. ---She is survived by two daughters and three sons, namely, Mrs. Warren Burnham of Gibbs, Missouri, Mrs. William Shuman of 
2 CONC Jerusalem, Ohio, James of Montpelier, Iowa, Ira of La Plata and Hartley with whom she made her home. She is also survived by seven grandchildren. ---Her husband died April 21, 1918. ---She joined the Illinois Bend Christian Church
2 CONC  under the ministry of Rev. Kitchen. ---Funeral services were held in the Christian Church at 3:15 Thursday afternoon by the pastor, Dannie F. Martin. Burial was made in the La Plata cemetery.
