1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''KANSAS CITY TIMES NEWSPAPER - March 18, 1974 GLENN W. IRICK <nowiki>-------</nowiki>''' - Glenn William IRICK, 62, of 5809 Laurel, Raytown, died Thursday at a hospital in Knoxville, Tennessee. He had been visiti
2 CONC ng a daughter, Mrs. Louis WHITE, Knoxville. He was born in Colony, Kansas, and had lived here five years. Mr. IRICK worked for the Missouri Highway Department. He also leaves his wife, Mrs. Helen IRICK of the home. Graveside servi
2 CONC ces will be at 3pm today in Edgewood Cemetery, Knoxville.
2 CONT
2 CONT First patient ever at Parkwest Hospital in Knoxville, TN on December 10, 1973. Was released and later readmitted in March, when he died there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joined Army September 1, 1943 at Jefferson Barracks, MO. "Enlistment for the duration of the War or other emergency, plus six months, subject to the discretion of the President or otherwise according to law"
