1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Andrew was born to parents John Yocum(1718-1761) and Elizabeth DeHaven/Inhaven(1723-1808). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of nine children: Eleanor(1742-?), Peter(1744–1785), Jonas(1746–1793), Peter(1747–1785,) Rebecca(1754–1843), Jesse(1756–1812), John(1757–1844) and Mary(1760–1844).
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew married Hannah Smith (1737-1811), daughter of Goerge and Jane Eagens in Philadelphia, Philadelphia County, Pa. on August 9, 1762. (source: Record of Pennsylvania Marriages & Marriage Record of the Swedes' Church aka Gloria 
2 CONC Dei. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Hannah had six children together: John(1766-1833), Peter(1767-1823), Moses(1769-1830), James(1771-1839), Isaac(1773-18550 and Rebecca(1775-1818).
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew died on February 17, 1777 and is laid to rest together with his wife Hannah in Christ Church (Old Swedes), 740 River Rd, Bridgeport, Pa. 19405. Upper Merion, Swedesburg, Pa. Near Bridgeport. (610) 272-6036 
2 CONT
2 CONT bio by Jill
2 CONT
2 CONT sources:  1. Pennsylvania, Marriage Records, 1700-1821 Record for John YocumPennsylvania, Marriage Records, 1700-1821  shows John Yocum marriage to Elizabeth L. Inhaven March 14, 1739. 2. American Revolution Records: John Yocum bi
2 CONC rth as 1718. 3. American Revolution Records: Andrew b. 2 Dec 1739, Philadelphia, Pa., paretns Joh Yocum & Elizabeth Dehaven, wife Hannah Smith
