2 CONT
2 CONT Grietjen Margariette Pletjes. She married Herman van de Alderkerk Opdengraeff on 16 August 1605 at Old Church, Muir, Kleve, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany.1 Grietjen Margariette Pletjes died on 7 January 1643 at Krefeld, Krefeld,
2 CONC  North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, at age 54.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Herman van de Alderkerk Opdengraeff b. 26 Nov 1585, d. 27 Dec 1642
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Herman Opdengraeff+1 b. 28 Feb 1616, d. 17 Jan 1669
2 CONT
2 CONT http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p5995.htm#i180026
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Jasper William Penn’s mother was the child of Alet Pletjes. Alet Pletjes is the sister of Greitjen Pletjes. Greitjen Pletjes marries Herman Op Den Graeff. The descendants of Herman and Greitjen Pletjes Op Den Graeff are a
2 CONC mong the original 13 Krefeld immigrants to Pennsylvania (Ulle, 1983), and they are William Penn’s first cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT (William Penn was the grandnephew of Herman1's wife, Grietje)
2 CONT
2 CONT Herman Op De graeffin the U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900-Name: Herman Op Degraeff Gender: Male Birth Place: Aldekerk, Herzogtum Kleve, Heiliges Römisches Reich Deutscher Nation, Birth Year: 1585 Spouse Name: Gr
2 CONC ietie Pleties,Spouse Birth Year:1587, Number Pages: 1 - http://search.ancestry.co.uk/cgibin/sse.dllindiv=1&db=WorldMarr_ga&h=328096&tid=&pid=&usePUB=true&usePUBJs=true&rhSource=7486
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Grietjen Pletjes1
2 CONT *F, b. 16 November 1588, d. 5 June 1643
2 CONT *Father*	Driessen Pletjes b. c 1560, d. 22 May 1608
2 CONT *Mother*	Adelheid Goebels b. c 1562
2 CONT *Last Edited	29 Sep 2009
2 CONT *Birth*	16 November 1588 	Margaret Grietjen Pletjes was born on 16 November 1588 at Kempen, Westphalia, Germany. 
2 CONT **She was the daughter of Driessen Pletjes and Adelheid Goebels. 
2 CONT *Marriage* Margaret Grietjen Pletjes married Herman Op Den Graef on 16 August 1605 at Aldekerk, Muir, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Germany. 
2 CONT *Death*	5 June 1643 	Margaret Grietjen Pletjes died on 5 June 1643 at Krefeld, Westphalia, Germany, at age 54. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note*	 	She Is the mystery of the Op Den Graff windows all serendipity? Did our Bishop Hermen and his wife, Grietje attend Krefeld Market one day and find two or more window frames for their townhouse? The frames just happened to 
2 CONC have hints of the Hebrew Cabala and signs of the Mysteries of the Rosary on them. Nevertheless, Hermen and Grietje decided such fancy work would be good advertising for the linen business and cloth industry. Their Pletjes family n
2 CONC iece, Margaret Jasper had married a Van Der Schuren and migrated to Ireland to escape the ridiculous. Religious wars over church real estate and to invest in or inherit her own real estate; and her crazy son from her second marria
2 CONC ge (William Penn, one of the largest real estate investors in history) had not yet been born to sit down, as if in front of the second window, to write or pen a pamphlet, entitled: "No Cross, No Crown."
2 CONT
2 CONT So, after all this recitation, we are still confronted by a haunting mystery displayed on a beautiful set of stained glass windows dated 1630 AD: One Hermen Op Den Graff, one Blessed Mother of Christ, one missing family seal, one 
2 CONC family motto, two extant windows, two different Lohengrin Swan Seals, three shields of a multiple Dukedom, three rectangular insets, four family seals, five centuries of Mennonite-Anabaptist Witness, twenty mystical circles of fra
2 CONC me decoration, twenty centuries of Apostolic Interrogation: Who shall separate us from the love of God?
2 CONT
2 CONT Readers of this Thesis are encouraged to discuss it with Glen Wayne Miller. Commentary, documentation and even logical speculation are welcome. You may write to: GW Miller, 136 West Price Street, Philadelphia, PA 19144, or Kevin L
2 CONC . Sholder, 414 Blackstone Dr., Centerville, OH 45459-4111.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.siscom.net/~rdrunner/HTML/Questions.html] 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father may have been Pletjes Driessen of Kempen, a small town halfway between Krefeld and Aldekerk. She sometimes went by surname Pletjes Driessen.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Had 18 children. Mennonite.
