2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Hallerken Op Den GRAEFF was born on 1 Jul 1614 in Kaldenkirchen, Lower Rhine, Prussia, German.(3751) She died in 1691 in Kaldenkirchen, Lower Rhine, Prussia, German. (3752) She was buried in 1691 in Kaldenkirchen, Lower Rhin
2 CONC e, Prussia, German.(3753)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT  Married Theodorus Daermans/DOORS  Katholisch, Toenisberg Kempen, Rheinland, Prussia Germany) Children were: Gertrude Op Den Graeff DOORS.
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT # ILLIKREN HALLERKEN AGNES OP DEN GRAEFF 1
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sex: F
2 CONT
2 CONT # Birth: 01 JUL 1614 in Kaldenkirchen, Rheinland, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aachen
2 CONT
2 CONT # Religion: Member of Reformed Church of Kaldenkirchen. 1655
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: Comment 1 Also known as Hallerken.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: Born- 01 SEP 1614 Kaldenkirchen, Rheinland, Germany 1
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: AFN: ZS09-S1
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: NEESSEN/ NEES Name- AGNES 1
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: Name-Alt. AGNES NESSGEN OP DEN GRAEFF
2 CONT
2 CONT # Event: Born-Alt. BET 1616 AND 1618 Kaldenkirchen, Rheinland, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT # Death: 20 AUG 1691 in Krefeld, Rheinland, Prussia, Germany 1
2 CONT
2 CONT # Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     The lexicon source or dictionary cited by Mr. Howard Swain in hisemail to CONCORD ORIGINAL 13 website in August 2001:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mr. Swain has located the missing source I had looked for in1997---but Mr. Swain has the opposite perspective on AGNES andHILLEKEN---with no linguistic connections in the listed origins of thewords in Hebrew or Greek or Latin 
2 CONC or German or Dutch.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Part of my original reasoning: HILLEKEN if traced back to the HebrewHILLEL means Praise (Hill) of God (El). AGNES from the Greek whenassociated with the Latin AGNUS DEI means Lamb (agnus) of God (Dei).
2 CONT
2 CONT     The Hebrew PRAISE OF GOD in the theology of the Christian liturgy isdirected to THE LAMB OF GOD which taketh away the sins of the world.The lamb is the CHASTE LAMB (without blemish)---and we speculate theRoman Catholic court r
2 CONC ecord or baptism record lists AGNES in place ofHilleken.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Since there were two HILLEKEN entries on the FREEMAN document for OpDen Graff---we speculated the HILLEKEN ABOVE as misread andtranscribed as HILLEKEN AGNES---but you notice we begin to makeexcuses for our inability to read th
2 CONC e correct years of birth ordeath---even with the aid of a magnifying glass.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Please feel free to post this EMAIL data---or contact Mr. Howard Swaindirectly whose work is to be commended for his attempt at INTEGRITYAND THOROUGHNESS.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Glenn Wayne Miller Research
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: HERMAN BISH ISAACKS OP DEN GRAEFF b: 26 NOV 1585 in Aldekerk, Rheinland, Prussia
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: MARGARET GRIETJEN SYLLYS PLETGENS PLETJENS b: 26 NOV 1588 in Holland
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 THEISS MATTHIAS (Imm) PETERS DOORS TYSON b: 18 SEP 1614 in Kaldenkirchen, Rheinland, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Married: ABT 1640 in Kaldenkirchen, Rheinland, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
