1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/139048211/peter-cassel
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1700's all legal and historical documents were written by hand. The person responsible for recording the information usually spelled a person’s name the way it sounded. Therefore, the same exact person was occasionally reco
2 CONC rded in different historical documents using slight variations in the spelling of his last name (and sometimes his first name). The last name of Castle was occasionally spelled as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Castle, or Cassel, or Cassell, or Kassell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Cassell was born in Palatinate, Germany. Peter immigrated to Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=bhree...
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Cassel was the son of Johannes Cassel, a Mennonite who came on the ship Jeffries to Philadelphia in 1682 after attending a meeting in Kriesham, Germany, in which William Penn himself spoke to the audience about religious fre
2 CONC edom and the land that was available in America.  Johannes became one of the signers of the Germantown, Pennsylvania charter.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hans Peter Kassel was a son of Johannes Cassel and Mary (?).
2 CONT
2 CONT His father Johannes was a Reverend of the Mennonites that Immigrated to America. Peter arrived in America in Philadelphia on 20 Nov 1686 on the ship "Jefries". His father was a weaver by trade and settled at Germantown county of P
2 CONC hiladelphia. (Source: Cassel Family pg 29 by Daniel Kolb Cassel 1896) https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhist00cass
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Peter Kassel Arrival Year: 1686 Arrival Place: Germantown, Pennsylvania Family Members: Wife Mary; Child Peter Source Publication Code: 3570.1 Primary Immigrant: Kassel, Johannes Annotation: Date of arrival with port or plac
2 CONC e of settlement, a few are date and place of first mention of residence in New World. Listings of mostly Mennonite German immigrants, the majority were from Baden-Durlach in the Palatinate. Source Bibliography: JOHNSON, MRS. ARTA 
2 CONC F., editor. "Immigrant Ancestors." In The Palatine Immigrant. Vol. 5:1 (Summer 1979), pp. 44-46; vol. 5:2 (Autumn 1979), pp. 87-91; vol. 5:3 (Winter 1980), pp. 138-143; vol. 5:4 (Spring 1980), pp. 183-187. Page: 88 Original data: 
2 CONC Filby, P. William, ed. Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s. Farmington Hills, MI, USA: Gale Research, 2012.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter married Catherine Elizabeth Hobart in Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is mentioned in the Cassel Family in America book by Daniel Kolb Cassel 1896 Morgan R Wills, Publisher on pg 30.
2 CONT
2 CONT "He has been court crier in Germantown for several years, and resided at Germantown."
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter and Catherine Elizabeth had a son Jacob 'The Hunter' Castle who founded Castle's Wood's later named Castlewood, Russell County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castlewood,_Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Court crier for several yeas. Resided in Germantown. 
