2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Cassell was born about 1682 in Kriegsheim, Worms, Hessen, Germany. She is the daughter of Johannes Cassell and Maria op den Graeff.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kriegsheim in the Palatinate (which is in the present day known as Kriegsheim in Rheinland-Pfalz, Germany).[1] She is the daughter of Johannes Kassell and sailed with him and her four older siblings aboard the ship "Jefries" in 16
2 CONC 86 to come to America.[2] Her father and immediate family were Quakers, although her extended family were Mennonites.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 30th, 1709, Sarah married Edward Dawes, widower of Elizabeth Rhodes[3]
