1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "'''Conrad Custer/Custard''', the son of Arnold Kusters, was born about 1695 in Germany. No record of his birth or baptism has been found, but it is now believed that Conrad's father, Arnold, did not leave Germany 
2 CONC until after 1696 so Conrad would have been born before they left. His mother was probably Gerdrut Conrats as found on the marriage certificate in Krefeld. In the years 1706-1708 Arnold Kuster sent his children to the Friend's Scho
2 CONC ol where Francis Daniel Pastorius taught, and it is assummed that Conrad was among the students..[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 1714 Conrad moved with his parents to the Manatawney tract, now in upper Montgomery County. About this time he met and married Susannah Adams/Addams. No record of their marriage has been found. Susannah was the oldest child
2 CONC  of Richard and Gertien (op den Graeff) Adams. Richard Adams and his family were members of the Vincent Branch of the Great Valley Baptist Church. Many records of this church are in Welch so it is believed that the Adams family wa
2 CONC s of Welch descent. The Great Valley Baptist Church was is Chester County, Pennsylvania, just across the Schuykill River from Arnold Kuster's land...."[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of Conrad:[5] 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Charity Custer, born about 1715...
2 CONT # Arnold Custer/Custard, born about 1718...
2 CONT # Richard Custer, born 1722/1723...
2 CONT # William Custard, born 1729 Philadelphia County, PA...
2 CONT # Paul Kustar, born about 1730, PA...
2 CONT # Nicholas Custer, born 1732...
2 CONT # Cunrad Custard, born 1735...
2 CONT # Joseph Kester/Custard, born 14 March 1752, PA...
2 CONT
2 CONT 7th Generation Grandson of Ololus Kuster, Kaldenkirchen, Germany
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://generations-past.net/castor/conrad01.html
2 CONT
2 CONT >Conrad CUSTER, was one of the most remarkable of the Castor clan.  He was born in Germany about 1695.  He migrated from Kaldenkirchen, Germany between 1696 and 1700 with his father, grandfather, and Uncles Johannes and  Hermanus.
2 CONC   He is reputed to have had thirty children; three daughters and twenty-seven sons.  Legend says all twenty-seven sons fought in the Revolutionary War. Amazingly he didoil lamp raise many children.  His son Arnold CUSTER (c1718-17
2 CONC 59) and his brother George CUSTER (1705-1759)  were both killed by Indians during the French and Indian War in 1759.  Also the wife of Conrad's grandson, William Custer, had been captured by Indians at about the same time leaving 
2 CONC him with children too young to fend for themselves.  Conrad had had two wives and at least eighteen children of his own and some of them were still young; so Conrad was likely responsible for 27-32 children under 16.  He died at B
2 CONC rock's Gap, Rockingham County, Virginia on 1 February 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kuster-39
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Conrad Kuster (Sr.) wife name is Elizabeth in his Last Will & Testament.  Wife Elizabeth is alive at this will proceeding on 16 Aug 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5582056/conrad-custer Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 11 2018, 13:43:04 UTC''
2 CONT *https://kycarter.com/charts/custer.pdf
2 CONT *http://www.caoa-genes.org/ccweb/ccv22-o/p1.htm#i2
2 CONT *http://generations-past.net/lola/castor-o/p16.htm#i579
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kuster-39
2 CONT
2 CONT Category: Kuster Name Study
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT "Arnold Kuesters, baptized 9 June 1669, Kaldenkirchen, Germany; married Gertrude Conrads 24 June 1691, Krefeld Reformed Church, Krefeld, Germany; married Rebecca (surname unknown); died 1739, Hanover Twp., Philadelphia County, PA,
2 CONC  buried Manatawney Mennonite Cemetery..." [TheDescendants of Paulus and Gertrude Kusters of Kaldenkirchen, Germany and Germantown, Pennsylvania, the first four generations", Jean M. White, Editor; Publisher The Castor Association 
2 CONC of America; page 18]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Conrad Custer/Custard, the son of Arnold Kusters, was born about 1695in Germany.  No record of his birth or baptism has been found, but itis now believed that Conrad's father, Arnold, did not leave Germany until after 1696 so Con
2 CONC rad would have been born before they left.  His mother was probably Gerdrut Conrats as found on the marriage certificate in Krefeld.  In the years 1706-1708 Arnold Kuster sent his childrento the Friend's School where Francis Danie
2 CONC l Pastorius taught, and it is assummed that Conrad was among the students. ["The Descendants of Paulus and Gertrude Kusters of Kaldenkirchen, Germany and Germantown, Pennsylvania, the first four generations", Jean M. White, Editor
2 CONC ; Publisher The Castor Association of America; page 18]
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 1714 Conrad moved with his parents to the Manatawney tract, nowin upper Montgomery County.  About this time he met and married Susannah Adams/Addams.  No record of their marriage has been found.  Susannah was the oldest chi
2 CONC ld of Richard and Gertien (op den Graeff) Adams. Richard Adams and his family were members of the Vincent Branch of the Great Valley Baptist Church.  Many records of this church are in Welch so it is believed that the Adams family
2 CONC  was of Welch descent.  The Great Valley Baptist Church was is Chester County, Pennsylvania, just across the Schuykill River from Arnold Kuster's land...." ["The Descendants of Paulus and Gertrude Kusters of Kaldenkirchen, Germany
2 CONC  and Germantown, Pennsylvania, the first four generations", Jean M. White, Editor; Publisher The Castor Association of America; page 99]
2 CONT "Conrad died 1 February 1772 in Brock's Gap, Augusta County, Virginia.On 17th of March Conrad's nuncupative[sic] will was proved...." ["The Descendants of Paulus and Gertrude Kusters of Kaldenkirchen, Germany and Germantown, Penns
2 CONC ylvania, the first four generations", Jean M.White, Editor; Publisher The Castor Association of America; page 107]
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children ===
2 CONT
2 CONT "Known children of Conrad: ["The Descendants of Paulus and GertrudeKusters of Kaldenkirchen, Germany and Germantown, Pennsylvania, the first four generations", Jean M. White, Editor; Publisher The Castor Association of America; pa
2 CONC ge 117]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  Charity Custer, born about 1715...
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  Arnold Custer/Custard, born about 1718...
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.  Richard Custer, born 1722/1723...
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  William Custard, born 1729 Philadelphia County, PA...
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  Paul Kustar, born about 1730, PA...
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  Nicholas Custer, born 1732...
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.  Cunrad Custard, born 1735...
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.  Joseph Kester/Custard, born 14 March 1752, PA...
