2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/156990749
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Trumbo married Mary Dorthea Custer in 1739. She had been born in 1718 in 
2 CONT Rockingham County, Virginia. She was the daughter of Conrad Custer and Susannah  Adams. She would have been 22; Jacob, 26.  They appear to have spent most of their lives in Virginia, and in particular  Rockingham County, where Mar
2 CONC y was apparently born in 1718. Mary lived until at  least to 1755 when her son, Jacob was born.  Jacob survived until 1783 and died in Brock‘s Gap, Augusta County (later  Rockingham), Virginia, at the age of 69. It is still uncert
2 CONC ain whether Jacob was  in the present-day Augusta County or Rockingham County.  Their home was “on the very edge of the frontier at that time. The wilderness  was over the mountains on the west side of the valley. [It was] a time 
2 CONC of war.  [In 1758], the Indian massacres occurred at Upper Tract and Ft. Seybeter. There  appears to be no record of the family having suffered at the hands of the  Indians. It is quite possible that for a time the family had to s
2 CONC eek safety from  the Indians.”  Jacob and Mary had several children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Elizabeth b. 1737 d. 1826 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Margaret b. 1740 d. 1811 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Andrew b. 1743 d. 1827 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Elizabeth b. 1745 d. 1819 
2 CONT
2 CONT • John b. 1747 d. 1819 
2 CONT
2 CONT • George b. 1750 d. 1830 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Margaret b. 1750 d. 1830 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Dorothy b. 1753 d. 1819 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Jacob b. 1755 d. 1841
2 CONT
