1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ancestor #:  A212969
2 CONT
2 CONT William Custard, Sr (son of Isaac Davids and Jannetje Mauritz) was born 1729 in Philadelphia,Philadelphia,PA, and died 1826 in Egypt Mills,Pike,PA204. He married Sarah Swartout on 05 Aug 1754 in Dutch Reformed,Machackeneck,Orange,
2 CONC NY204, daughter of Barnardus Coobes Swartout and Margeret Decker.
2 CONT
2 CONT VALLEY VIEW CEMETERY -
2 CONT
2 CONT Located about 3.25 miles north of Bushkill in Lehman Township on a hill just west of Route 209.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Found this reference-need to review info on link:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Tombstone death date is in error: Please see my entry detailing the circumstance, with images of William's Will & Probate of 1806, at: http://minisinkvalleygenealogy.blogspot.com/2013/05/tombstone-errors-william-custard-egypt.html
2 CONC  ~ ATJ on 5/25/2013
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The information below is from a newspaper article published to locate next of kin for those interred in this cemetery. This cemetery is known as both "Valley View Cemetery" and "Swartwood Cemetery".
2 CONT
2 CONT Pike Co. Dispatch Thursday Dec 7, 1972
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTICE
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the fourth of a series of Notices by Gannett Fleming Corddry and Carpenter, Inc., Engineers, Harrisburg, Pennsylvania, for information needed by them to complete a survey and report concerning the existing cemeteries on th
2 CONC e Pennsylvania side of the proposed Tocks Island Lake. The survey is being made for the Philadelphia District, Corps of Engineers, for the purpose of determining the actual number of graves, the names of the deceased, and the name
2 CONC s and addresses of the next of kin or nearest living relative.
2 CONT
2 CONT This Notice seeks information about the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT - VALLEY VIEW CEMETERY -
2 CONT
2 CONT Located about 3.25 miles north of Bushkill in Lehman Township on a hill just west of Route 209. The following names or initials were taken from headstones:
2 CONT
2 CONT (A list of names follows, among them the interred person here.)
2 CONT
2 CONT NEW INFORMATION PROVIDED BY FAG CONTRIBUTOR #47582697 --
2 CONT While browsing the images in Family Search's Pennsylvania Probate Records I happened upon an entry which surprised me:
2 CONT William Custard's Last Will and Testament & Probate, Wayne Co Wills, Vol. I, No. 12, are both dated 1806. His tombstone, located at the Swartwood burying ground in Pike County Pennsylvania, bears a death date of 1826.
2 CONT
2 CONT I've detailed the error with an image and a link to Family Search, together with my photo of his & Sarah's tombstones (which are all over Ancestry.com - used without permission or credit) in a blog entry here:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://minisinkvalleygenealogy.blogspot.com/2013/05/tombstone-errors-william-custard-egypt.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Thought you might be interested in joining me to correct the date by noting this error in your bio of William. I've added an update to the current caption for my photo on your memorial for him.
2 CONT
2 CONT I suspect the origin of the error was the 1933 transcription in the book, Cemeteries, Graveyards and Burying in Pike County Pennsylvania IF the replacement headstone postdates the transcription.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT William Custard actually died in 1806. This is proved by his will in the Wayne County PA probate records, vol 1 - 2, image 13. The will was written 21 June, 1806. Letters of Administration were granted 10 October, 1806, indicating
2 CONC  that he had passed away prior to that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps 1826 was the date in which the stone was erected.
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributor Judy Martin notes: " I agree something is wrong somewhere because he is listed on the 1800, 1810 and 1820 census records, which would be more inline with the death year 1826."
