1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Chalfant Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken from'' An Addington/Chalfant Family History'' by David Vern Addington, published 1992.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://daddington.com/chalfantfamily.htm<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT John Chalfant emigrated on the ship "Canterbury", arriving in the Port of Philadelphia on 30 Nov 1699 with his uncle John Chalfant and cousins John Chalfant, born 1689, and Robert Chalfant, born 1688. John settled with his uncle J
2 CONC ohn on the Brandywine near Birmingham, in Chester County, Pennsylvania. They named this land "Rockland Manor". John Chalfant, born 14 Apr 1690, is often identified as John Chalfant of West Marborough where he settled. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John and his wife, name unknown, had sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Joseph Chalfant
2 CONT (2) Isaac Chalfant
2 CONT (3) Henry Chalfant
2 CONT m. 15 Aug 1742, Elizabeth Jackson
2 CONT (4) James Chalfant*, b. 20 Feb 1717, d. 1 Jan 1808
2 CONT m. Hannah Harris
2 CONT (5) William Chalfant
2 CONT (6) John Chalfant
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT John Chalfant's father was Henry Chalfant, born 13 May 1663, who married in 1687 in England to Elizabeth Chandler, a daughter of Thomas Chandler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry and Elizabeth (Chandler) Chalfant had children
2 CONT (1) Robert Chalfant, b. 26 Sep 1688, d. 13 May 1693
2 CONT (2) Henry Chalfant, b. 3 Jul 1689, d. 7 Sep 1728
2 CONT (3) John Chalfant*, b. 14 Apr 1690, d. 7 Sep 1729, Pennsylvania
2 CONT (4) Elizabeth Chalfant, b. 12 Mar 1691 m. 4 Jul 1712, Caleb Swayne
2 CONT (5) Ruth Chalfant, b. 28 Jun 1692, died young.
