3 NOTE Wilhelm Strepers came on the Concord in 1683 as well he sold to Nicolas Kreesman who in turn sold to Rev. H.M. Mühlenberg... so goes the chain of title for these central early PA families...
3 NOTE The Concord is said to be the first of the "German" ships under Penn's stewardship (13 Mennonite-Quaker families of Krefeld.) https://gameo.org/index.php?title=Concord_%28Ship%29
3 NOTE Many of the earlies on the Map were given free land by Penn:  > Lenart Arets and Opdengraff were two
4 CONT Rotterdam, Germany (6 July) via London, England (24 July) to Philadelphia, Pennsylvania
4 CONT 6 October 1683
4 CONT
4 CONT Captain William Jeffries
4 CONT A 500 ton ship measuring 130 x 32 feet.
