1 NAME Clarissa Martha /Clark/
2 GIVN Clarissa Martha
2 SURN Clark
2 _MARNM Olin
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 FEB 1822
2 ADDR
3 CITY Springfield
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 AUG 1883
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kent
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''[Ransom] was married October 10th, 1843, to Clarissa M. Clark, at her father's home in Franklin township. She was born February 6th, 1822, in Springfield, Summit County, Ohio. She was of a family of ten children,
2 CONC  eight of whom reached mature years. Her father moved into the southeast part of Streetsboro when she was about eight years old...
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Mrs. Olin was a truly excellent woman. To her, the home was the sacred place on earth, and here she found her largest and best field of work; and she still lives embodied in the lives and characters of her children, who honor he
2 CONC r memory. But she reached beyond the home circle, and every worthy enterprise found in her a friend and helper. With the Universalist branch of the Christian church, she united soon after an organization was secured in Kent, in 18
2 CONC 66, and ever continued a consistent and worthy member. Her departure leaves a sad vacancy in the home and church, but the memory of her Christian life and work is a source of great comfort to all who mourn. She had been in feeble 
2 CONC health for a considerable time, but the hope of her recovery was entertained till within a few weeks of her death. The best efforts of medical skill were unable to save her, and Monday morning, August 13th, 1883, she bade adieu to
2 CONC  earth life. Her funeral services, conducted by Rev. Andrew Willson, her former pastor, and the Rev. Edward Morris, were held in the Universalist Church at four o'clock, Wednesday afternoon, and were largely attended.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''They had eleven children. '' 
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Biographical Sketches and Records of the Ezra Olin Family" by George Sheldon Nye
