1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information from Lloyd D. Ellis: http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dubart&id=I447
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I447 
2 CONT *Name: Margaret "Peggy" HUDSON 
2 CONT *RFN: 447 
2 CONT *Change Date: 10 NOV 2003 
2 CONT *Sex: F 
2 CONT *ALIA: Peggy or "Peigi" (Gaelic for /Margaret)./ 
2 CONT *Birth: 20 SEP 1794 in Sumner Co.,, TN 
2 CONT *Change Date: 11 AUG 1996 
2 CONT *Death: 1851 in Vernon Co.,, MO 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  Per Hudson Family Assn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Her son Joshua moved to Missouri. Joshua and Penelope's children all born in St Clair Co., MO per 1860 census: 
2 CONT *1. James R. Ellis, ca 1854; 
2 CONT *2. Alex S. Ellis, ca1855; 
2 CONT *3. John Ellis, ca 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Married at age 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sumner County Schools. From Loose Records, Microfilm item 39, in the Sumner County Archives. June 30, 1838 Students ages 6 to 16, show Margaret Ellis Dist. 20 with 2 children in school. Only other Ellis listed is Isaac in Dist. 20
2 CONC  with 3 children. Margarets 2 children could have been 
2 CONT *Margaret age 8 and 
2 CONT *Snellings son Joshua age 14.
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears that "Peggy" went to Bates Co., MO, per the 1840 census, with three children 
2 CONT *Edward S. age 3 (b. 1837), 
2 CONT *Jane age 5 (b. 1835), 
2 CONT *Margaret age 9-10 (b. 1830).
2 CONT
2 CONT Compare this with the Abram in Lewis Co., MO 1840 census.(another person?)
2 CONT
2 CONT Bates County 1850 census shows her married to a Mr. Lewis. Double check Boon and Bates county census.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Her son Joshua lived in St. Clair Co., MO.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: Chamberlain Hudson JR. 
2 CONT *Mother: Margaret GWIN b: 28 MAR 1760 in Orange Co.,, NC
2 CONT
