1 NOTE {geni:about_me} see: "J. Francis" on attached map detail (Shannonville)
2 CONT
2 CONT fun fact : near the crossing of Egypt Rd was a settlemet once called Shannonville. The name was changed to Audubon c. 1900
2 CONT Here's the Audubon site c. 1950 http://www.phillytrolley.org/audubon/audubon_mill-grove_map-1.html Read more at http://www.phillytrolley.org/audubon/audubon-shannonville.html
2 CONT
2 CONT "A petition with a hundred names was submitted to the postal service, and the name of the town was changed to Audubon. The author's concerns were of course bourne out: a hundred years later not many in Lower Providence Township (M
2 CONC ontgomery County, PA) think of the Shannons. But for the names of a couple local roads, not many today think of '''''Francis''''', Walts, Crawford, Wetherill, Walker, '''''Highly''''', Kulp, or Dettra either." > By Mike Szilagyi o
2 CONC f the Philly Gazette (Mike Szilagyi's career as a bicycle-trail planner and designer includes researching former railroad rights-of-way)
