1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ≤p>Served in Civil War on Union Side Co. A, 10th Ill. Vol. Cavalry. After the war he moved his family (in 1866) from near Springfield, Illinois to Rusty Knob, Kansas, (near Emporia) where he had relatives, later to Four Mile, Butl
2 CONC er Co. Where they homesteaded. They moved to Pretty Prairie in 1885. Per E. Lester Foulke's obituary, Watson and Olive moved from Cottonwood Falls to Wichita and then to Pretty Prairie where E. Lester was reared.≤/p>te with metal 
2 CONC case that belonged to Watson.≤/p>
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ≤p>≤span style="color: #202121; font-family: verdana, 'PingFang SC Light', 'PingFang TC Light', PingFang-SC-Light, PingFang-TC-Light, 'PingFang SC', 'PingFang TC', 'Hiragino Sans GB', 'Lantinghei TC Extralight', 'Lantinghei SC Ext
2 CONC ralight', FZLTXHB--B51-0, FZLTZHK--GBK1-0, 'Heiti SC Light', STHeitiSC-Light, 'Heiti SC', 'Heiti TC Light', STHeitiTC-Light, 'Heiti TC', 'Microsoft Yahei', 'Microsoft Jhenghei', 'Noto Sans CJK KR', 'Noto Sans CJK JP', 'Noto Sans C
2 CONC JK SC', 'Noto Sans CJK TC', 'Source Han Sans K', 'Source Han Sans KR', 'Source Han Sans JP', 'Source Han Sans CN', 'Source Han Sans HK', 'Source Han Sans TW', 'Source Han Sans TWHK', 'Droid Sans Fallback', HanaMinBFont, Ayuthaya, 
2 CONC sans-serif; font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.035px; background-color: #ffffff;">When Watson Everard Foulke was born on 10 September 1826, in Buckingham, Buckingham Township, Bucks, Pennsylvania, United States, his father, Everer
2 CONC d Foulke Jr., was 26 and his mother, Frances Watson, was 30. He married Olive Helen Sayles in 1860, in Champaign, Illinois, United States. They were the parents of at least 3 sons and 3 daughters. He lived in Bruno Township, Butle
2 CONC r, Kansas, United States in 1880 and Ninnescah Township, Reno, Kansas, United States in 1900. He died on 27 February 1909, in Pretty Prairie, Reno, Kansas, United States, at the age of 82, and was buried in Lone Star Cemetery, Pre
2 CONC tty Prairie, Reno, Kansas, United States.≤/span>≤/p>
