1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Josiah Seely served in the Orange County Militia during the Revolutionary War. References to his military service include the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT "New York in the Revolution," by James A Roberts, published in 1898, Page 253.  He is shown as an enlisted man in the First Regiment of the Militia, commanded by Major Zarhariah Du Bois.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Documents relating to the Colonial History  of the State of New York," by Berthold Fernow, published in 1887, Pages 289 and 290.  He is shown as a 1st Lieutenant in the Oxford Company of the Cornwall Regiment, commanded by Colone
2 CONC l Jesse Woodhull.  The Oxford Company commander was Captain Thomas Horton.  The notation is listed under, "Changes in the Regiment," dated March 31, 1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT "History Of Orange County, New York," by R.M. Ruttenber and L.H. Clark, published in 1881, Page 48.  He is shown as a 1st Lieutenant in the Oxford Company commanded by Captain Thomas Horton with the date of 1777.  The company was 
2 CONC part of Colonel Jesse Woodhull's Cornwall Regiment.  The Cornwall Regiment and four others made up the Fourth Brigade commanded by General George Clinton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is listed in the SGS Vol. I as # 181on Page 25.
