1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Obadiah Seely III
2 CONT
2 CONT M, b. 1670, d. 4 September 1745
2 CONT
2 CONT  •Father: Obadiah Seely II b. c 1645, d. 25 Jul 1679
2 CONT  •Mother: Esther Stevens b. 1648
2 CONT
2 CONT  •Note*: Obadiah spent most of his life in Stamford, Ct. He was one of the founders of Bedford, NY., but returned to Stamford, selling his Bedford property to Thomas Chambers by 1710. When Quenn Anne issued the patent in 1704 for 
2 CONC the Dibble and Vinyard Purchase, Obadiah was among the 1st proprietors, along with Cornelius Seeley's, Sr and Jr. and Samuel Seeley. The Van Cortlandts later bought most of the share, but Obadieh is not listed among those selling.
2 CONC  His grandsons John and Gideon moved to that area about 1760.
2 CONT  •Note: Children all born Stamford, Ct.
2 CONT  •Birth*: 1670, Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT.
2 CONT  •Marriage*: 5 December 1692, Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT., Principal=Susanna Finch
2 CONT  •(Witness) Note: 31 October 1696, Fairfield, Ct, Usa, his brother Obadiah was appointed adminstrator Mar. 9, 1697 This info from SGS page, 10 Fairfield Probates Vol 3, page, 171 The child listed for this bBentamin has not ben pro
2 CONC ven, Data sent to me with other data., Principal=Benjamin Seely
2 CONT  •Will: 2 September 1745, His will was dated Sep. 2, 1745; proved Oct. 1, 1745; inventory of the estate Nov. 2, 1745. Mentions wife Susanna and children John, Nathaniel, Obadiah, Elijah and Susanna Bishop.
2 CONT  •Death*: 4 September 1745, Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: Susanna Finch b. c 1671, d. a 1745
2 CONT  •Marriage*: 5 December 1692, Stamford, Fairfield Co. CT., Principal=Susanna Finch
