1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001 1799 - 1867
2 CONT ==Birth==
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001 is thought to have been born about 1797/99. She was the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Gustin/6000000011564853883 and https://www.geni.com/people/Abigai
2 CONC l-Gustin/6000000011564762175. 
2 CONT ==Marriages==
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Manuel/6000000000008361306 and https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001 were married around 1816.
2 CONT # John Stone and https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001 were married in 1836 in Erie County, Ohio. (There is an incomplete license in 1942 which had been requested by Ebeniser Warner. Her husband may have 
2 CONC been https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stone-III/5678040426580060202
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/John-Manuel/6000000000008361306 and https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Caroline-Sturges/6000000219465475737
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Frederick-Manuel/6000000219465475488
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Eliphalet-Manuel/6000000226811818876
2 CONT John Stone and https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001 
2 CONT # Salome Stone
2 CONT ==Residences==
2 CONT * She was living in Charlotteville Twp., Norfolk Co., ON, in 1823, when she and her siblings quitclaimed the remainder of their father's lands to their brother Eliphalet.
2 CONT * Port Huron, St. Clair, MI 
2 CONT ==Property==
2 CONT St. Clair Mortgages
2 CONT
2 CONT Saloma F Little to Eliphalet G. Manuel  18 July 1870
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated: 26 June 1870  $ 1000
2 CONT
2 CONT being land formerly owned by F. D. Manuel (https://www.geni.com/people/Frederick-Manuel/6000000219465475488) and conveyed to him to Freelove Stone and by said F. Stone to Salomia F. Little 
2 CONT
2 CONT Executed by Saloma F Little & Nelson Little
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Death==
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Freelove-Manuel/6000000059566991001 passed away on June 9, 1867 in Port Huron, St. Clair County, Michigan.  She was buried in Block K Lot 35 in Lakeside Cemetery, Port Huron, St. Clair County, Michigan.
2 CONT ==Will==
2 CONT Will of Freelove Stone Cal 2 338 St. Clair Probate Office  
2 CONT Witnessed: 9 June 1857
2 CONT Entered probate: 7 October 1867 
2 CONT Son-in-law and daughter Salome & Nelson Little
2 CONT land deeded to her from F D Manuel and Harriett his wife 
2 CONT
2 CONT Court - And it further Appearing that said Freelove Stone last dwelt and had her residence  in, and was an inhabitant of Port Huron in said County and there died.
2 CONT ==Son-In-Law==
2 CONT CAPT. NELSON LITTLE, Section 21, P. O. Port Huron, is a native of Canada, and was born on the St. Clair River April 6, 1833. He began sailing when twelve years of age on the schooner Comet. When eighteen years old he was mate of t
2 CONC he Smead and the Tom Corwin for two years, and in 1853 sailed Captain of the Tom Corwin, and since then has sailed master of the Scott, Storm, Barclay, Forwarder, the tug Kate Moffatt, the Kate Richmond. He has been in the marine 
2 CONC service thirty-five years, and is one of the oldest Captains sailing from this port, and has lived here on the river twenty-nine years. He owns a farm of forty acres where he lives, and forty acres near home. In 1854, he married M
2 CONC iss Salomi F. Stone, a native of Vermillion, Erie County, Ohio. They have one son, John, living in Port Huron.
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/arx2236.0001.001.umich.edu/page/581/mode/1up
2 CONT ==Note== 
2 CONT The information in this memorial, created by the late Tom Hoot, has not been verified in primary sources and should be considered questionable. Tom showed Freelove's birth year as 1807, which is clearly incorrect since she was nam
2 CONC ed in her father's will in the year 1800. It is unclear why he created memorials for two different spouses named Sterns. Further documentation of Freelove's life and vital dates is needed. The death year and burial place shown see
2 CONC m very questionable.
