2 CONT * '''NOTE''': As of 1874, three towns in the southern portion of Westchester County---Kingsbridge, West Farms, and Morrisania---were appended to the City of New York (which at that time consisted of Manhattan Island). These three 
2 CONC towns were located west of the Bronx River. As of 1895, the village of Wakefield, and the towns of Westchester, Pelham, and Eastchester---all of them located east of the Bronx River---were appended to New York County. Thus, it is 
2 CONC difficult to know where Frank died in New York County, although most likely he died on Manhattan Island. 
2 CONT * '''NOTE''': As of 1898, the southern portion of Westchester County became the Borough of the Bronx, after the creation of Greater New York City. In 1914, the Borough of the Bronx was separated from New York County and became New
2 CONC  York state's newest county, Bronx County---while retaining its name of the Borough of the Bronx.
