1 NOTE {geni:about_me} After the personal property taxes of 1794 were paid, William and his family left Virginia and moved to the Ohio Territory by flatboats on the Ohio River. they settled in the part of Hamilton County that was designa
2 CONC ted as Sugarcreek Twp., Greene County when Ohio became a state in 1803. William was one of the organizers of the Middle Run Baptist Church, July 27, 1799, and was a very active member of the church and community affairs. He served
2 CONC  as a state senator in 1816 and later served as County Commissioner.
2 CONT
