1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fort Worth Gazette – Friday - October 30, 1891 DEATHS. Marshall, Harrison County, Oct. 27. Died in this city, October 26, at 12:15 p.m., after a protracted illness of eight months, Dr. R.G. Hamill, aged seventy-nin
2 CONC e years. His remains were interred in the Greenwood cemetery Tuesday, October 27, at 3 o'clock p.m. Dr. Hamill was born in South Carolina in 1812, and moved to Marshall in 1865. He was a minister in the Methodist church, having be
2 CONC gun preaching in 1831 at the age of nineteen years. He was one of the oldest dentists of the South.
