1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth 	22 Mar 1891 Pleasant Lake, Steuben County, Indiana, USA Death 	15 Apr 1980 (aged 89) Coldwater, Branch County, Michigan, USA Burial 	 Lyon Lake Cemetery Wrights Corners, Calhoun County, Michigan, USA Plot 	R
2 CONC ow 40N, Lot 80N Memorial ID 	99520672 · View Source Marshall (MI) Evening Chronicle Wednesday, April 16, 1980 Warren O. Goodwin GIRARD - Warren O. Goodwin, 89, of Girard, died April 15 at the Maple Lawn Medical Care Facility in Co
2 CONC ldwater after a long illness. ---Mr. Goodwin was born March 22, 1891, at Pleasant Lake, Ind., the son of Joseph W. and Oliva (Brown) Goodwin. He was married July 23, 1933, at Crown Pointe, Ind., to Grace Hall. He had lived in Gira
2 CONC rd since 1930, retiring in 1960 from the Goodwin Saw Mill. A 1913 Tri-State College graduate in electrical engineering, he was a member of the First Baptist Church and over 50 years belonged to the Northeastern Masonic Lodge No. 2
2 CONC 10 of Fremont, Ind. He also belonged to the Branch County Historical Society. ---Surviving are his wife; four sons, Barry L. Goodwin of Coldwater, Van P. Goodwin of Sudbury, Mass., John Goodwin of Houston, Texas, and Charles Goodw
2 CONC in of Charlemont, Mass.; two daughters, Mrs. Barbara G. Avery and Mrs. Ann Doyle, both of Charlemont, Mass.; 15 grandchildren; nine great-grandchildren. ---Services will be at 2 p.m. Thursday at the Putnam Funeral Home in Tekonsha
2 CONC  with the Rev. Don F. Price of the Family Altar of the Air officiating. The family will receive friends at the funeral home from 7 to 9 p.m. today. Interment will be at Lyon Lake Cemetery, Marshall.
