1 NAME George Washington /Son/
2 GIVN George Washington
2 _MARNM Son
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 SEP 1852
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 DEC 1924
2 ADDR
3 STAE WY
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dr. George W. Son, who practiced medicine in Desloge for a number of years and left here with his family several years ago to settle in Wyoming, died at his home in that state Wednesday, December 24, 1924. Dr. Son 
2 CONC suffered a stroke of paralysis some two years since shortly after the death of his wife, and his death was brought about from a second stroke. Interment took place in Wyoming.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Son was 72 years of age at the time of his death and will be remembered by many Desloge and Flat River people. He enjoyed a large practice in his profession, while located in this district, and was widely and favorably known. 
2 CONC He was a native of Missouri, having been born and reared in Jefferson City. He was a brother of Dr. T. A. Son, who is still practicing in Bonne Terre, and leaves a large family of brothers and sisters who join with his immediate f
2 CONC amily, three children, Eva, James and Oliver, and his grandchildren, in mourning his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE DESLOGE SUN, Desloge, St. Francois Co. MO, Tues. Jan. 6, 1925
2 CONT
2 CONT
