1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Susanna Supplee, the widow of Peter Supplee, the Revolutionary soldier, some time after the close of the war emigrated to Yates county, New York. She took her daughter Rachel with her, leaving her son Peter with hi
2 CONC s grandmother Magdaline, at the old homestead place in Worcester, Montgomery county, Pennsylvania. Rachel belonged to the fifth generation of the Supplee family in America.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of Melchoir and Gertrude Steyer Wagener.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=153434670 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 26 2018, 1:19:41 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st m. 3-6-1774 PETER SUPPLEE Sr. (1745-1778) & 2 known CHILDREN survived- RACHEL & PETER Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd m. SGT PHILIP CLUMBER(G) Jr. (d. Sept 1793 PA #166038182), Occupation: Barber, 2 known CHILDREN- REBECCA 1783-1846 & JOHN 1791-1849.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3rd m. [presumed] Mr. CLANFORD.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Melchior Wagener and Gertrude Steyer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 'Genealogical Record of the Schwenkfelter Families', S.K. Brecht, pg 1440; FREE ONLINE https://books.google.com
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT 'Susanna is buried in The Sheppard Lot...the name on the tombstone is given as Susanna Clanford' and her children also buried there are given the name Clanford Rebecca & John (no FAG found)
