1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/15441013/abraham_wagener
2 CONT
2 CONT page 1447 Schwenkfelder book
2 CONT
2 CONT Pioneer. Descended from Montgomery County, Pennsylvania, farmers, he continued farming when he moved to New York state. He also owned apple orchards (the Wagener apple is named after him), a saw mill, and a grist mill. When the vi
2 CONC llage of Penn Yan was incorporated in 1833, he became its first president. Wagener is generally credited as the founder of the village Penn Yan, New York.
