2 CONT Emery : Four generations of the descendants of John Emery, Sen , of Newbury, Mass , and Anthony Emery Kittery, Maine by Emery, Rufus,  author; Cleaves, Emery publisher, printer 1889  
2 CONT 3em>vii Ambrose b. probably in Dracut 1736, m. Rebecca Yocum. He was a soldier in the French and Indian War and the Crown Point Expedition was wounded by an arrow. It is said that he participated in the Boston Tea Party. He lived 
2 CONC near Philadelphia; his home was in one of the winter camps of General Washington's army and his wife cooked the soldiers; rations
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. Rufus Emery, Genealogical Records of Descendants of John and Anthony Emery of Newbury, Mass. 1590 - 1890, The (1890, Salem Publishing and Printing Co. The Salem Press, 1891), pg. 27.
2 CONT 3em>203 Ambrose Emery son of James and Ruth (Watson) Emery
2 CONT 3em>married Mrs. Catherine Foster of Pelham, N.H.He entered the intention of marriage with the town  clerk of Dacut July 17, 1762
2 CONT 3em>He was a farmer and lived in Dracut
2 CONT 3em>He married for his second wife Rebecca Yocum of Pennsylvania. She was born in 1746
2 CONT 3em>They lived at Philadelphia and Thompsontown, Pa, and also in Mifflin co., and Greene Co. Pa.
2 CONT 3em>He was a soldier in the British service in the French and Indiana Way, and was mustered into service Oct. 11, 1756 in Capt. Jonathan Butterfield's company.
2 CONT 3em>He was in the Crown Point expedition and was reported on one of the muster-rolls of his company as "killed or taken" This was a mistake, but he was wounded by an arrow.
2 CONT 3em>He was in the Boston "Tea Party".
2 CONT 3em>His home was within hearing distance  of the battle of Brandywine and in one of the winter camps of Genera; Washington's army and his wife Rebecca cooked the soldiers' rations. 
2 CONT 3em>He died near Jefferson, Greene Co. Pa. in 1824. She died there in 1843 
2 CONT
2 CONT The interesting fact of his life is stated in the emery book of 1890 - 'He was in the Boston Tea party  (1773)  - Did he go all they way back to Boston just to join in the fun? as by this time he was a resident of Philadelphia, Pa
2 CONC .! 
2 CONT
