2 CONT John Emrie's Will
2 CONT 3em>I John Emrie of the town of Hillsborogh, County of Highland Ohio, do make and publish this my last will and testament.
2 CONT 3em>1st I do here b y give and devise to my daughter Mary Ann the annual rents of my lot in the town of Hillsborough known ny lot number sixty-five (65) for her support during her lifetime. At her decease it is my will that the sa
2 CONC id lot be sold and the avails there of to be equally divided amongst my four granddaughters viz: Margaret Ellen Chaney, Mary  Louiza Emrie daughter of J. Ambrose Emrie, Lydia Jane Emerie daughter of James Emrie & Sarah Lavinia Emr
2 CONC ie daughter of Jonas R. Emerie.
2 CONT 3em>It is also my will & thereby give & bequeath to my said daughter Mary Ann all my personal property consisting of household & kitchen furniture such as beds, bedding, chairs, tables, hereaus, cupboards, & cupboard ware includin
2 CONC g all kitchen furniture and cooking utensils for her own use and support while she shall live.
2 CONT 3em>2nd It is also my will and desire that at my deceased or as soon thereafter as a fair price can be obtained thereof my lot in Hillsborough known b y number eighty-three (83) shall be sold and the avails of said sale to be equa
2 CONC lly divided among my sons as follows viz: Jams St. Clair Emrie, J. Ambrose  Emrie, Jonas R. Emerie & my son-in-law Benjamin Chaney.
2 CONT 3em>3rd it is my will that all my just debts be paid out of my estate including physicians bills if any & funeral expenses.
2 CONT 3em>4th It is my will and desire and I here by constitute and appoint my son-in-law Benjamin Chaney executor of this my last will and testament and as there are some debts owing to me by note as will be seen among my papers my exe
2 CONC cutory is authored at his discretion to collect the same if sh shall be of opinion that any of the can be collected by suit & the amount to be appropriated too the remainder to go to the use and support of my daughter Mary Ann.
2 CONT 3em>In testimony where of I have here unto set my hand and seal this 13th day of March in theyear 1847 '
2 CONT 3em>John Emerie 
2 CONT 3em>Signed sealed and acknowledge by the said John Emerie as his last will and testament in our presence and signed  by us in his presence and at is request William Keys John P Ellis
2 CONT 3em>The State of Ohio Highland County SS Highland Probate Court Sept 17th 1856
2 CONT 3em>This day the last will and testament of John Emrie late of Highland County Ohio deceased was produced in open court, whereupon came personally William Keys and John P. Ellis subscribing witnesses thereto. WHO being first duly 
2 CONC sworn depose and say that said John Emrie after the time of executing and publishing said last will and testament(which is attached) was over the age of twenty-one years of sound mind and memory and not under any restraint that he
2 CONC  voluntarily subscribed said last will and testament and in their presence and having published and declared the same to be his last will and testament and that they in his prosect and at his request signed to same as subscribing 
2 CONC witnesses thereto and in the presence of each other.
2 CONT 3em>William Keys John P. Ellis
2 CONT 3em>Sworn to and subscribe in open court this 17th day of December 1856 A. G. Matthews Probate Judge
2 CONT
