2 CONT
2 CONT Ambrose Emery Jr. 
2 CONT Birth 13 Nov 1790 Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT Death 8 Jul 1873 (aged 82) Greene County, Indiana, USA
2 CONT Burial Taylor Ridge Cemetery Scotland, Greene County, Indiana, USA
2 CONT Memorial ID 8161532 · View Source
2 CONT Note: on FInd a grave there is a note left that  "Ambrose has no marker but researchers Sandra Taylor & Mildred Uland believe he is buried here. He is s/o Ambrose and Rebecca. The New Salem Christian Church was once here"  Just wh
2 CONC en a marker was installed and by whom is unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S., Family History Books 
2 CONT Name Ambrose
2 CONT Birth Date 23 Nov 1790
2 CONT Birth Place Philadelphia
2 CONT Father Ambrose Emery
2 CONT Mother Rebecca Yocum
2 CONT Title Genealogical Records of Descendants of John and Anthony Emery, of Newbury, Mass., 1590-1890
2 CONT Author Emery, Rufus, 1827-
2 CONT
2 CONT  Biographical Memiors of Greene County, Indiana; 3 Vols., 1908 B. F. Bowen & Co. Indianapolis, In., VOl. 1 pg. 388-90. 
2 CONT CHARLES ANDERSON EMERY 
2 CONT 3em>Charles Anderson Emery Biography: Charles A. Emery was born in Coshocton county, Ohio, March 14, 1839, March 14, 1839, and is the son of THOMAS B. HAYS and an adopted son of AMBROSE EMERY, of Coshocton county
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT 3em>Ambrose Emery married Polly Anderson both natives of Pennsylvania, but they spent most of their lives in Ohio and raised a large family. 
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT 3em>They moved to Greene County Indiana, in 1848, and located in Taylor township. He got three hundred and sixty acres of virgin land which he cleared, and spoon made a splendid home.. He was always a farmer but became widely know
2 CONC n and was highly respected. Both he and his wife died in Taylor township...."
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. Rufus Emery, Genealogical Records of Descendants of John and Anthony Emery of Newbury, Mass. 1590 - 1890, The (1890, Salem Publishing and Printing Co. The Salem Press, 1891), 
2 CONT 3em>pg. 52. "son of Ambrose and his second wife Rebecca (Yocum) Emery; married Mary Anderson sister of Sarah, who married Samuel Emery, 1812, in Greene co., Pa. They removed to Coshocton co., O. and next to Greene co., Ind., in 18
2 CONC 48. He was a farmer and died near Scotland, Ind., July 8, 1878. His wife died March 21, 1870. Children listed: John, Sarah, Elizabeth, Richard A., Rebecca, Ambrose Jr., William S., Mary Ann, Clementine, Nathaniel, Jonas and Jesse.
2 CONC "
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Elaine Burns, Revised Genealogical Records of Descendants of John Emery of Newbury, Massachuetts,The (1982, Gateway Press Inc. Baltimore, Md.), pg. 91.
2 CONT 1511 AMMBROSE EMERY m. MARY ANDERSON b. 5 Mar. 1790 Fayette co., Pa. d. 21 Mar. 1879 d/o Richard and Mary Anderson. They moved to Coshocton co., Oh. and next to Greene co., In. in 1848. He was a farmer and d. near Scotland, Greene
2 CONC , In. 8 Jul. 1873. Both are buried Taylor Ridge Cemetery Taylor twp., Greene co., In.
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT 5055 JOHN EMERY b. 22 Dec. 1812 Greene co., Pa.
2 CONT 5056 SARAH E. EMERY b. 24 Dec. 1814; teacher; res. near Scotland, Greene, In.; d. unm. 22 Jan. 1894 bur. Simpson Chapel Cemetery Taylor Twp., Greene co., In.
2 CONT 5057 ELIZABETH EMERY b. 12 Nov. 1816; d. unm. 30 Apr. 1843 Coshocton co., Oh.
2 CONT 5058 RICHARD A. EMERY b. 29 Mar. 1818; d. 25 Dec. 1827 Greene co., Pa.
2 CONT 5059 REBECCA EMERY b. 16 Sep. 1820 Pa.
2 CONT 5060 AMBROSE EMERY JR. b. 17 Aug. 1822 Pa.
2 CONT 5061 WILLIAM SPENCER EMERY b. 17 Aug. 1824 *5062 MARY ANN EMERY b. [28] 29 Jul. [28 Sep.] 1829 [1826] near Uniontown, Fayette, Pa.
2 CONT 5063 CLEMENTINE/CLEMMY EMERY b. 8 Feb. 1830 Pa.
2 CONT 5064 NATHANIEL EMERY b. 2 Apr. 1831 Coshocton co., Oh.
2 CONT 5065 JONAS EMERY b. 4 Sep. 1834 Oh.; d. in field hospital on the field at Battle of Antieham 27 Sep. 1862. He was wounded during the Bloody Lane received a mortal wound. Enlisted Apr. 1861 as Pvt. in Co. D. 14th Reg. In. Inf.; mus
2 CONC tered unto service 7 Jun. 1861 was in theBattle of Cheat Mountain, Gree Brier, Haniey Rock, Bloomery Furnace, Winchester, Ft. Royal, Harrison's Landing and Antietam; teacher; unm.; buried grave no.3470 In. section Antieham Nationa
2 CONC l Cemetery.
