2 CONT Coshocton Will Records, Vol D-E, 1837-1861  pg 458-60
2 CONT Will of Nathaniel Emery deceased
2 CONT Nathaniel Emery decd Will & Probate
2 CONT 3em>The state of Ohio Coshocton county ss Court of common pleas March Term towit on the 2d day of April A.D. 1846
2 CONT 3em>Be it remembered that on the day & year aforesaid the last will & testament of Nathaniel Emery late of Coshocton County dec. was this day produced in writing and Daniel Forker & William Dunlap credible witnesses thereunto bein
2 CONC g in open court duly sown and severally examined and whose testimony was taken in writing and it apearing to the court from the said testimony of said witnesses that the said last will & Testament was duly executed that the testat
2 CONC or at the time of executing the same was of ull age of sound mind and memory and not under any restraint. It is by the court that said last will and testament together with the proof be recorded by the clerk of this court.
2 CONT 3em>Which said last will & testament is in the words & figuring following towit -
2 CONT 3em>I Nathaniel Emery of the county of Coshocton & state of Ohio do make &publish this my last will & testament in the manner and form following that is to say.
2 CONT 3em>First It is my will that all my just debts and funeral expenses and last sickness shall be paid - 
2 CONT 3em>Second I give & devise to my beloved wife Elizabeth Emery all the home farm on which we now live in Pike township in the county of Coshocton & state of Ohio all the stock, farming interest household goods & Kitchen   furniture
2 CONC  during her natural life also the eight acres bought of James Arnold
2 CONT 3em>3rd I give & devise to John Horner the lea_e that now lives with me all the home farm on which we now live on in Pike farm on which we now live on in Pike township in the county of Coshocton & state of Ohio after my wife death
2 CONC  and all my goods & chattels, money, notes and accounts that will be left at my wife death and the eight of lan bought of James Arnold - 
2 CONT 3em>4th It is my will that my sister Rebecca Emery shall have the privileged of a home with my wife & John Horner so long as she shall live -
2 CONT 3em>In witness where of I have set my hand and seal this 11th day of February A. D. 1846 Nathaniel Emery (seal)
2 CONT 3em>Signed sealed published & declared by the said Nathaniel Emery in out presents to be his last will & Testament Daniel Forker William
2 CONT 3em>Proof of WIll
2 CONT 3em>The State of Ohio Coshocton County SS Be it remembered that on this 6th day of April A.D. 1846 personally appeared in open court Daniel Forker and William Dunlap who being duly sworn according to law depose & say that they are
2 CONC  the subscribing witnesses to the last will and testament of Nathaniel Emery of Coshocton county Ohio deceased that said Nathaniel Emery was of full age of sound mind and memory and not under any restraint within th knowledge of t
2 CONC hese respondents that the saw the testator subscribe the said will and that they attested and subscribed the same in his presence and at his request. Daniel Forker and William Dunlap 
2 CONT 3em>Sown to & subscribed in open court
2 CONT
