1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''MIX UP Lancaster Mennonite Vital Statistics has this Jacob and Ann mixed up with this Jacob'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/143775115/jacob_clemens
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/208278788/jacob-clemens
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Jacob Clemens
2 CONT Marriage Date	14 Sep 1771
2 CONT Marriage Place	Pennsylvania
2 CONT Spouse's Name	Ann Updegraff
2 CONT Skippack Deaths No. 205: "Jacob Clemens died January 17, 1823." However, the information published in the Montgomery County Historical Society Bulletin about this Jacob is not correct, due to mixing up two different Jacob/Ann Clem
2 CONC ens couples.
2 CONT
2 CONT The only Jacob Clemens with an estate filed in Montgomery County is Jacob of Worcester Twp., who died before November 1822 when his wife Ann was appointed administrator. This Jacob cannot be the same person as the Jacob who is not
2 CONC ed in Skippack Deaths to have died January 17, 1823. The Skippack Deaths records in date order and David Hess & wife and Andreas Waldt (nos. 203 and 204) are noted to have died earlier in January 1823. Further, in Methacton Cemete
2 CONC ry in Worcester Twp. is buried Jacob Clemens 1761-1822, which is clearly the Jacob who died in Worcester Twp. before November 1822 and not in January 1823.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many Clemens family records mix up these two Jacob/Ann couples, and misplace the Jacob who died in 1823.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerhart Clemens had three sons: Jacob, Abraham and John, all of whom had sons Jacob. Abraham's son Jacob is widely acknowledged to be Jacob 1756-1816 who moved to Chester Co. The Jacob who married Ann Updegrave is often reported t
2 CONC o the be son of John but that is not correct. John died in Buckingham Twp., Bucks Co. in February 1782. A Jacob Clemens died in Plumstead Twp. (neighboring Buckingham Twp.) also in Febuary 1782. This Jacob was the son of John. His
2 CONC  wife was Susanna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Therefore, this leaves Gerhart's son Jacob. That Jacob is document to have had sons Jacob born in 1739 and 1749. The 1739 Jacob probably died young. The Jacob who died in January 1823 is undoubtedly the son of Jacob & Barbara (Cle
2 CONC mmer) who was born in 1749.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Book "Pennsylvania Marriages Prior to 1790" notes that a marriage license was issued on 9/14/1771 for Jacob Clemens and Ann Updegraff. Ann was the daughter of Edward & Ann Updegrave and Edward's will written in 1775 confirms t
2 CONC hat his daughter Ann was married (i.e. prior to 1775) to Jacob Clemens.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Jacob who died in 1823 is the son of Jacob & Barbara (Clemmer) Clemens, born in 1749. Some researchers have documented that Methacton Jacob born 1761 was the husband of Ann Updegrave but that's not possible because he would ha
2 CONC ve been only 10 years old in 1771. So clearly, the husband of Ann Updegrave was the Jacob born 1749, son of Jacob & Barbara (Clemmer) Clemens and he must be the Jacob Clemens who died in January 1823.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1790 census shows two Jacob's living in central Montgomery County - one in Worcester and one in Skippack. The one in Worcester is undoubtedly Methacton Jacob. The 1790 census shows Methacton Jacob with two sons under 16 which 
2 CONC fits with his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1790 census enumerates Skippack Jacob near Henry Updegrave and Joseph Updegrave. Henry was a cousin to Ann Updegrave and Joseph was her brother. So this must be the family of Jacob & Ann (Updegrave) Clemens. The 1790 census sh
2 CONC ow them with one son over 16 and two sons under 16. This fits for a couple married in 1771. However, the identities of the three sons of Jacob & Ann (Updegrave) are unknown. This couple is not the parents of John Clemens (1787-185
2 CONC 6) and his siblings. John and his siblings were children of Methacton Jacob.
2 CONT
2 CONT Skippack Jacob's burial place is unmarked but he is probably buried with his wife's family at Lower Skippack. Several of Jacob's sisters are also buried at Lower Skippack.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''MIX UP''' Lancaster Mennonite Vital Statistics has this Jacob and Ann mixed up with this Jacob=
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/208278788/jacob-clemens
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob died before November 1822 when his wife Ann was appointed administratrix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many researchers have confused this Jacob and his wife Ann with the Jacob Clemens who died in January 1823 and married Ann Updegrave.  Jacob and Ann Updegrave were married in 1771.  The Jacob/Ann couple buried at Methacton Mennoni
2 CONC te are too young to have been married in 1771.  So this is a different Jacob/Ann couple.  Researchers have also assumed that Jacob/Ann (Updegrave) were the parents of John Clemens (1787-1856) and his siblings but this Jacob/Ann co
2 CONC uple were the parents of those children.
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems likely that this Jacob is part of the Gerhart Clemens family but it's not clear where he fits.  Gerhart's three sons are known to have had sons Jacob born earlier than 1761.  So this Jacob would have to be a son of one of
2 CONC  Gerhart's grandsons, but they are generally too young to have a son born in 1761 or had known sons Jacob with different birth years.  So it's a mystery who this Jacob's parents are.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memoria
2 CONC l/143775115/jacob-clemens Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 7 2022, 0:22:15 UTC''
