2 CONT
2 CONT BIO: "Of the many Dutch Non-conformist families coming to America during the colonial times, the Tysons were of the earliest and most prominent. We find that one Reynier Tyson with twelve other men and families, a company comprisi
2 CONC ng thirty-three persons, came across the sea and settled at Germantown, Pennsylvania, in 1692, if not earlier..we find that in 1703 one by the name of Cornelius Tyson came from Crefeld, Germany, and settled at Germantown, Pennsylv
2 CONC ania.  This Tyson died May 9th, 1716, and his body was interred in Axe's Graveyard, Germantown.  All of the Tysons in Pennsylvania are descendants of these two named Tysons."quote from Eby book page 351.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/28078440/cornelius-doors-tiesen Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 7 2019, 9:25:23 UTC''
