1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   Merken/ Maria Theissen by BEcker and others. b c 1659 d 1742
2 CONT
2 CONT   Mary Tyson.
2 CONT
2 CONT       White has "?married Jochim Huiskens", she wasn't sure?
2 CONT
2 CONT       She cites an entry in 1675 in the Reformed Church in Kaldenkirchen
2 CONT
2 CONT       of the baptism of "the little daughter of Jochim Huiskens
2 CONT
2 CONT       and Maria Doors w witnesses Thonis Huiskens and Nys Doors.  (Niess?)
2 CONT
2 CONT       HOwever, no marriage record for this couple.  White has "Maria
2 CONT
2 CONT       did marry Jan Lykens around 1683 at the time of their leaving
2 CONT
2 CONT       Germany to come to Germantown" (White, 1683)
2 CONT
2 CONT       Many think she is the wife of Jan Luckens/  Luykens / Lukens 
2 CONT
2 CONT       who came to America.(Custer) (Krefeld Immigr) Jochim Huiskens/
2 CONT
2 CONT       Johann Lucken of Dahlen or Wickerath (:WHite, who thinks they
2 CONT
2 CONT       m around 1683)
2 CONT
2 CONT       But though American writers state that Jan Luckens' wife was Maria 
2 CONT
2 CONT       Theissen, a sister to Reiner, (?)he found no indication that Jan m
2 CONT
2 CONT       more than once.  He noted that Niepoth said Jan Luckens m Merken/ Maria 
2 CONT
2 CONT       Gastes.  Gudo Gotthoff wrote that Jan Luckns m lst Merken Gastes but
2 CONT
2 CONT       that he left her in Germanyu, just as Wilhelm Strepers had left his
2 CONT
2 CONT       wife, and shortly after coming to America he m Maria Theissen.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Jack Bowman, who is of this line, says "Earliest records say that
2 CONT
2 CONT       he married Marie Thiessen, sister to Reynier Thiessen...Many of
2 CONT
2 CONT       the documents refer to Jan's wife as Mary, but there are no
2 CONT
2 CONT       records of their marriage.  Niepoth... concludes that his wife
2 CONT
2 CONT       was Mercken Gastes.  This comes from a written document dated
2 CONT
2 CONT       6/15/1683, which was drwon up by the Lucken siblings in Krefeld."
2 CONT
2 CONT       "In 1995 a 'conclave' of Lukens researchers got together to decide
2 CONT
2 CONT       on their interpretation of all documents relating to Jans wife's
2 CONT
2 CONT       name.  They concluded that she had to be Marie Tyson.  Niepoth
2 CONT
2 CONT       may be correct if Jan was married bef leaving Krefeld and his 
2 CONT
2 CONT       wife died.  But they could not find any documentation for the
2 CONT
2 CONT       Gastes name.  "
2 CONT
2 CONT       Niepoth says that Maria or Mercken is not mentioned among the sisters 
2 CONT
2 CONT       of Reiner Theissen. He also presents evidence on who Johann Lucken
2 CONT
2 CONT       did marry.  Bans published on 12 Sep 1679 in REformed Church in
2 CONT
2 CONT       Crefeld for "JOhann Simes of Gladbach and Merken Wilhelms of 
2 CONT
2 CONT       Gladbach".  A Rheydt power of attorney in  1683 says Merken Lucken
2 CONT
2 CONT       is daughter of married couple Wilhelm Lucken and Adelheid, and
2 CONT
2 CONT       her name appears in the Quaker wedding as Merken Willems.  So she
2 CONT
2 CONT       definitely was not the daughter of Theiss Doors!  Nieboth also 
2 CONT
2 CONT       mentions that Wilhelm was related on his motgher's side to the
2 CONT
2 CONT       Ther Mehr family.  
2 CONT
2 CONT       Jan Lykens was b in 1650/1, son of Wilhelm and Adelheid Lucken, and 
2 CONT
2 CONT       grew up in Gladbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT       Luykens was one of the pioneer settlers of GErmantown in 1683.  He
2 CONT
2 CONT       was constable of the town 1691-5, sheriff 1694-5, d. 1744.  Brought
2 CONT
2 CONT       a Dutch Bible from Krefeld, one of his descendants still owns it.
2 CONT
2 CONT       His will dated 9th of 8th mo 1741 in Philadelphia's registry
2 CONT
2 CONT       of wills, his property includes the trappings of a linen weaving
2 CONT
2 CONT       profession and some books, a house and lot in Germantown, and
2 CONT
2 CONT       two hundred acres of land joining Spipenk. 
2 CONT
