2 CONT [https://familypedia.fandom.com/wiki/Anna_op_den_Graeff_van_de_Aldekerk https://familypedia.fandom.com/wiki/Anna_op_den_Graeff_van_de_Aldekerk]
2 CONT '''Anna op den Graeff van de Aldekerk''' (also Anna van de Aldekerk) (* 1557 in Aldekerk; † 1613 ibid), is a member of the originally Cleves family Op den Graeff. The morganatic descent and relationship to the De La Mark (Von der 
2 CONC Mark), Dukes of Cleves, claimed by their descendants, is not historically proven.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Anna's alleged father Herman op den Graeff, called van de Aldekerk (detail from a painting by Matthias Laurenz Gräff, 2007)
2 CONT Anna's alleged mother, Princess Amalia of Cleves; according to obscure sources, morganatically married to Herman op den Graeff van de Aldekerk (* 1520); (Detail from a painting by Matthias Laurenz Gräff, 2007)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna's life dates are based on a family tradition that cannot be proven genealogically. Herman op den Graeff van de Aldekerk is given as Anna's father. Nothing is known about her mother; unreliable sources give her as Amalia, Prin
2 CONC cess of Cleves, sister of the english queen Anna of Cleves. Anna op den Graeff van de Aldekerk was a nun in the Woestenraedt monastery (also Aldekerk Kloster West), who, according to dubious sources, had a liaison with Johan Wilhe
2 CONC lm, Duke of Jülich-Kleve-Berg. It is said: He possibly had a son, Herman op den Graeff (b. 26 November 1585) from an unproven morganatic marriage with Anna op den Graeff van de Aldekerk (b. 1565, m. 1585, d. 1616). According to th
2 CONC is and various other statements, Anna had two sons who took over their mother's family name, and allegedly founded the female line of the Op den Graeff.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna of Cleves and her nephew Johan Wilhelm of Cleves. According to obscure family sources, Anna of Cleves was Anna's aunt and Johan Wilhelm of Cleves was the father of Anna's two sons (detail from a painting by Matthias Laurenz G
2 CONC räff, 2007)
2 CONT Abraham op den Graeff (* 1583), unknown if he has descendants
2 CONT Herman op den Graeff (1585-1642), mennonite "Herren-Bischof von Krefeld" (lord bishop of Krefeld)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was buried in her Aldekerk monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT Krefeld Immigrants and Their Descendants, Bände 7-12, S. 15ff und 53ff, Links Genealogy Publications, 1990
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna, Duchess of Cleves: The King's 'Beloved Sister', von Heather R. Darsie (2019)
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogie Amalia von Kleve
2 CONT
2 CONT Gelre and Kleve See under Duke William of Gelre (House van Kleve)- children
2 CONT
2 CONT "Anna, Duchess of Cleves: The King's 'Beloved Sister'", von Heather R. Darsie, 2019
2 CONT
2 CONT Krefeld Immigrants and Their Descendants, Bände 7-12, S. 53, Links Genealogy Publications, 1990.. Hence, Herman op den Graff (Lord - Man of the Count) is the morganatic or natural son (excluded from the feudal succession) of John 
2 CONC William de la Marck van Altena of Cleves (1562-1609)..
2 CONT
