2 CONT Jan John Crey, also spelled Crey, Kray, etc was born in Kriegsheim in the German Palatinate and a Mennonite. He emigrated to Philadelphia in 1702 and was one of the original settlers of Skippack PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wives were Helena Winnertzkamp by whom he had 4 children, Magdalena Haldeman  (a known Swiss Mennonite family), and Sytge Van Bebber Op Den Graeff (also Updegrave) by whom he also had 4 children.* Reference: [https://www.finda
2 CONC grave.com/memorial/114362277/jan-john-krey Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 11 2021, 0:40:15 UTC''
