1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/45427410/deborah-oberholtzer
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth date is an about date. She married Jacob Oberholtzer son of Jacob the pioneer about 1735 in Salford, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania. The Oberholtzer Family genealogy incorrect states that this Deborah was Deborah Haldem
2 CONC an and that Deborah Krey married Jacob Oberholtzer Sr. However, there were no Deborah's in the Haldeman family. Jacob Jr.'s will notes that his brother-in-law was Christian Haldeman so some researchers have assumed that Deborah wa
2 CONC s his sister. But Christian married Catharine Krey, sister of Deborah Krey, which is how he was a brother-in-law to Jacob Oberholtzer Jr. Deborah Krey was not married to Jacob Sr.
2 CONT =====
2 CONT Lancaster Mennonite vital Records Deborah opdenGraeff Krey Married Jacob Oberholtzer FAG#77881526 the pioneer who came from Switzerland in 1709 and married Deborah opdenGraeff Krey daughter of John and Susan (Sytche) opden Graeff 
2 CONC Krey in 1710.
2 CONT
