1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/74764916/henry-cassel
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry was the son of Huppert and Syche op den Graeff Cassel. He married Margrit Custer Godshall about 1745. Henry and Margrit had three children: Eva, Yelles and Susanna. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrit was the daughter of Godshalk Hermans Godhsalk and Eva Kuster. It is unknown were Margrit is buried. ........................................ His property was damaged during the Rev. War. A document regarding the damage rea
2 CONC ds as follows: Estimate of damage on the plantation of Henry Cassel, by the army under the command of His Excellency, General Washington, between the 7th and 16th inst. 696 Fence Rails, @ 25c a piece . . . . . . 8pounds.14s. We, w
2 CONC hose names are undersigned, at the request and desire of Henry Cassel, have taken a strict and careful survey of the damage done to his plantation, and to the best of our knowledge and judgment believe the same to amout to eight p
2 CONC ounds and fourteen shillings, current Pennsylvania money of Pennsylvania, and we are ready to qualify unto when called upon. Given under our hands on said plantation in Towamensing township this 23d October, 1777. Fred Wampole, Ni
2 CONC cholas Schwenk, John Lukens.
2 CONT
2 CONT The above referenced document was in the hands of Henry Cassel's great-grandson, Jacob H. Cassel, in 1896. ........................................ Henry CASSEL- 1797 Will (Will written 17 May 1797, proven 14 Aug 1797) In the Name
2 CONC  of God, Amen I Henry CASSEL of Towamensin Township In the County of Montgomery and State of Pennsylvania Being Advanced in Age But of Sound Mind Understatnding & Memory Thanks be to God do Make & ordain this my Last Will and Test
2 CONC ament In Manner following. First I will that all my Just Debts and funeral Charges be Duly Satisfied & paid by my Executor out of my Personal Estate, Item It is my Will and I give to my Beloved Wife '''Margaret''' our Bed & Bedste
2 CONC ad all Belonging thereto My Pipe stove, thiry hour Clock, One Cow, her Choice, and as Much other Households goods as She Chuseth, and fifty Pound In Money to be paid to her In three Months after my Desease. I also give unto her Tw
2 CONC o Rooms the Northwest End off the House Where we Now Live and the Two upper Rooms, and Priiviledge at the fire place and in the Seller for her use With Sufficient Egress & Regress, and fire wood Ready Cut and Brought to the Door, 
2 CONC fit for the pipe stove as much as She Chuseth, one quarter of the garden and Dung Brought in as much as She Chuseth, and fruit of the Orchard as Much as She has need of. And Fifteen Pound yearly and every year The First Payment to
2 CONC  Commence in one year after my Decease. And my '''son Yellis''' or his Successors is to keep her Cow Summer and Winter as he Keeps his own. All this above Mentioned she is to have as Long as she Remains My Widow. Item I give unto 
2 CONC My son Yellis my Waggon, Plough, Harrow Horge geers, the Weaver Loom With all the Tackling Belonging thereunto. And Whereas I Hold One Hundred & thirty one acres of Land Sittuated in Towamensin Township. Item I give the Aforesaid 
2 CONC One Hundred and thirty one acres of Land With the apurtenances thereunto Belonging to my son Yellis CASSEL his heirs and Assigns for ever and he the said Yellis CASSEL is to pay & allow all the above Mentioned Articles to his Moth
2 CONC er, and I do Estimate and Value the aforesaid Plantation to my son Yellis at Seven Hundred Pounds in Specia, out of Which I give unto him One Hundred Pounds first and foremost Instead of What I have Given to my '''Two Daughters Ev
2 CONC e and Susanna''' in Households and Money, and the Remainder what is unpaid he is to pay As followeth Seventy five Pounds in one year after My and My Wifes Decease and so yearly and every year still _____ is paid, he having his Equ
2 CONC al Share in Each payment. Item I give all my Personal Estate What is not already Willed to my three Children Named Yellis, '''Eve wife of John SPRINGER''' '''Susanna wife of George TRUMBOR''', Share and share alike and after My wi
2 CONC fes Decease, My son Yellis is to have the Thiry hour Clock, the pipe stove and the Large Bible first and foremost, the Remainder is to be Divided among my three Children as Aforesaid. Item it is my will and I order that my son Yel
2 CONC lis is to Get any Necessarys my wife is in Need of Such as going to Mill & Stores or Elsewhare, But he is not to have no Pay for his Trouble, And Lastly I Constitude and appoint My son Yellis CASSEL to be My Executor of this my La
2 CONC st Will & Testament, Disannulling all other Wills and Confirming this and no other to be my Last will and Testament. In Witness Whereof I the said Henry CASSEL have hereunto set my Hand and seal Dated the Seventeenth Day of May In
2 CONC  the year of our Lord One thousand Seven Hundred and Ninety Seven 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry CASSEL
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed and Delivered by the said Henry CASSEL as his Last Will & Testament Before us the Subscribers Jacob KOLB Jacob KULP Junr
2 CONT
