2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT '''Johannes Kuster''' was born 10 Dec 1670 in Kaldenkirchen, Germany, to parents [[Kuster-3 | Paulus Kuster]] and [[Doors-3 | Gertrude DoorsKuster]].  <ref name="White">  White, Jean M. - editor; "The '''Descendants of Paulus and 
2 CONC Gertrude Kusters''' of Kaldenkirchen, Germany andGermantown, Pennsylvania the first four generations"; Castor Association Of America, 1991;  303 Pages, Indexed.  pages 18, 23-27.  </ref> <ref name="Pound and Kester"> Hunt, John E.
2 CONC , Compiled by; [[Space:Pound_and_Kester_Families |  '''"Pound and Kester Families"''']]; Regan Printing House, 1904; 628 pages, Indexed; Pages 3-6 and Part I, The Kester Ancestry, pages 301-305.  </ref>  <ref name="F.A.G.">  {{Fin
2 CONC dAGrave|116676971}}, this memorial is by Bonnie & Clyde DeWeese, it has "Johannes 'Custer' Kuster", with birth: " Oct 12, 1670 Germany" and death: "Aug 6, 1740 Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania".  </ref>  Johannes was baptized at 
2 CONC the Reformed Church, Kaldenkirchen, Germany on 12 Dec 1670. <ref name="White"/>  <ref name="Delphine"> Delphine, Dominique Z.,  "Cable-Bucher-Hawbaker-Ulery-Kester-Priest-Stafford-Scanland-Price-Hapner"; Ancestry, Ancestry Family 
2 CONC Trees, Ancestry.com, The Generations Network, Inc., 2006-2016, Provo, Utah, USA;  The information from Ancestry Family Trees has been submitted by Ancestry members (Dominique Delphine), the information may have come from one or mo
2 CONC re Family Trees submitted by other Ancestry members, all of these members may have edited or deleted information since this source was used.  </ref> 
2 CONT "Johannes was the second son and second child of Paulus and Gertrude Kusters.  He was baptized at the Reformed Church, Kaldenkirchen, Germany on 12 December 1670.  Johannes came to America about 1684, <ref> "U.S. and Canada, Passe
2 CONC nger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s";  Page 45, "Arrival 1683 in Germantown, Pennsylvania"; Ancestry.com,  TheGenerations Network, Inc., Provo, Utah, USA 2006; [http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?db=pili354&h=102
2 CONC 4804&indiv=try]  </ref>ahead of his parents and siblings.  His is listed on the first tax list of Philadelphia County in 1693 as living in Bristol Township (now inBucks County).  Johannes name is also on the 1691 petition for natu
2 CONC ralization."  <ref name="White"/> Johannes married [[Cassel-275 | Elizabeth Cassel]] on 31 Aug 1692 in the Abington Meeting of Friends.  <ref name="White"/> <ref name="Poundand Kester"/>   <ref name="Delphine"/>  "Johannes married
2 CONC  Elizabeth Cassell on 31 August 1692 at the Abington Meeting of Friends. <ref name="Pound and Kester"/> Johannes lived in Germantown and in Bristol Township.  Johannes Koester and Elizabeth Koester were witnesses to a Marriage Cer
2 CONC tificate the 2nd month 14th day 1694.  Johannes Koster brought suit and recovered from Johannes Pettinger three shillings for an assault which was filed in court, at Germantown, 11th month, 19th day 1694."   <ref name="White"/> <r
2 CONC ef> "Philadelphia Yearly Meeting Minutes, 1682-1746"; Collection from: Swarthmore College, Swarthmore, Pennsylvania, United States; Call Number: MR-Ph 4 </ref>  "In 1694, 1695 and 1696 Johannes was elected Constable of Germantown.
2 CONC  He was elected a Committeeman in 1698 and 1699.  In 1701 he again waselected Constable.  In 1704 he appears as a committeeman and in 1705 he was elected a committeeman, Constable and a Road Viewer.  Johannes became a Burgess in 1
2 CONC 706 and the following year there was a complaint the he had married a couple outside the Germantown corporate limits." <ref name="White"/> "Johannes made a gift of three pounds to German Friends in need the 10th month, 25th day, 1
2 CONC 699.  He died sometime during the summer or fall of 1708 since the Philadelphia Administrations, Book B, page 70, showsthat 23 October 1708 "Elizabeth Custers", a widow of Germantown, withArnold Cassell of Philadelphia County, and
2 CONC  Thomas and Peter Shoemakerof Germantown as bondsmen on a bond for two hundred pounds, was appointed administratrix of the estate of "Johannes Custers""..."On 3 August 1709, "Johannes Kosters" son and heir, and "Elizabeth relict" 
2 CONC of "Johannes Kusters dededent" of Philadelphia County, conveyed by deed to Daniel Falkner, land in Springfield, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania.Johannes and Elizabeth had at least six children:"  <ref name="White"/> Johannes pas
2 CONC sed away 1708, in Germantown, Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania. <ref name="White"/> <ref name="Pound and Kester"/> <ref name="F.A.G."/>   <ref name="Delphine"/>   
2 CONT
