1 NOTE (Research):!AHNENTAFEL NO 960
2 CONT
2 CONT !<1>ANCESTRAL FILE NO. X3DJ-49 and 4452-8K
2 CONT
2 CONT !<2>BIRTH-PARENTS-SPOUSE-CHILDREN: Jean M. White, editor, THE DESCENDANTS OF PAULUS AND GERTRUDE KUSTERS; 1542-1819; The Castor Association of America, Richmond, TX, 1991; pp 139-140.
2 CONT "***HERMANUS KESTER, the son of Johannes and Elizabeth (Cassel) Koster, was born 2, 11th month 1703 [Jan 1704]. Abington Monthly Meeting granted Hermanus a certificate to join Buckingham Monthly Meeting 28, 6th month 1732. The 5, 
2 CONC 7th month 1732 he was received at Buckingham MM and granted a certificate to Chesterfield MM in Burlington County, NJ. Hermanus located at Kingwood, Hunterdon Co, NJ before 1733. He married Anne Large in 1733 at the Chesterfield M
2 CONC onthly Meeting. Anne was born 29, 3rd month 1712. Hermanus
2 CONT raised some of Paul Kester's (2.6) small children after Paul died between 1745-1750. These children were William [2.6.1], Rebecca [2.6.2], and John [2.6.3] Kester.
2 CONT A tax list for Kingwood Township in May 1778 shows Hermanus as having 60 acres, 2 horses, 3 cows, 1 pig and being exempt (which probably meant from military duty as Hermanus and his family were Quakers). In January/February 1780 h
2 CONC e was listed as owning 5 pigs."
2 CONT
2 CONT !<3>BIO-CHILDREN: Eleanore C. Custer, HER FAMILY AND CONNECTIONS; 1703-1780; compiled by Agnes W. Storer, Genealogist of The Daughters of Colonial Wars in the State of New Jersey; p 55; Seattle [WA] Public Library [R929.2, C967S].
2 CONT "4. ***HERMANUS KOSTER, or Herman Kister, son of Johannes and Elizabeth Koster of Germantown was born 11 Jan 1703 and married Ann ____.
2 CONT From the Records of the Abington, Philadelphia Monthly Meeting, 28th of 6 mo. 1732, we find that "A certificate was granted to Harman Kuster in order to join himself to Friends of Buckingham Monthly Meeting." The minutes of the Bu
2 CONC ckingham and Wrightstown Monthly Meeting for 7 mo. 5, 1732 show that his certificate from Abington was accepted, and that at the same meeting he requested a certificate to the Chesterfield Monthly Meeting. Buckingham Meeting was i
2 CONC n Bucks County, PA, and Chesterfield Meeting was across the river in Burlington County, NJ. We next find Herman on the records of the Kingwood (or as it was later known Quakertown) Monthly Meeting, in Hunterdon County, NJ. It was 
2 CONC here that ***HERMAN KESTER (the form of spelling this family adopted) permanently settled. His wife, whose surname is unknown, was probably from NJ."
2 CONT
2 CONT !<4>BIRTH-SPOUSE-CHILDREN: James W. Moore, RECORDS OF THE KINGWOOD MONTHLY MEETING OF FRIENDS OF HUNTERDON NJ [Now Quakertown MM], Beginning in 1744; 1703-1755;; Seattle [WA] Public Library [Microcard, 929.2]
2 CONT "Children of ***HARMANUS KESTER, SR., b 2, 11th mo [Jan] 1703 and Ann, his wife, b 29, 3rd mo [May] 1712.
2 CONT [1] Susanna, b 10, 9th mo [Nov] 1733
2 CONT [2] Elisabeth, b 25, 6th mo [Aug] 1735
2 CONT [3] Samuel, b 26, 9th mo [Nov] 1737
2 CONT [4] John b 21, 11th mo [Jan] 1739
2 CONT [5] Rebecca b 16, 2nd mo [Apr] 1742
2 CONT [6] Hermanus b 17, 5th mo [Jul] 1744
2 CONT [7] Peter b 4, 11th mo [Jan] 1746
2 CONT [8] Paul b 26, 3rd mo [May] 1749
2 CONT [9] Thomas b 24, 11th mo [Jan] 1752
2 CONT [10] Margaret b 20, 6th mo [Aug] 1755
2 CONT
2 CONT !<5>PARENTS-SIBLINGS: Marcus L. Miller, "Germantown Residents Naturalized in 1691"; 1691; MENNONITE FAMILY HISTORY, Vol II, No 3, July 1983; pp 102-104; Seattle [WA] Public Library.
2 CONT "Johannes Kusters married Elizabeth Cassel in 1702 and became a Quaker that same year. His two brothers, Arnold and Hermanus, were Mennonites. Johannes' children were John, Margaret, Reiner, ***HERMAN, Arnold, Abigal, Samuel, Doro
2 CONC thy, and Charity. Johannes was the son of Paulas Kuster. In 1702, Johannes moved to the Skippack area and died in the fall of 1708.[f.34]
2 CONT Footnote 34: Samuel W. Pennypacker, SETTLEMENT OF GERMANTOWN, N.Y., Benjamin Blom, 1970 (1899), pp 136, 142."
2 CONT
2 CONT !<6>BIRTH-PARENTS-SIBLINGS(8)-SPOUSE-MARRIAGE-CHILDREN(10)-DEATH: RootsWeb's WorldConnect Project; SWAYNE/WALTON/FRAZEE/SKINNER Origins; Entries: 31343; Contact: Rick Swayne <rswayne@compuserve.com>
2 CONT "Ann Mary Large, _UID: FA592A35C7938C4E8A6CD672E4F921C5E7B3, b 29 May 1713 in Germantown Twp, Philadelphia Co, PA; d Hunterdon Co, NJ, d/o Samuel Large, b 3 Oct 1686 in Amesbury, MA; and Rebecca Willson, b 14 Apr 1677 in Scarborou
2 CONC gh, Yorkshire, England; m Dec 1732/1733, Chesterfield Mtg, NJ to ***HERMANUS KESTER, b 2 Jan 1703 or 22 Jan 1703 in Germantown Twp, Philadelphia Co, PA, d aft 11 May 1780, Hunterdon Co, NJ, s/o Johannes Koster and Elizabeth Cassel
2 CONC l.
2 CONT Children
2 CONT 1. Susanna Kester, b 19 Sep 1733 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 2. Elizabeth Kester, b 25 Jun 1735 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 3. Samuel Kester, b 26 Nov 1737 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 4. John Kester, b 21 Jan 1739 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 5. Rebecca Kester, b 16 Feb 1742 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 6. Hermanus Kester, b 5 Jul 1744 or 17 Jul 1744 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 7. Peter Kester, b 4 Nov 1746 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 8. Paul Kester b 26 Mar 1749 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 9. Thomas Kester, b 24 Nov 1752 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ
2 CONT 10. Margaret Kester, b 10 Aug 1755 in Kingwood (now Quakertown), Hunterdon Co, NJ"
