1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bridget Strauder was born in 1722 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, the only child of her parents. She married Arnold Custer in 1740. They had 11 children in 16 years. She died in 1759 in Pennsylvania, at the age of 3
2 CONC 7
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:LRTJ-GN7 FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 30 2018, 17:10:33 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/G4T7-SDH
2 CONT Brief Life History of Bridget'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Bridget Strauder was born in 1722, in Philadelphia, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, British Colonial America, her father, George Strauder, was 28 and her mother, Susan Jane Clark, was 27. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Arnold Kuster/Custer in 1740, in Augusta, Virginia, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 9 sons and 6 daughters. 
2 CONT John Custer 1739–1780
2 CONT Benjamin M. Custer 1741–1826
2 CONT Conrad Custer 1742–1828
2 CONT George Custer 1745–1850
2 CONT Susannah Custer 1745–
2 CONT Mary Barbara Custer 1747–1815
2 CONT Catherine Custer 1747–1826
2 CONT Thomas Custer 1749–1782
2 CONT Jacob Custer 1750–1833
2 CONT Elizabeth Custer 1751–1818
2 CONT Joseph Custer 1752–1839
2 CONT John A. Caster Sr. 1754–1823 [incorrect entry?]
2 CONT Eve Custer 1756–1821
2 CONT Bridget (Biddy) Dorcas Custer 1756–1815
2 CONT Noah Castor 1758–1829
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in March 1759, in Augusta, Virginia, United States, at the age of 37, and was buried in Custer Family Cemetery, Fulks Run, Rockingham, Virginia, United States.
