2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 JUL 1829
2 ADDR
3 CITY Green
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://generations-past.net/lola/castor-o/p14.htm#i489
2 CONT
2 CONT >Noah Castor was farmer at Ashland County, Ohio. He Politics; Democrate. He was born in 1758 or 1764 at Brock's Gap, Augusta County, Virginia; There is some dispute about his birth date and parents. If computed from his tombstone,
2 CONC  he was born in 1764 and his father was Conrad Castor. There is evidence to support the theory that his father was Arnold Custer and he was raised by his grandfather, Conrad Castor. If that is so then he must have been born in 175
2 CONC 8 because Arnold died in March of 1759.1,2 
2 CONT
2 CONT >He married Rebecca Matheny, daughter of Nathan Matheny, circa 1785 at Monongalia County, Virginia;
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Recently I received a request to show Noah being the son of Arnold rather than the son of Conrad. I reviewed the genealogy information that is available on-line and again concluded it is difficult to really determine the fact. May
2 CONC be DNA testing will provide a definite answer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT However, my review did find various trees describing Arnold as the father of Noah. So, I have decided to honor the edit request and have now changed this memorial to show Noah being the son of Arnold.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy Articles List...
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on census data Noah Castor was born between 1755 and 1765 in Virginia. Haine's History of Hamilton County, Indiana states that Noah was "one of thirty children born to Conrad Castor, who lived at Brock's Gap, Virginia." Howe
2 CONC ver, Noah may have been a son of Arnold, which would make Noah a grandson of Conrad. Noah could have been a ward of Conrad after Arnold died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad Castor [Custer] - https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5582056/conrad-custer
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah married Rebecca Matheny around 1785 in Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime after Noah died, Rebecca went to Hamilton County, Indiana to live with Frederick and Nancy Harger. <br/>
2 CONT She died 22 August 1848 and was buried at the Prairie Baptist Church Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Noah and Rebeccca:
2 CONT # Nathan Castor born 1786 PA
2 CONT # Susan Castor born 16 August 1792 PA
2 CONT # Conrad Castor born 9 December 1789 Beaver County, PA
2 CONT # Uriah Castor born 1790-1800 PA
2 CONT # Sampson Castor born about 1800 PA
2 CONT # Rachel Castor born about 1801 PA
2 CONT # Ruth Castor born 29 November 1806 PA
2 CONT # Nancy Castor born 24 December 1807 Beaver County, PA; married Frederick Harger 18 November 1825 OH; died 20 February 1869 IN.
2 CONT #  Benjamin Castor born 1809 Beaver County, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/45626484/noah-castor Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 16 2020, 7:16:55 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Recent suggested edit:
2 CONT In the Geneanet Community Trees Index it shows Noah was born in 1758, in Brocks Gap, Augusta, Virginia, USA. It also shows his last name as Custer.
2 CONT Contributor: AjR (47767178)
2 CONT
2 CONT Previously, I received a request to show Noah being the son of Arnold rather than the son of Conrad. I reviewed the genealogy information that is available on-line and again concluded it is difficult to really determine the fact. 
2 CONC Maybe DNA testing will provide a definite answer.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, my review did find various trees describing Arnold as the father of Noah. So, I have decided to honor the edit request and have now changed this memorial to show Noah being the son of Arnold.
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy Articles List...
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on census data Noah Castor was born between 1755 and 1765 in Virginia. Haine's History of Hamilton County, Indiana states that Noah was "one of thirty children born to Conrad Castor, who lived at Brock's Gap, Virginia." Howe
2 CONC ver, Noah may have been a son of Arnold, which would make Noah a grandson of Conrad. Noah could have been a ward of Conrad after Arnold died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conrad Castor [Custer]
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah married Rebecca Matheny around 1785 in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime after Noah died, Rebecca went to Hamilton County, Indiana to live with Frederick and Nancy Harger. She died 22 August 1848 and was buried at the Prairie Baptist Church Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT ildren of Noah and Rebeccca:
2 CONT 1. Nathan Castor born 1786 PA
2 CONT 2. Susan Castor born 16 August 1792 PA
2 CONT 3. Conrad Castor born 9 December 1789 Beaver County, PA
2 CONT 4. Uriah Castor born 1790-1800 PA
2 CONT 5. Sampson Castor born about 1800 PA
2 CONT 6. Rachel Castor born about 1801 PA
2 CONT 7. Ruth Castor born 29 November 1806 PA
2 CONT 8. Nancy Castor born 24 December 1807 Beaver County, PA; married Frederick Harger 18 November 1825 OH; died 20 February 1869 IN.
2 CONT 9. Benjamin Castor born 1809 Beaver County, PA
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Aged 65y 28d
2 CONT
2 CONT ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
