1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=106532930 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 11 2018, 6:46:12 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT Also a son Adam b c 1802 d c 1857 burial not yet found.   Fulton Co probate has an inventory Adam Sipes dtd Mar 1857.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===will===
2 CONT May 1832
2 CONT  In the name of God - Amen. I Emanuel Sipe of Bedford County in the State of Pennsylvania, being sick and weak of body but of sound mind, memory and understanding, considering the certainty of death and the uncertainty of the time
2 CONC  thereof and being desirous to settle my worldly affairs and thereby be the better prepared to leave this world when it shall please God to call me hence, do make and publish this last will and testament in the manner and form fol
2 CONC lowing. Item - I give and bequeath to my beloved wife Margaret, thirty bushels of grain each and every year as long as she remains my widow to be paid her by my executor hereafter mentioned in wheat, corn, rye, and buckwheat in pr
2 CONC oportion as the crops may chance to be. It is also my desire for my wife to have the house and garden where my son Jacob lives with an acre of ground round the house as long as she remains my widow, she has also the privilege of p
2 CONC asture for one cow. My son Solomon, now at the breast, is to be raised and taken care of by his mother until he is old enough to go ahead as she may see proper. As for my wife property she had before our marriage is to be hers aga
2 CONC in and the bargain between us before marriage that I was to give her fifty dollars at my death, void. I give and bequeath to my son John the parcel of land heretofore laid off to him. I give and bequeath to my son Adam the parcel 
2 CONC of land that he has built a house on and heretofore laid off to him. I give and bequeath to my eldest daughter Francy George and her husband a parcel of land he now occupies. I give and bequeath to my daughter Margaraet and her hu
2 CONC sband Robert Woodcock the parcel of land heretofore laid off to him. I give and bequeath to my daughter Elizabeth and her husband Ephraim Dunham the set of blacksmith tools he has now in his possession and also a note I hold again
2 CONC st said Dunham. I give and bequeath to my daughter Catherine and her husband John Brubaker the parcel of land whereon he has built a house now touching my patented land. It is my will and desire that after the death of my wife or 
2 CONC provided she should marry again that the whole of my patented land be sold and divided in the following manner after giving my son Amos thirty dollars and my son Robert twenty five dollars to make them equal with my other sons tha
2 CONC t I have divided land it is my desire that the balance be equally divided among my six sons Henry, John, Adam, Amos, Robert and Solomon and I give and bequeath to my son Robert a black colt two years old. I give and bequeath to my
2 CONC  four daughters, Franey, Margaret, Elizabeth and Catherine the whole of my household furniture, except the stove which is to remain in the house, to be equally divided among them and to be in full of their part of my estate. It is
2 CONC  my will and desire that my son Amos farm and take care of the plantation whereon I now live and also the place where Ephraim Dunham now lives as long as my wife remains a widow and pay her each and every year the aforesaid thirty
2 CONC  bushels of grain in the way and manner before mentioned. My son John is to pay the taxes and keep the plantation in repair and has full privilege to rent out any part of the land he may think proper. Provided my son Solomon shoul
2 CONC d die before he arrives to the year of twenty one it is my desire that his part of my estate be divided equally among the other five sons Henry, John, Adam, Amos and Robert. It is further my desire that the balance of my personal 
2 CONC property be sold and after my just debts and funeral expenses are paid the balance to be divided among my six sons, share and share alike. It is my further desire that my wife give my son Amos peaceable possession of the home I no
2 CONC w live in and lastly I do hereby constitute and appoint my three sons John, Adam, and Amos executors of my last will and testament, annulling all former wills by be heretofore made, ratifying and confirming this and no other to be
2 CONC  my last will and testament. May 28, 1832
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT Fulton Co Historical Society cemetery transcriptions have Emanuel d-4 Dec. 1832
2 CONT
2 CONT Will was probated in Bedford Co, PA but land is located in what now is Licking Creek Twp, Fulton Co.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of burial have also been erroneously reported to be December 1832 at McConnellsburg, Fulton County, Pennsylvania, United States (unattested, conflicts with his Find A Grave memorial).
2 CONT
