2 NOTE As a Revolutionary War Soldier he was not a "Daughter of the American Revolution". He was the the participant who made eligible his daughters and other ancesters to claim DAR status.  His heirs male would be SAR's - Sons of the Am
3 CONC erican Revolution
1 NOTE 1. Elizabeth's father was General John Bull of the Revolutionary War. General John Bull was born on Jun 1 1728 in Providence Township, Philadelphia (Montgomery Co.) Pennsylvania. He resided in 1771 in Morristown, Pennsylvania. He 
2 CONC was a Member - 2nd Provincial Convention in 1775 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. This determined an open rebellion to the King He was a Colonel - 1st Pennsylvania Battalion of Continental Troops on Jan 20 1776 in Pennsylvania. He w
2 CONC as a Colonel of the Pennsylvania Regiment of Foot on May 2 1777 in Pennsylvania. He was an Adjutant General of Pennsylvania on Jun 17 1777 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. He died on Aug 9 1824 in Morristown, Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Mary Phillipps on Aug 13 1752 in Northumberland County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Phillipps was born in 1731 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. She died on Feb 23 1811 in Morristown, Pennsylvania.
