1 NOTE !BIRTH - SOME PROMINENT VA FAMILIES VOL 4 P. 101 by Louise Du Bellet
2 CONT See Death
2 CONT
2 CONT !MAR - Ibid
2 CONT The wife of Gen. John Smith, to whom he was married February 10, 1781, by Rev. Mr. Surgis in Berkeley Co., VA has been variously named Anna, Animus and Quinia Bull.  It is probable that she assumed the name of Anna when a young gi
2 CONC rl and retained it through life.
2 CONT
2 CONT !DEATH - Ibid
2 CONT Mrs. Anna Bull Smith died September 15, 1831, prob. in Frederick Co., VA, aged about 70 years.  She never would tell the date of her birth; said when asked, that she was as old as her eyes and a little older than her teeth. Notwit
2 CONC hstanding this peculiarity, she was a woman of more than ordinary business capacity and literary ability. - Ibid
2 CONT
2 CONT !BURIAL - Ibid 
2 CONT Her body was moved from Hackwood Estate to Mt. Hebron Cemetery, Winchester, VA. - (photo)
2 CONT Tombstone reads:
2 CONT Anna Bull
2 CONT Died 1832
2 CONT Aged 75 years
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  This tombstone differs from Louise duBellet's account.  If the grandson, Edward Jaquelin Davis put up the tombstone, he may have just guessed at her age. - JMC
