1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in Chester Cty., Pa. but moved to Catawissa where was a farmer and lived there until he died.   Because of his religious scruples, he did no fighting in the Revolutionary war, but with his own teams, conveyed supplies 
2 CONC for the American army from place to place.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notice in Lycoming Gazette 11/8/1826 titled "Jacob Casselberry: Land in Muncy Twp".,(in Notice of Sheriff's Sale), control #00653233.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob's estate was to be administered by John and William .  It was in the Lycoming Gazette on 4/16/1834 Page.4 control #00648329.
