1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !NOTES: During Civil War (?) Battle of Shiloh, he tripped on log and lost his rifle, falling down just as a canonball whizzed past over his head. Married by J. P. Squire Thomas. William & Lillie McBEE buried (?) next to Earl L. Mc
2 CONC BEE at the Salem Cemetery; no headstone. Grace McBee MILLER, Tom Doolin's dau., remembers going to his grave as a youngster with Estil BARRON, from Aunt Mag (Margaret McBee BARRON), who was living at Willie BARRON's in Bobtown KY.
2 CONC  This would mitigate towards internment at Eden Cemetery at Bobtown, rather than Salem Cemetery at Coin. (11-04-1981). Grandpa & Grandma McBee buried next to Earl Lucien MCBEE, s/o Tom Doolin McBEE; Earl has a headstone. (01-04-19
2 CONC 82).
2 CONT
2 CONT !AFN: Also, C965-7H.
2 CONT
2 CONT !MILITARY SERVICE: Pvt. Co. A, 63rd Inf. Regt. (Tenn, CSA), Nat'l Archives. aka: 74th Regt./Fains' Regt.
2 CONT
2 CONT !SOURCES: Family Bible of Willie BARRON ipo Eugene O. BARRON, Greencastle IN. Family Bible of William McBEE ipo Earl Quintrell, Knoxville TN. Family Bible of Viola RAY, Wilmington NC. Claibourne Co. TN, 1850 Census: p. 324 #1150 C
2 CONC laibourne Co. TN, 1860 Census: p. 50 (272) #315, 3d District (P.O. Tazwell) Claibourne Co. TN Marriage Records, Bk. 2, p. 144. Pulaski Co. KY Census: 1870-1880. Pulaski Co. KY Marriage Records. Laurel Co. KY Birth & Deaths (1852-1
2 CONC 862). Correspondence with Grace (McBee) MILLER (RIN: 3780), 659 Fair Rd., Sidney OH 45365 (Nov 1981 to Apr 1983). Correspondence with Earl W. Quintrell, 1814 Highland Ave. #13, Knoxville TN 37916 (6-21-81).
2 CONT
2 CONT !LDS: BE/SP, Batch # 8220103-61. SS, Batch # 7606305-26.
