1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HENRY DEVORE is a native of Bracken County, Ky., born August
2 CONT
2 CONT 1, 1795, and is the son of Jerry and Nancy (Mann) Devore, natives of
2 CONT
2 CONT New Jersey and of English descent. Henry was reared as a farmer until
2 CONT
2 CONT he reached the age of sixteen years, when he became a learner to the
2 CONT
2 CONT trade of carpentering, and followed the same for nearly thirty years.
2 CONT
2 CONT When about twenty-two years of age, he married Anna, daughter of Rev.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Barnes, of Kentucky, to which union succeeded six children, of
2 CONT
2 CONT which number four are living. After emigrating to this county, he lived
2 CONT
2 CONT in Spencer, and there followed his trade for about twelve years, when he
2 CONT
2 CONT purchased land in this township and engaged in farming. He now owns
2 CONT
2 CONT 565 acres, a portion of which he entered from the Government, and has
2 CONT
2 CONT a large share of the honor due to those who have developed this section.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of his wife, in 1863, he was united in marriage to Miranda
2 CONT
2 CONT A. (Tool) Martin, of Putnam County, daughter of John Teel, one
2 CONT
2 CONT of the earliest settlers of this county, who came bither in 1818. Mr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Devore is said to have made the first improvements in this county, and
2 CONT
2 CONT has had a large share of experience. F or many years his life ww; one of
2 CONT
2 CONT toil, hardships and privations. He is one of the earliest settlers of the county. Politically, he is a stanch Republican.
