1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HUGH B. DEVORE, farmer and stock-raiser, was born in Montgomery
2 CONT
2 CONT Town~hip, Owen County, Ind., March 29, 1830, and is a son of Hew'y
2 CONT
2 CONT and Anna (Barnes) DeVore, both natives of Kentucky, and of French and
2 CONT
2 CONT Dutch descent respectively. Hugh received some education in youth, and
2 CONT
2 CONT was brought np as a farmer. When twenty years of age, he married
2 CONT
2 CONT MiBS ISlibella, daughter of William and Polly Combs, from which union
2 CONT
2 CONT sprang one child-Lara. Mrs. DeVore having died, he married, July
2 CONT
2 CONT 26, 1860, Sarah Gray, daughter of William and Jane Bestal, and from
2 CONT
2 CONT this nnion resulted five children-Nora E. (Mrs. Layne), Cora E., Hattie
2 CONT
2 CONT G., Metta O. arid Maud H. Mr. DeVore is the owner of 950 acres of
2 CONT
2 CONT land, containing many improvements lind well cultivated, nearly all of which is the attainment of itR possessor, and the result of well-direcW
2 CONT
2 CONT purpose IlIld labor. Mr. DeVore is filling his second term as County
2 CONT
2 CONT Commissioner. He is a member of the Masonic fraternity, and a generally
2 CONT
2 CONT respected citizen. Mrs. DeVore is a member of the Christian
2 CONT
2 CONT Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Counties of Clay and Owen Indiana, Pg 951 & 952.
