1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Erepta (or Sarepta) Abigail Savage (1839-1917) was born in Townscroft, Michigan and died in Linn, Oregon.  She arrived in Oregon with her parents and 7 siblings in 1846.
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents: Towner Savage b: 18 Mar 1803 in Washington Co., NewYork & Matilda Purdy
2 CONT
2 CONT married
2 CONT # Thomas DeHaven b: 1829/1830
2 CONT # Samuel Edwards
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Ruey Catherine b: abt 1857 in Oregon.  Married William A. Roberts.
2 CONT # Sarah Alice  b: 1859 in Oregon.  
2 CONT # Eva Elizabeth  b: 1861 in  Oregon.  Married George Stallcup.
2 CONT # Amelia Ann  b: 1862 in Oregon.  Married Joel Howton.
2 CONT # George Henry  b: 1864 in Oregon.  Married Ama.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES: 
2 CONT * Marion Co. Probate File #421 
2 CONT * DAR pg 25 Steeves, BOOK OF REMEMBRANCE, pp 65-67 
2 CONT * DOS 1 Mar 1871 3:1 
2 CONT * PCA 11 Mar 1871 (index only)
2 CONT * Notes
2 CONT * Name: Erepta (or Sarepta) Abigail Savage
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents: Towner Savage b: 18 Mar 1803 in Washington Co., NewYork & Matilda Purdy
2 CONT
2 CONT married
2 CONT # Thomas DeHaven b: 1829/1830
2 CONT # Samuel Edwards
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Ruey Catherine b: abt 1857 in Oregon.  Married William A. Roberts.
2 CONT # Sarah Alice  b: 1859 in Oregon.  
2 CONT # Eva Elizabeth  b: 1861 in  Oregon.  Married George Stallcup.
2 CONT # Amelia Ann  b: 1862 in Oregon.  Married Joel Howton.
2 CONT # George Henry  b: 1864 in Oregon.  Married Ama.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * 1910 OR CENSUS - Hollas Edwards, age 55, occupation barber, b. Oregon, is enumerated with his wife of 43 years, Sarah A. [Alice], age 53, b. Oregon. Also enumerated with the family is Erepta A. Edwards, identified as mother-in-l
2 CONC aw [of Hollas], age 69, widow, and Frankie L Edwards, age 7, single, identifed as granddaughter [of Hollas], b. Oregon.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.salempioneercemetery.org/records/pf_display_record.php?id=5803
2 CONT
2 CONT From: Steeves, Sarah Hunt, BOOK OF REMEMBRANCE OF MARION COUNTY, OREGON, PIONEERS 1840 - 1860, Portland, Oregon, The Berncliff Press, 1927, (Source: G. O. Savage, Salem, Oregon, 1926), pp 65-67Steeves, "Book of Remembrance", pp 65
2 CONC -67
2 CONT
2 CONT > … As to politics Mr. Savage was a republican. Part of his family were members of the Methodist Church. Mr. Savage always followed farming. To the union of Towner Savage and his wife Matilda Purdy were born the following children
2 CONC : Lydia, who died as a child. Hannah, who married Samuel Holderness. John, who married Rhoda Pressley, and after her death he married Eleanor Tarrant. Lewis, who married Minerva Connelley. Alfred, who married Lucretia Connelley. L
2 CONC yman, who married, first, Matilda Stewart; second, Theresa Keene. Surepta, who married, first, Thomas DeHaven; second, Samuel Edwards. Oren G., who married, first, Martha Walk; second, Loretta Johnson. Elizabeth, who married John 
2 CONC Crawford. Mortimer R., who married Sarah Murphy." 
2 CONT
2 CONT
