1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ~• of Jeffersonville
2 CONT c.1870 he lived on a farm there which can be seen on an Map page of an atlas of that period "F. Highley" This had either been part of the Jesse Bean farm until the mid 1800s when Jesse died... or it is possible that Jesse sold par
2 CONC t of the farm to the Highleys before he died; or Jesse's father John may have sold him the land.
2 CONT
2 CONT Felix had a  <Highley> close relative who rode with the 1st Montgomery Troop of Mounted Dragoons  in 1844
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/projects/1st-Montgomery-Troop-of-Light-Dragoons/4477281 quite a few of these Dragoons were from Jeffersonville, including Jesse Weber Bean and the Matheys young men eg. Wm. Zell Matheys who led the Troop
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT > children
2 CONT Albert Crawford Highley, George Norman Highley, Ione Boyd Everett (born Highley), Charles Corson Highley, Sara Corson Holstein (born Highley), Anna B. Highley
