2 TITL Early 1700's properties of West Norriton
2 NOTE one focus Bean's History of Montgomery County in the 1880s was farming. See: https://www.geni.com/documents/view/named_event-6000000204653939850?doc_id=6000000204654463821&event_id=6000000204653939850 
2 NOTE researchinr the names on this map reveals that Robert Thomson and Robert Curry were husbands of Mary Norris. RObert curry (2nd husband died before  Mary and by codicil of his estate left lands to the heirs of his step children inc
3 CONC luding various later generations of the  Darrah family. This distribution in alluded to in https://www.geni.com/documents/view/6000000019182195571?doc_id=6000000180787159811 , a letter written by Jesse Weber Bean (CSA) who had hea
3 CONC rd his grandfather  speak of the chain of title of this land... including Archibald Darrah "Archie".
2 NOTE In reading the preceding, it is clear that Samuel Swift, Esq. once owned a good portion of  the land shown on the map above.
3 CONT John Bean of Perkiomen
2 NOTE ''as written by Jesse Weber Bean to his brother Edwin Adams Bean in 1895'' (full original is attached. See Sources attached to Jesse Weber Bean and his grandfather Jesse Bean
3 CONT
3 CONT (from last page)
3 CONT
3 CONT "Grand Father('s) Father (John Bean)'''' gave him (the writer's grandfather Jesse) the old Woodville place (.) 
3 CONT I think he bought it of(f of) one of the old stock of Boyers that come to (grief) in building the house that was on it and it contained many broad acres. (I)t took in all of the [https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Swift-Esq/600000
3 CONC 0009085402860 ''Samuel Swift farm''] and a large part of the Steven Porter or Wm Hamill place(.) Grandfather lost many acres of land in set(t)ling old man Markleys land(,) (f)ather of Abraham and Samuel Markley(.) They told him th
3 CONC at there (were) no debts against the Estate of any amount and persuaded him to pay of some claims in full thereby making him responsible for the whole amount of all claims (;) and it took more than half of his land(.) Saml and Abr
3 CONC aham gave Grandfather papers obligating themselves to make the amount good if they ever got able but our Father  (William Bean) told me them paper(s) were never found and he su(p)posed that Abraham tricked Grand Father (Jesse Bean
3 CONC ) out of them some how(.)''
2 NOTE The upper branch of Indian Creek shown here has a pond at its headwaters. From looking around I suppose this is the same as the one that now lies in the Jeffersonville Golf Club c. 2023:: effersonvillegolfclub.org 
2 NOTE Robert Curry on early mapping: https://maps.archives.upenn.edu/WestPhila1777/view-parcel.php?pid=10245 
2 NOTE The mayor of Philadelphia, "Thom. Griffith" sic & wife  deeded 100 acres to Robert Thompson on Sept 2, 1737 on the "Spring Run" off Indian Creek. Note that there was once a "Log House" there. Some of the succession of owners of th
3 CONC is 100 acres are included here.
2 NOTE parenthetically: Felix Francis Highley owned 100 ac somewhere on this rendering. A map of 1870 confirms that the "F. Highley" farm consisted of 100 acres.  Perhaps that farm had the same metes and bounds as "Thom. Grffith & wife t
3 CONC o Robt. Thompson; Sept 2, 1737 - 100 acres"
3 CONT
