1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Wack Follows Son and Husband In Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Lansdale Women Died Two Months After the Late David Wack
2 CONT
2 CONT For the third time within two months the grim reaper visited the Wack home, at 25 Mount Vernon street, Lansdale, when the mother, Mrs. Susan Wack, succumbed, Tuesday night.
2 CONT She was seventy-six years old and the mother of eleven children, seven of whom survive. Her husband died on April 1 and a son, John F., died on Sunday.
2 CONT The following children survive: Percy and David Jr., Mrs. Fred E. Brunner, Mrs. Harrison Godschall of Lansdale; Otis, of Nova Scotia; Mrs. Clarence Walker, of West Point and Mrs. Ethel Pool, of Philadelphia. Nineteen grandchildren
2 CONC  and eleven great-grandchildren also survive, in addition to the following brothers and sisters: Charles Fetterolf and Mrs. Alice Crouthamel, of Philadelphia; Nathan Fetterolf, of West Point, Isaac Fetterolf, of Towamencin and Dan
2 CONC iel Fetterolf, of Collegeville.
2 CONT The funeral will be held Saturday afternoon with services at her late home and interment at Lansdale cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lansdale Reporter
2 CONT Friday, June 2, 1922* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/37176602/susan_g_wack Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 26 2025, 13:16:12 UTC''
