1 NOTE {geni:about_me} C. G. FETTEROLF DIES, NATIVE OF NORTH PENN
2 CONT
2 CONT Philadelphia Man Formerly Published Weekly 
2 CONT Newspaper At Langhorne
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles G. Fetterolf, of 2131 North Seventh street, Philadelphia, a native of the North Penn section, died this morning.
2 CONT Mr. Fetterolf with his brother, George G., once published the Langhorne Standard.  He had bee employed by Cyrus W. Curtis, in Philadelphia, but left the Curtis company to join his brother in publishing the Langhorne weekly.  After
2 CONC  the death of his brother, Mr. Fetterolf continued with the paper until the publishing plant was destroyed by fire twenty-five years ago.  He never resumed publication, moving soon afterward to Philadelphia.
2 CONT He was a pastmaster of the Newtown lodge of the Free and Accepted Masons.
2 CONT Mr. Fetterolf's wife, Elizabeth, is dead. Three daughters who survive are: Rebecca and Elizabeth, at home and Ruth , of Germantown.  A sister Mrs. Alice G. Crauthamel, lives in Philadelphia.
2 CONT Funeral arrangements have not been completed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The North Penn Reporter
2 CONT Thursday, January 23, 1941* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/37163137/charles-groff-fetterolf Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 30 2022, 13:09:25 UTC''
