2 CONT Veteran North Penn Resident was 86; Funeral Service Tuesday
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Alice G. Crauthamel, a veteran resident of the North Penn Valley, died Friday afternoon in Elm Terrace Hospital.  She lived at 101 St. Elmo street, Lansdale.
2 CONT Mrs. Crauthamel, who was eighty-six, had been in failing health for some time.
2 CONT A daughter of the late Daniel and Rebecca Fetterolf, pioneer residents in the area, she was born on a farm near Lederach.  At the age of four her parents moved to Kulpsville and at the age of eight she came to Lansdale.  The decea
2 CONC sed was a member of Trinity Lutheran Church, Lansdale.
2 CONT Surviving are four children:  Mrs. Elizabeth F. Trimble and George F., Lansdale, Joseph G., Cleveland, O., and Charles F., San Pedro, Calif.
2 CONT Funeral services will be held on Tuesday.
2 CONT
2 CONT The North Penn Reporter
2 CONT Monday, July 14, 1952* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/37102379/alice-groff-crauthamel Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 30 2022, 13:09:25 UTC''
