1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/24166708/sarah-r_-kissinger
2 CONT
2 CONT Reading Eagle-March 11, 1903-Front Page Sarah R., wife of Abraham N. Kissinger, died of pleurisy at 5:55 a.m. today, at her residence, 1030 Penn Street. She was ailing the past six months and was bedfast since last Friday. Mrs. Ki
2 CONC ssinger was a daughter of Daniel and the late Sarah Spohn (Reiff), and was a life-long resident of this city. Her father was a well-known contractor. Deceased was an active member of Trinity Lutheran Church and several of the soci
2 CONC eties connected with the congregation, and was held in high esteem by a wide circle of friends. Besides her husband, she is survived by three children: Clifford W., Sarah E., wife of H. Seidel Throm, and Anita Kissinger; also thes
2 CONC e brothers and sisters: Llewellyn J. Spohn, Mrs. John B. Moore, and Mrs. Harry Hunsberger, Reading; Mrs. Wallace C. Wise, San Francisco; Mrs. Henry C. Jones and Charles D. Kissinger (sic Spohn) , Philadelphia. Mrs. Kissinger was o
2 CONC f a charitable disposition and a good friend of the needy.
2 CONT ---
2 CONT Reading Eagle-March 16, 1903-page 3 The funeral of Sarah R., wife of Abraham N. Kissinger, took place from her residence, 1030 Penn Street, at 11 a.m. and was largely attended. Rev. Dr. Jacob Fry, of Mt. Airy, formerly of this cit
2 CONC y, and the Rev. Dr. E. T. Horn, of Trinity Lutheran Church, of which the deceased was a faithful member, conducted the services. A choir under the leadership of Prof. Willoughby S. Wilde, sang a number of selections. The remains l
2 CONC ay in a black cloth covered red cedar casket, with copper lining, full French plate front glass, oxidized trimmings and plate bearing name and age of deceased and date of death. The tributes from deceased's many friends and relati
2 CONC ves were numerous and included many handsome designs. Among the out-of-town people present were: Mr. and Mrs. Henry C. Jones and daughter; Mr. and Mrs. Chas. D. Spohn and and son; Mr. and Mrs. Amos Jones and family, Phila.; Mr. an
2 CONC d Mrs. Nicholas Dennebaum, Mr. and Mrs. Valentine Stichter, Mrs. Milton Hamilton, Pottsville; Mrs. H. A. Kissinger, Birdsboro; Mrs. James Dubson, Blandon; Dr. Emma Richards, Miss Kate Richards and Miss Louise Warren, Norristown; F
2 CONC rank Seidel, Blandon; John B. Reiff, Pottstown; Mr. and Mrs. Keiser, Lebanon; Nicholas Yocum, Chester; Mr. and Mrs. John F. Gingrich, Lancaster; Mrs. Emma Heffner, Lyons; Mr. and Mrs. Henry Spohn, Phila.; and others from various p
2 CONC oints. The bearers were Nicholas Dennebaum, William H. Yocum, James Mercer, Adam B. Reeser, Albert Ritter and George W. Leiss. Interment in Charles Evans Cemetery. Funeral director Hunter Henninger.
