1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Everard Lester Foulke was a judge in Wichita, Kansas and was a member of the legal firm of Foulke and Nash. Per Iva Shinkle, he lived at 1204 N. Topeka, Wichita, Kansas. The following is a transcription of a newspaper article at t
2 CONC he time of E. Lester Foulke's death in Wichita in 1936; E. Lester Foulke, Wichita Attorney for Years, Passes. Church and University, Official for years, was stricken lastFriday. To Wichita in 1899, E. Lester Foulke, prominent atto
2 CONC rney, trustee of Friends church and member of the board of directors of Friends Univeristy died in a hospital Sunday. He was 67. E. Lester Foulke was born in Cottonwood Falls, KS in 1868 and attended Lewis Academy in Wichita and W
2 CONC ichita High School. His parents moved from Cottonwood Falls to Wichita and then to Pretty Prairie where he was reared. He studied law in an Attorney's office in Hutchinson and was admitted to the bar at Hutchinson in 1896. In 1899
2 CONC , he came to Wichita to practice law. At the time of his death in 1936, he was survived by his wife, Clara, two daughters, Majorie and Dorothy, all of 2015 University; three sisters, Mrs. Grace Emery, Hutchinson, Mrs Amy Roehl, Wi
2 CONC eser, Idaho, Mrs. Fannie Mitchell, Los Angeles, and a bother Myron Foulke, of Mountain View, MO.
