1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Jemima is mentioned as daughter of Abraham Collins. There is a  record of a marriage between Abraham Collins and Ann Major in:  
2 CONT Marriages Grace Church, Jamaica, New York 1710 to 1731
2 CONT Origin and History of Grace Church, Jamaica, New York
2 CONT By Horation Oliver Ladd
2 CONT Published by Shakespeare Press, New York, 1914
2 CONT Found at library of New-York Historical Society, 2004 
2 CONT Transcriber: Peter Devine Feb. 2004 
2 CONT Joseph Kissam & Deborah Whitehead 2/7/1727 at Jamaica lic
2 CONT Stephen Evans & Catherine Brass 4/16/1728 at Jamaica publ
2 CONT Augustus Grassett & Elizabeth Whitehead 7/24/1728 at Jamaica lic
2 CONT ABRAHAM COLLINS & ANN MAJOR 8/11/1728 at Jamaica publ
2 CONT If this is Abraham, father of Jemima, it is likely that Ann died within a  few years of the marriage as there are some researching this family who  feel very strongly that Jemima's mother was a Baldridge. In New York City  Wills, 
2 CONC 1777-1783 appears the following which seems to mention Jemima  Seata? (Seeley), daughter of Abraham Collins, deceased as if she were  related. :Page 249.--"In the name of God, Amen. I, ADAM BALDERIDGE, of  New Utrecht, in Kings Co
2 CONC unty, on Long Island. I leave to Sarah Coleman,  Jemima Seata, and Elizabeth, formerly the wife of David Cameron, all of  them the daughters of Abraham Collins, deceased, of Blooming Grove, New  York, all of my estate, real and pe
2 CONC rsonal, except as follows. To my  friend, Jacob Gale, ?100. To my friend, Benjamin Whitehead, of Jamaica,  ?50. But if none of the above legatees should appear and make lawful  claims to my said estate, then I leave all my estate 
2 CONC to the Church of New  Utrecht, to be put at interest and the interest used for the relief of  the Poor of New Utrecht by the Elders of the Church. My executors are to  take proper pains to notify the above legatees. I make my frie
2 CONC nds, Adrian  Van Brunt, Peter Van Pelt, John Edmonds, executors, all of New Utrecht." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated October 1, 1777. Witnesses, Evert Suydam, Teunis Suydam, John  Dennis. Proved, May 6, 1780. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Samuel Seeley b. 2 Feb 1754 is placed as a son of Nathaniel  Seeley and Jemima Collins when he is called nephew in the The Will of  Adam Collins of Blooming Grove, Orange County dated 1 May 1770, which  named sister Jem
2 CONC ima Seeley, brother in law Nathaniel Seeley, and nephew  Samuel Seeley.
