2 CONT
2 CONT England & Wales Christening Records, 1530-1906 about William Seelie
2 CONT
2 CONT Name:  William Seelie
2 CONT
2 CONT Gender:  Male
2 CONT
2 CONT Christening Date:  23 Feb 1564
2 CONT
2 CONT Christening Place:  Great Gransden, Huntingdonshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Citation: Place: Great Gransden, Huntingdonshire, England; ; Date Range: 1555 - 1653; Film Number: 1040625. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Seeley-69
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born about 1563 in Bluntisham-cum-Earith, Huntingdon, England[1] It is believed he first married Grace Prett 23 Feb 1584 at Great Gransden.[2] With Grace Prett he had son Robert.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT William's wife Grace, Robert's mother, died and William remarried on October 12, 1614 to Briget Hills[4], a widow with a daughter Anne who married a Fiske. William and Briget had a son William who married Margaret Brenham on Janua
2 CONC ry 14, 1638 - they had a daughter Margaret by 1641.
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of William Seeley the elder, joiner, was found at the parish of Bluntisham cum Earity, a joint parish about seven miles from Huntingdon town. The will, two witnesses of which were found to be constables, was proved 4 Apr 
2 CONC 1646 and son Robert is not named in the will. Ralph Seeley, NEHGR cited below, speculates that Robert may have received his inheritance when he went to London or at age 21 or William may not have known his whereabouts when the wil
2 CONC l was drawn up in 1641. Records of the New Haven Colony 26 Oct 1646 show Robert being given leave to return to England.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Also found at the parish of Bluntisham cum Earity are a marriage record of William Seley and Bridget Hills; a marriage record of William Sealey and Margaret Brenham; and a burial record of "Grand. Seley" which might be the William
2 CONC  Seeley mentioned in the will of William Seeley the Elder.[4] Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Seely was apprenticed in the Cordwainers' Company of London on March 10, 1623 to serve seven years, but was freed between August 1, 1626 and July 17, 1627. He married Mary, the widow of Walter Mason on December 15, 1626.
2 CONT
2 CONT The publication of the Seeley Genealogical Society cited below contradicts NEHGR and other sources on a number of critical facts yet presents no documentation for its statements. It claims William died 1614 and that Grace Prett li
2 CONC ved until 1635. Update: note that this link goes to updated information from SGS with a thorough discussion of sources and analysis. This profile should be updated with information contained at the link. (9 Aug 2019 T Stanton) Sou
2 CONC rces
2 CONT
