1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ben M. Angel (no relation) notes: Could not find anything confirming title specifically to John Angell as "Lord of Temple Ewell". He did have ownership (second generation, continuing to another John Angell who died
2 CONC  in 1784 without heir) of a manor, formerly owned by the Knights Templar, at Temple Ewell, Kent, according to British History Online:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.british-history.ac.uk/report.aspx?compid=63586
2 CONT
