3 STAE Utah
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =John Henry Owen Wilcox=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Hazzard Willcox and Sarah Seely of Arkansas
2 CONT * Born February 14, 1824, in Arkansas. Came to Utah 1847.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000000193711569?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000082903854506&position=0 '''John Henry Owen Wilcox Death Certificate''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000000193711569&photo_id=6000000198299067922&position=0 '''John Henry Owen Wilcox Geneology and Family Pioneer History Records Compiled by the Mount Pleasant Histor
2 CONC ical Association.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Henry was a farmer born in Arkansas Feb 14, 1824. The family removed to Marion County Missouri where his father died. His mother joined the Mormon church in Marion County, then moved to Jackson county, then to Clay Co, then t
2 CONC o Caldwell, and Lee County Missouri. Then to Iowa from which they departed for Salt Lake City in ox team with John Taylor, arriving September 30, 1847. In 1850 John moved to Manti, then to Pleasant Grove and then North Ogden, and 
2 CONC in 1860 came to Mt. Pleasant. He took up 20 acres of land which he still owns, with his residence in the city, when the Walker war broke out. He worked in Pleasant Creek Canyon and lost his wagon and lumber and two yoke of oxen. H
2 CONC e took a active part in the Indian war. His wife was Mary, daughter of James and Elizabeth Seeley Young born in upper Canada on June 6 1831. She drove three yoke of oxen across the plains assisted in hauling logs to build her pare
2 CONC nt's house and molded the adobes for the chimney. They were married in SLC on March 14, 1848. Their 11 children are: Hassard, Elizabeth, sarah, James H., John C., Mary, Clarissa, Ella, Hannah, Martha, and Justus
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:	'''Mary Young''' on  March 14, 1848, Salt Lake City (daughter of James Young and Elizabeth Seely of Canada, pioneers 1847). She was born June 6, 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Their children:==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hazzard, married Tilda Westwood;
2 CONT * Elizabeth, married Philip Hurst;
2 CONT * Sarah, married Wesley Bills;
2 CONT * James Henry, married Harrett Day; married Ellis Staker;
2 CONT * John Carlos, married Violet Westwood;
2 CONT * Mary Mehitable, married Hurbet Day;
2 CONT * Clarissa Jane, married Peter Meiling;
2 CONT * Ellen (Sabray), married John Oliver;
2 CONT * Hannah, married Joseph Corlson;
2 CONT * Martha A., married Richard D. Westwood;
2 CONT * Justice Azel, married Selma Corlson.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Family home Mt. Pleasant, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Farmer. Died November 21, 1909, Mt. Pleasant, Utah. Sources:	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah, page 1248
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/briefhistoryofde00jaco/page/21/mode/1up?view=theater
