1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eleazer became one of the original patentees of Bedford, Westchester County, New York, and resided there although he never gave up his holdings in Stamford, CT. He returned to Stamford about 1697, where he died in 
2 CONC 1695/98(?). His will is dated 29 Apr 1691, and proved 22 Jul 1699.
2 CONT
2 CONT >On June 6, 1692, he testified in favor of the accused witch, Elizabeth CLAWSON, that he had lived near her as neighbors for many years, and always observed her to be a woman for peace and without malice.
2 CONT
