1 NOTE In 1680 took wife Susannah and family from Stamford, CT, to Bedford,
2 CONT now in Westchester County, NY. He was one of the original patentees of
2 CONT Bedford. On June 6, 1692, Eleazer testified in favor of the accused
2 CONT witch Elizabeth Clawson, that he had lived as her near neighbor for many
2 CONT years, and he always observed her to be a woman of peace and without
2 CONT malice. He never gave up his holdings in Stamford and in 1697 they
2 CONT returned to Stamford, CT. Eleazer died about a year later in Stamford.
