0 @N6000000007283508277@ NOTE
1 CONT Judy Goldbaum, 17 May 2000.
1 CONT
1 CONT Donna N. Basinger, Clymer Connections, RootsWeb's WorldConnect
1 CONT Project, 22 May 2000.  Abraham op den Graf.
1 CONT
1 CONT June (Shaull) Lutz 1988, History of the Op den Graef/Updegraff
1 CONT Family, pp. U-6 and U-10.  Birth 1646 or 1658.  Died 25/27 March
1 CONT 1731.  One of the immigrants to Philadelphia in 1783, sharing 2000
1 CONT acres purchased by himself and his two brothers from Jacob Telner who
1 CONT received an original land grant from William Penn.  He was a charter
1 CONT member in establishing Germantown in 1689.  In 1704 he and his wife
1 CONT moved from Germantown to the neighboring Perkiomen area now part of
1 CONT Montgomery County.  Buried Evansburg Memmonite Cemetery, Perkiomen
1 CONT Township, Skippackville, Pennsylvania.  Five, possibly six (no date
1 CONT for a daughter Elizabeth), children, four of whom shared in the land
1 CONT division after his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT Dora Smith, Op Den Graeff Ancestry,
1 CONT http://www.geocities.com/Heartland/Acres/5127/Webster/herman.html, 17
1 CONT July 2000.  Various sources give birth in 1647, 1651 or 1660.  Died
1 CONT 1719 or 25 March 1731.
1 CONT
1 CONT Paul Redden, Descendants of Herman op den Graef.  Immigrant 6 October
1 CONT 1683.  Signatory to the 1688 antislavery petition.
1 CONT
1 CONT Joe Patter, 4 March 1999, messages #227, #231, archive for The
1 CONT Original 13 Germantown Settlers.  One of only two Germantown
1 CONT residents who served in the assembly of the Pennsylvania colony in
1 CONT its first three decades, during 1687 and 1692.  Also held a number of
1 CONT offices in the Germantown borough.
1 CONT
1 CONT Wilhelm Niepoth, The Ancestry of the Thirteen Krefeld Emigrants of
1 CONT 1683.  Bans of marriage published 23 July 1679.  Abraham Isaaks op
1 CONT dem Graeff arrived Pennsylvania 6 October 1683.
0 @N6000000007283508247@ NOTE
