1 CONT supporters, the "Christian Quakers" or "Separatists" or "Keithians,"
1 CONT maintained that their opponents were not true believers in Christ
1 CONT Jesus,  were not Christians, and thus could not be joined with in
1 CONT worship; the Keithians instituted separate meetings.  At the
1 CONT Philadelphia Quarterly Meeting of the Society of Friends in 1692
1 CONT Keith was condemned.  Ultimately Keith left the Society of Friends
