1 CONT
1 CONT Wilhelm Niepoth, The Ancestry of the Thirteen Krefeld Emigrants of
1 CONT 1683.  Hermann Isaaks op dem Graeff arrived Pennsylvania 6 October
1 CONT 1863.
1 CONT
1 CONT Guidebook to Historical Germantown, 1902 Edition.  First settlers
1 CONT came from the lower Rhine country, near Holland.  Thirteen families
1 CONT (33 persons) left Crefeld in 1683 for London, where they embarked on
1 CONT the ship Concord.  Leaving London on 24 July, they arrived in
1 CONT Philadelphia 6 October.  On 23 October, thirteen settlers selected
1 CONT their land by lot in the newly laid out Germantown Township; they
1 CONT included Abraham op den Graeff, Herman op den Graeff, and Dirck op
1 CONT den Graeff.
