0 @N6000000007283505034@ NOTE
1 CONT G. W. Miller 1991, "Reconstructing the Op Den Graff windows of 1630
1 CONT A.D. to fit the Lohengrin Genealogy of the House of Cleves," Krefeld
1 CONT Immigrants and Their Descendants, vol. 8, #1, pp. 9-28.  Anna van
1 CONT Aldekerk (Dutch), Anne de Aldekerk (French), or Anna Altenkirchen
1 CONT (German), a woman associated with the village, church or cloister of
1 CONT Aldekerk (possibly a former nun).  Either died in childbirth of
1 CONT possibly living in 1616 when four noble-born nuns (three sisters von
1 CONT Brackel and sister Gudula von Arfft) were living in the home of
1 CONT Herman op den Graff in Krefeld.
1 CONT Aldekerk was under the jurisdiction of either the County of
1 CONT Geldern or the County of Altena.
1 CONT
1 CONT G. W. Miller 1996, "The Transfiguration of the Windows," Krefeld
1 CONT Immigrants and Their Descendants, vol. 13, #2, pp. 51-67.  Sister
1 CONT Gudula van Arkel aan de Aldekerk.  Believed to be buried at the
1 CONT Cloister of Aldekerk.
