1 CONT [LDBrown3-19.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT J.H. Gwathmey 1938, Historical Record of Virginians in the Revolution 
1 CONT 1775-1783. Edward Uptograve of Albemarle. From the Index of the 
1 CONT Revolutionary Records in the Virginia State Archives.
1 CONT
1 CONT State Library Board of Virginia 1913, Revolutionary Soldiers of 
1 CONT Virginia, Vol. I, Registers 33-34. Register of Description of the 
1 CONT Non-commissioned officers and privates at Chesterfield Court House. 
1 CONT Edward Uptegrove age 42, height 5 foot 6.5 inches, grey eyes, black 
1 CONT hair, fair complexion, no distinguishing marks. Carpenter from 
1 CONT Albemarle County, Virginia. Place of birth Pennsylvania Barracks. 
1 CONT Substitute from Albemarle County 30 March 1781. Enlistment for 6 
1 CONT months. Previous service in "F" Camp (Flying Camp, a mobile infantry 
1 CONT or artillery unit). Signed 4 April 1781. Quoted from Diane Fuerst, 
1 CONT Ancestry.com Uptegrove Surname Board, 16 February 2001. 
1 CONT
1 CONT PARENTS ARE NOT PROVEN, BUT ARE INFERRED FROM CIRCUMSTANTIAL 
1 CONT EVIDENCE. See below.
1 CONT
1 CONT Miles Philbeck, 1 July 1997. Descendant of the Uptegraf or Op den 
1 CONT graef family which came to Philadelphia in 1683. Much of Uptegroves 
1 CONT genealogy is not reliable. Specific link of Edward to family is 
1 CONT unknown.
1 CONT
1 CONT John B. Wells III, July 1997. Edward served as a private in the 
1 CONT Albemarle Militia in the Revolutionary War. About 1800 he went to 
1 CONT Rutherford County where he built his home on a farm on Puzzle Creek 
1 CONT in the Bostic community.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ronald Dale Dobbins, 4 May 2000. Some of the relatives of daughter 
1 CONT Mary also moved to Rutherford County, North Carolina, but shortened 
1 CONT their names to simply Groves.
1 CONT
1 CONT C.E. Ratcliff 1984, North Carolina Taxpayers 1701-1786. No 
1 CONT Updegroves.
1 CONT
1 CONT A.K. Register 1974, State Census of North Carolina 1784-1787. No 
1 CONT Uptegroves.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1800 North Carolina census, Rutherford County p. 148. George, 
1 CONT Soloman, and William Updegrove, all aged 26-45, with their families. 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT June (Shaull) Lutz 1988, History of the Op den Graef / Updegraff 
1 CONT Family. This Uptegroves family is not included. A group of German 
1 CONT immigrants from Krefeld left Gravesend, England, on 24 July 1683 on 
1 CONT the ship Concord which arrived in Philadelphia on 6 October 1683. 
1 CONT The passengers included three brothers: Dirck Isaacs, Hermann Isaacs 
1 CONT and Abraham Isaacs Op den Graeff, weavers from Krefeld and originally 
1 CONT Mennonites. They were grandsons of the "Bishop of the Mennonites" 
1 CONT Hermann Op den Graef (26 November 1585 Aldekirk, Muir, Germany- 27 
1 CONT December 1642 Krefeld, Germany) and Greitgen Pletjes (26 November 
1 CONT 1588 Kempen, Holland/Germany - January 1643 Krefeld). With them 
1 CONT came their mother and sister Margarette. This group established 
1 CONT Germantown. By 1690 or so, town records suggest the surname has 
1 CONT become Optegraff, though there are variants such as up de graeff and 
1 CONT up den graef.
1 CONT
1 CONT June (Shaull) Lutz 1988, History of the Op den Graef/Updegraff 
1 CONT Family. Ancestral lines (some not proven):
1 CONT 1 - Leonardo DeGroben, m. Maria De Norhelm
1 CONT 2 - Wolfgang DeGroben (1483 - )
1 CONT 3 - Abraham Op den Graeff (1490 - after 1561 Dusseldorf, Germany)
1 CONT 4 - Herman Op den Graeff (26 November 1585 Aldekirk, Muir, Germany - 
1 CONT 27 December 1642 Krefeld, Germany), m. August 1605 Krefeld, Germany, 
1 CONT Greitgen Pletjes (26 November 1588 Kempen, Holland (Germany?) - 7 
1 CONT January 1643 Krefeld, Germany), daughter of Driessen Pletjes (circa 
1 CONT 155 0 - 27 December 1645) and Alet Gobels ( ? Syllys - 7 January 
1 CONT 1640). [This family is related to William Penn, founder of 
1 CONT Pennsylvania.] 18 children.
1 CONT 5 - Isaak (Isaac) Op den Graeff (28 December 1615 or 28 February 1616 
1 CONT Krefeld, Germany - 17 January 1669 or 17 November 1678 or 16 January 
1 CONT 1679), m. after 1636 Grietgen Peters (Greietjen Porteis or Pieters) 
1 CONT (? - 19 October 1683 Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania). His wife 
1 CONT emigrated 1683 from Krefeld to Pennsylvania with three sons (and 
1 CONT their families) and a daughter.
1 CONT 6a - Hermann I. Op den Graeff (1642 - 1704/8), m. Liesbet (Elizabeth) 
1 CONT Van Bebber; also ? Debra Van Bebber. Before leaving Germany, the 
1 CONT three brothers Hermann, Derick and Abraham purchased 2000 acres of 
1 CONT land in Pennsylvania from Jacob Telner.
1 CONT 6b - Derick (Dirck or Derek) Op den Graeff (before 1642 Krefeld, 
1 CONT Germany - before 24 May 1697), m. 20 March 1681 Krefeld, Germany, to 
1 CONT Nilcken (Nellie) Vijtten (or Vyten). To Pennsylvania 1683. 
1 CONT Apparently no children.
1 CONT 6c - Abraham Isaacs Op den Graeff (1646/1658 - 25 March 1731 
1 CONT Skippackville, Pennsylvania), m. 23 July 1679 Trintje (Trijntje; also 
1 CONT Catharina) Jansen ( - before 1710). Moved from Germantown to the 
1 CONT Perkiomen area (now Montgomery County, Pennsylvania) about 16 May 
1 CONT 1704.
1 CONT 6c1 - Jacob Op den Graeff (1687 - 1750), married Anneken Ten Haven 
1 CONT (or De Haven).
1 CONT 6c2 - Margaret (Margrit or Margery) Op den Graeff (1691 - ), married 
1 CONT Thomas Howe.
1 CONT 6c3 - Isaac Updegraf/Updegraft/Uptigrave/Op den Graeff (1678 
1 CONT ?Krefeld, Germany - August 1743/8 Chester County, Pennsylvania), 
1 CONT married Mary, then Charity. In Chester County by 1732. Five known 
1 CONT children.
1 CONT 6c31 - Herman Updegraff (circa 1700 - 1758), married Mary Ann Louden 
1 CONT and Ann Ursula ?.
1 CONT 6c32 - Jack Updegraff (1701 - 1750).
1 CONT 6c33 - Derick or Dirck Updegraff (? - 1738), married Margaret ?
1 CONT 6c34 - Peter Updegraff, married Gertrude ?
1 CONT 6c35 - Abraham Updegrove (? - 1740), married Elizabeth Evans.
1 CONT 6c4 - Anne (Anneken) Op den Graeff (1690/1700 - ), married Herman 
1 CONT (Harmenken) IndeHofan (TenHeuvan or DeHaven).
1 CONT 6c5 - Gertien Op den Graeff (1683 - 1770), married Richard Addams.
1 CONT ?6c6 - Elizabeth Op den Graeff.
1 CONT 6d - Margrit Op den Graeff. To America in 1683?
1 CONT 6e - Adolphus Op den Graeff. Settled near Coblentz, Germany. A 
1 CONT grandson John William Graef/Op den Graeff emigrated to Germantown, 
1 CONT Pennsylvania, in 1753, later moving to Berks County, Pennsylvania.
1 CONT 6f - Vonder Op den Graeff. Settled near Coblentz after 1680.
1 CONT
1 CONT Judy Goldbaum, 30 June 1998, 10 August 1998, and 12 June 1999, posts 
1 CONT to GenForum Uptegraff Family Genealogy Forum. Edward Uptegrove (born 
1 CONT 1739 in Delaware or Pennsylvania) who married Sarah Lewis (born circa 
1 CONT 1740) possibly the son of Isaac Opdengraeff (born 1693 in Germantown, 
1 CONT Pennsylvania, moved to Mispillion Head, Kent County, Delaware) and 
1 CONT Rachel Linton (widow of Daniel Walker) who both died in Kent County, 
1 CONT Delaware, before 1747. Known children of Isaac and Rachel include 
1 CONT John (born 1732, married Sarah), Joseph, and William (born 1721, 
1 CONT married Sarah).
1 CONT Edward may have been removed from the family as he fought in the 
1 CONT Revolutionary War. Edward and Sarah had eleven children including 
1 CONT Isaac Uptegrove (circa 1762 in Pennsylvania).
1 CONT Genealogy:
1 CONT 1) Herman op den Graeff and Griejte Pletjes (from Krefeld, Germany, 
1 CONT to Germantown, Pennsylvania, on the Concord in 1683).
1 CONT 2) Isaac op den Graeff and Greietjen Porteis.
1 CONT 3) Herman Isaacs Updengraeff and Lisbet Isaacs Van Bebber.
1 CONT 4) Isaac Opdengraeff and Rachel Linton.
1 CONT
1 CONT Judy Goldbaum, 12 May 2000. Edward enlisted at the Chesterfield 
1 CONT County Courthouse in Virginia, for Revolutionary War service.
1 CONT
1 CONT Judy Goldbaum, 17 May 2000. Edward Uptegrove, 1739 - 1782. Married 
1 CONT 1760. Circumstantial evidence suggests parents were Isaac 
1 CONT Opdengraeff and Rachel Linton. Twelve children.
1 CONT
1 CONT Judy Goldbaum, 15 January 2001, post to Original-13-L@rootsweb.com. 
1 CONT Edward re-enlisted at the Chesterfield Court House, Virginia. He 
1 CONT died in 1782 in Virginia. Document is poor but appears to say he was 
1 CONT born in Barracks[, Pennsylvania?].
1 CONT
1 CONT June (Shaull) Lutz 1988, History of the Op den Graef/Updegraff 
1 CONT Family, p. U-399, citing Gladys Uptegrove of University City, 
1 CONT Missouri. Edward Uptegrove died in the Revolutionary War before 
1 CONT 1785.
1 CONT
