0 @N6000000000323084586@ NOTE Shenandoah , VA the original town was Millerstown
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: He moved with his parents to Greene County, Tennessee in 1804. He learned about hat making from his father. He moved to Monroe Co. Indiana in 1819 and ws one of the first pioneers of Nomroe County, Indiana. He became a minis
1 CONC ter of the Methodist Episcopal Chruch. In 1820 he married 1st to Jency Tyrant (Grant). They had eight children, all became Methodist ministers. Five years after Jency died, he married Mrs. Matida Williams-Butcher. She had eight ch
1 CONC ildren and she and Elias had nine children. Five of their children are listed in the Monroe Co. IN census in 1850. Some time after it was taken about 1852 Elias and his second family moved to McLennan Co. TX. There his last four c
1 CONC hildren were born. In 1869 they moved to Benton Co. AR. where he died on April 10-1870.
0 @N6000000000140962491@ NOTE
1 CONT He was President of the Phoenixville Bridge Company, and director of the National Bank of Phoenixville.
