1 CONT Quotes from Joseph WORDEN  “When Great Grandfather (Dr. Nathaniel WORDEN Jr.) moved into the town of Pawling New York ist was a wilderness  The nearest wagon road was two miles from where he started his home.  Now in 1890 there is
1 CONC  several wagon roads through the property and a railroad the entire length of the valley.”
1 CONT Dutchess county records, at Poughkeepsie----1867  will of Dr. Nathaniel WORDEN Jr. of Pawlington three farms, comprising of 320 acres, and a mill - names wife Sarah, daughters Deborah PERRY, Dernius SMITH, Sally or Sarah WINTERS, 
1 CONC LucyAVERY (wife of Abaham ) sons Marshall, Daniel or David, Deliverance, Silas, Isreal, Stephen and grandson William, son of Moses D?.
1 CONT The daughters of the American Revolution says they “Find no record of his right to be called doctor.  This seems to be all we have though, his service record in our DAR papers says he was “Physcian and surgeon aiding the injured a
1 CONC t the old Quacker Church on Quaker Hill which was used as a hospital during the Revolutionary War.
